Engineering design problems in China
Since the reform and open policy was established in 1978 , China has enjoyed a booming development in economy and technology .
A large amount of foreign capital as well as advanced foreign technologies have been introduced to China .
As a result , a lot of factories are built to provide the whole world with cheap and quality products .
However , the technological innovation for engineering design is still a weak point for Chinese manufactories .
Many Chinese enterprises do not have their own technology and the technological innovation is mainly dependent on the introduced foreign technology .
What exactly hampers the engineering design innovations in China ?
In my opinion , a serious plagiarism problem of Chinese institutes and the conservative consumption concept of Chinese people are two significant restrictions for the innovation of engineering design in China .
The plagiarism problem in both researching process and manufacturing process of engineering design is very serious in China .
In Chinese universities and other research organizations , plagiarism is rampant .
A Chinese study shows that " 60 percent of PhD candidates admitted to plagiarism , bribery " ( Marquand , 2006 ) .
University professors are also exposed to plagiarism .
For instance , Wang Mingming , a sociology professor in Peking University plagiarized 100.000 words from an American anthropologist 's work in the year 2002 ( Academic Circles , 2002 ) .
Plagiarism also exists in manufactories .
A notable number of Chinese factories make pirated products by copying foreign products .
For example , Meizu , a Chinese electrical manufactory famous for its pseudo " Apple inspired design " music players recently came up with a new product M8 .
This new product is actually another copycat of Apple iphone ( Ricker , 2007 ) .
Another example is the popular Chinese website " Xiaonei " .
It is exactly a fake " Facebook " .
Plagiarism can have strong negative effects on the innovation of engineering design .
By plagiarizing , engineers are not inclined to generate and analyze multiple solutions ( Khandani , 2005 ) .
They tend to copy other engineers ' work and become less creative , which in turn , significantly hampers the engineering design innovation of the whole nation .
The other important factor is the traditional conservative consumption concept of Chinese people .
Chinese culture used to appreciate consistency and changelessness .
In modern society , many Chinese people are still traditional and conservative in their consumption concepts .
They tend to reject engineering innovation and be slow in accepting new technological products .
Consequently , the conservative consumption concept can lead to low evaluation estimation of innovative products .
For the famous Russian Anti-Virus software , Kaspersky , many Chinese people would prefer to get a free registration key than pay certain amount of money .
Furthermore , the commercializing process of engineering design innovation can also be strongly affected by the conservative consumption concepts .
Take " Xianjian ( the Legend of Sword and Fairy ) " , a fantastic Chinese video game for example .
It is a very popular video game in china .
However , the game company lacks capital for research and development since most players are using cracked versions of Xianjian .
With few responses from local consumers , it is really tough for the innovation of engineering design in China .
The world is becoming more competitive .
Only creative countries with innovative engineers can lead the technology of the world .
Therefore , innovation in engineering design is of extreme importance .
China has to be aware of its problems in engineering design in order to be a leading nation in the 21st century .
By reducing the plagiarism rate of Chinese institutes and gradually changing the conservative consumption concept of Chinese people , China can really make a big difference .
