Facing the food shortage
Food shortage is much more serious now than it used to be .
According to an article published on the Internet , the impact of food crisis is historically spreading from the developing world to the developed world ( Kate Smith and Rob Edwards , 2009 ) .
It is the critical time to make some substantial changes to solve this essential challenge .
Appropriate facilities , efficient technological support and proper use of food are required to increase the food production in order to solve the food shortage problem .
First and foremost , the government should improve the facilities in the current agricultural system to satisfy the fundamental needs .
To be more accurate , in the developing countries , the government should make a good plan to build irrigation canals and banks based on the analysis of local climate and geography .
The government should provide stable surroundings for farmers to plant food .
Protecting plants from droughts and floods is necessary to have a good harvest .
Besides the infrastructure construction , another advisable method to increase production is to mechanize the agricultural system .
Armed with machinery , farmers can make the most of limited farmland and time .
In addition to the improvement of facilities in the current agricultural system , high-tech support also plays a crucial role in increasing food production .
It is effortless to come up with the idea that we can use biological engineering to change certain properties of plants .
Through this method , more food can be harvested in the same area of farmland .
The government should also make some regulations to urge experts to teach farmers how to farm scientifically .
For example , people grew a certain kind of plant in a county of China traditionally .
However , the plant is not an ideal plant for that environment .
After those farmers were told this , they changed the plant .
Then a better harvest is obtained .
Having made a good plan to help farmers to produce more food , the government must use the food properly .
Otherwise , no matter how much food can be harvested , many people will still suffer starvation .
From the same article which was mentioned in the first paragraph , a surprising fact emerges from the sophisticated Internet .
" Last year a quarter of the US maize crop was turned into ethanol to fuel vehicles - and the US supplies more than 60 % of the world 's maize exports .
" ( Kate Smith and Rob Edwards , 2009 ) .
It sounds very ridiculous that while 102.1 million people received food from UN WFP ( WFP in numbers , 2009 ) because they did not have enough food , an appreciable percentage of food was used to run cars .
It can never be called progress but ignorance .
It is an inhumane action to turn food into ethanol to feed cars instead of helping those starving people .
The government should not abuse food .
In conclusion , there are three advisable ways to solve the food shortage .
Infrastructure is the foundation of agriculture .
Upgrading the infrastructure is necessary for food production to increase .
Apart from infrastructure , high-tech can also do a big favor in this issue .
Last but not least , proper use of food must be highlighted .
Through these methods , a better situation will come soon .
