Over the years , we have seen many new technological innovations and inventions .
Some are deemed beneficial to mankind , while others are just created for the sake of businessmen to reap in business profits .
However , this technological innovation which I am describing has brought about a large change in human life .
It has also brought about much convenience and is now considered an asset to most people .
The technological innovation which I am referring to is the introduction of 3G mobile phones .
In the early 1990s,mobile phones were first introduced to replace pagers .
Back then , mobile phones could only serve 1 basic function , and that was just to make basic phone calls .
There was no other functions in a mobile phone .
Apart from being a device with minimal functions , the design and shape of the mobile phone back then was also very ugly .
It was because at that time , the technology was not advanced enough for manufacturers to come up with cool and sleek designs like the mobile phones nowadays .
It was also very costly to own one .
Hence , not many people were able to afford a mobile phone in the past .
However , take a look at today 's society .
Mobile phones are a necessity .
Almost everyone owns a mobile phone , including a certain percentage of primary school students .
The phones which people nowadays possess also differs from the past , in terms of functions , designs and sizes .
All these transformation have been brought about due to several factors .
Firstly , the manufacturers of the modern day mobile phones recognized and acknowledged the problem of phones in the past .
As quoted by incorrect in-text citation : " The innovation-development process often begins with recognition of a problem or need .
"
Manufacturers of mobile phones found out the disadvantages and hassles of the mobile phones in the past .
As stated earlier , mobile phones back then had no other functions except for making phone calls .
Hence , if people back then required the services of surfing the internet or sending plural , they had to rely on other device such as the computer to do it .
Unlike the 3G mobile phones which is able to perform all these functions within it , mobile phones back then were really considered unproductive and inefficient .
Time is money .
Every second wasted is equivalent to every cent lost .
Hence , in order to work in a more productive manner which saves time and bring about convenience for users , manufacturers today have come up with 3G phones which are equipped with internet , video-capturing device and an in-bulit music player which aims to provide entertainment to the users .
Secondly , this technological innovation was brought about by technical improvements in technology .
Over the years , we can see that technology is improving and more people are able to take advantage of it .
Hence , phone manufacturers decided to take a risk by adding a few new features into the mobile phone to see whether it is acceptable in the market .
A typical example is the production of NOKIA 8310 in 2002 .
This phone was the first phone in the industry to be equipped with radio function , apart from the basic functions of a phone .
After this production , many other rival brands followed suit .
This thus proves that the society is open and adaptable to new features in the phone .
This was further echoed by the good sales results of this model .
Hence , this sent a signal to phone manufacturersthatthe public is more than willing to accept a phone with more functions and will not even mind to replace their previous models for newer ones with added features or functions .
As a result , it gave manufacturers an incentive to keep up with the times and to constantly upgrade their mobile phones .
This is why we are able to see the presence/existence of the 3G mobile phones .
Economic factors also play an important role in this technological innovation .
Over the years , the production of parts for mobile phones has become cheaper .
This could be achieved as manufacturers are able to reap economics of scale as their production size increases .
Hence , as the cost is now lower , manufacturers are more willing to produce and come up with more features to be added to the mobile phone to attract consumers to purchase it .
This is exactly the case for the production of 3G phones .
People find the 3G phone to be a useful device as it is able to perform many functions , which inevitably saves time and brings about a lot of convenience .
As it has so many functions , it will definitely attract consumers to purchase it .
Since the demand for it is so high , manufacturers will then find it profitable to increase the supply .
This thus leads to the vast production of 3G phones , bringing technology to the next level .
In conclusion , the transformation of mobile phones from a black-grey screen to one that is so highly sophiscated is indeed remarkable .
This technological innovation can not be achieved without the factors listed above .
I believe in the near future to come , we are able to expect more innovations and creativity in the production of mobile phones .
factors such as economic conditions , political decisions , technological , advertising and even military demands can affect the development of technological innovation .
One very important technology that has been shaped by the society is the development of electric vehicle .
One of the factors that determines and shapes technological innovation the most is the country 's economic status .
When people are richer , they will want to own something such as a car to show their social status .
Electric car in the past was very expensive and only very wealthy people could afford it .
It was a display of social standing when one is seen in an electric car .
Therefore it was more common to see people in cars in rich countries than poor countries .
Political factors such as government decisions and military demands could also shape technological innovation .
Before World War one , the use of automobiles were limited as there were very few roads .
During the war , there was mass construction of roads leading to suburbanization of the world making it more ideal to own an automobile .
However there was shortage of coal during the war thus making electric vehicle impractical to operate .
Therefore gasoline vehicles became more popular as governments subsidized the building of gasoline vehicles to support their war .
After the war , gasoline vehicles became the preferred choice as it is more Development of technologies can be easily shaped and influenced by the group of users and the society .
commonly seen on the roads due to mass production during war .
Gasoline vehicles also seemed more durable and electric plural were considered unsuitable .
After people attained a certain level of standard of living they became more concerned with the environment .
They began to worry about the problem of pollution caused by gasoline plural .
Therefore governments stepped in to ensure that for the total sales of plural followed by , 10 percent must be nonpolluting , which meant that it has to be electric car or electric/gasoline cars .
Therefore people who were more environmentally friendly began to use electric vehicles again .
The technological advancement of a country also affects the development of the electric vehicle .
A very important component of the electric vehicle is the battery .
A very powerful battery is needed to power and run the vehicle for a long time and it is only possible with advanced battery technology .
It is only natural that nobody would want an electric car that needs recharging for every few miles it travels .
According to EM Roger ( 2003 ) , in the early 1990s , the battery technology can only support the vehicle to travel for 100miles .
For every 100 miles of travelling the vehicle requires 4 hours of recharging to a 220-volt outlet .
Before , the use of electric vehicle was very limited as the battery technology was not available or was .
There are many factors that may shape the technological innovation of the technology .
The factors may leave a positive or negative impact on the technological innovation depending on the market and how socially acceptable the technology is at that point of time .
Once such example of a technology that has been shaped by it users would be the electric vehicle .
Therefore the society also plays an important role in technological innovation .
People nowadays do not only think of creating tools that can ease their life .
They also need to choose the most efficient technology that can meet their needs .
Furthermore , the processes to create and choose the suitable technology is called engineering design .
engineering design recently has been implemented in many of Asia-Pacific countries , including Indonesia .
