The design process of cooling apparatuses
As Khandani ( 2005 ) points out , innovations are designed to meet human needs .
Human needs and problems are the motivation for conceiving new ideas and designing new products .
In Singapore , and other countries next to the equator , air conditioners and electric fans have greatly contributed to people 's lives and people are able to enjoy cool and refreshing air on burning hot days .
Throughout human history , people have conceived of many ways to get rid of heat in hot weather .
The design process of electric fans and air conditioners is a process in which engineers make designs to meet people 's needs .
From the very primary fan to the electric fan , and all the way to the air conditioner , engineering designs gradually solve the problem and meet people 's needs .
In ancient times heat and humidity tortured people a lot .
In hot days , people felt physically uncomfortable and mentally irritable .
The working efficacy was low and diseases transmitted easily .
People began to think of ways to solve the problem .
Some great minds , probably the engineers in those days , created fans .
Fans were generally made from leather or palm leaves sewed together .
The fan basically combined the theory of flowing air and wind , but it was a great success and everybody uses fans to generate breeze and keep cool in summer .
It relieves discomfort in summer .
Gradually , people were not satisfied by fans , since they had to keep shaking fans to keep cool .
It was disturbing to shake a fan at work or during sleep .
At the same time , electricity was invented and people began to appreciate the convenience brought by it .
In 1886 , Schulyer Wheeler ( Inventors , 2009 ) devised a new type of machine using electricity to send breeze .
After careful design and a hard process of trial and error , the first electric fan was created .
The advent of the electric fan was a great success and it was implemented around the world .
People 's needs were met by the air vortex flow which automatically .
The electric fan was the standard at that time .
As time went by , the electric fan seemed to be unsatisfactory .
It can not really cool the temperature and does not control humidity .
As more and more individuals and companies started to work on more effective cooling machines , Willis H. Carrier , a mechanical engineer made a breakthrough in 1902 .
( Bookrags , 2005 ) The air conditioner was first invented by him to improve the performance of a printing plant .
It proved to be effective in manipulating the heat and lowering humidity .
The air conditioner was so effective that despite its relatively high price , it was integrated into people 's lives and installed everywhere .
Now electric fans and air conditioners are better designed than the original ones .
People feel more comfortable on hot days .
Productivity is increased and industries flourish .
The design was initiated by people 's needs , and it ultimately met people 's needs .
It is believed that the design will not end there so that more advanced products will appear .
More developed and enhanced functions will be added to improve people 's lives better and better .
