Since the attack on the London Underground on July 2005 , surveillance technology has generated a lot of attention after it was used to track the movements of the terrorists responsible for the attack .
Reports and articles have shown that the use of surveillance technology to track people can be beneficial to us , particularly in the healthcare and crime prevention sectors and in the enhancement of security .
Therefore , I fully agree that surveillance technology should not be banned .
Firstly , surveillance technology such as radio identification technology ( RFID ) can be used to track patients in the hospital where it will notify the nurse or hospital staffs if a patient begins to collapse .
( { http : //news.cnet.com/Human-chips-more-than-skin-deep/2009-1008_3-5318076.html } [ HYPERLINK : http : //news.cnet.com/Human-chips-more-than-skin-deep/2009-1008_3-5318076.html ] ) This way , the chances of reviving and saving a patient is greater .
If a patient suddenly collapses in her room and there is no one to alert the nurse , it will probably take one or more hours for her to be saved when the nurse goes around to check on the patients .
By that time , the patient 's life would be in danger and this would most probably bring about dire consequences such as death .
Not only that , RFID strap can also be used to monitor patients with Alzheimer 's disease .
( { http : //news.cnet.com/Human-chips-more-than-skin-deep/2009-1008_3-5318076.html } [ HYPERLINK : http : //news.cnet.com/Human-chips-more-than-skin-deep/2009-1008_3-5318076.html ] )
Secondly , the implementation of radio identification technology in prison can also help to track prisoners and reduce violence in the prisons .
( { http : //www.rfidjournal.com/article/view/1601/1/1 } [ HYPERLINK : http : //www.rfidjournal.com/article/view/1601/1/1 ] ) .
Prison officers will be able to monitor the movement and exact locations of the inmates and thus this will deter them from committing crimes in the prison .
Not only that , if indeed a crime happens , the prison guards will be able to investigate and know who the culprit is .
Furthermore , it can also ensure that the inmates do not escape by sending alerts when an inmate approaches the jail perimeter .
Thirdly , surveillance technology can also be used to keep track of our children and prevent kidnapping .
( HYPERLINK " http : //technu.nst.com.my/Current_News/techNu/Monday/Notebook/20080211123356/Article/index_html " http : //technu.nst.com.my/Current_News/techNu/Monday/Notebook/20080211123356/Article/index_html ) .
Parents can strap radio identification technology on the wrist of their children in order to monitor the location of their children .
For example , when the child is missing or kidnapped , the parents will be able to know the exact location of their kids .
This can also help the police in their investigative work .
In conclusion , surveillance technology should not be banned to track people as it can not only save life but also improve the healthcare sector while enhancing the security of our society .
