The Individual Requesting Genetic Testing Should Not Have the Final Say in Whether to Reveal the Results
Genetic testing is the analysis of genes , chromosomes , RNA and proteins .
It is used to predict the risk of disease , identify carriers of disease , diagnose disease ( Genetic Testing , 2006 , para 1 ) , and can also be used to determine parents of the child .
Genetic testing includes scientific methods in biology , chemistry , and sometimes even biochemical tests .
Nowadays , as the technology develops , individuals have more approaches to such tests .
However , such people requesting genetic tests should not have the final say in whether to reveal the results of the tests .
Firstly , if someone discovers that he or she has a particular mutation , the existence of that knowledge has immediate implications for the person 's blood relatives ( Skene , 2003 ) .
When they are informed of the potential risk of the mutation that could lead to a genetic disease that is also hereditary , they can undergo their own genetic tests in order to determine the extent of the mutation risk as soon as possible .
If they are positive , they can undertake a further diagnostic procedure to determine whether any physical symptom will developg .
If necessary , they can receive the proper medical treatment in time , for instance , prophylactic surgery .
When the first genetic tester does not want to reveal the results , blood relatives will not be alerted to the existence of the risk , and then it will be too late for them to get effective intervention .

Secondly , when the result of a particular genetic test is beneficial to the whole society , researchers have the right to disclose the outcome outcome .
As we know , scientists all over the world are working together to make people 's lives better by studying the genome of human and other organisms .
In doing such a significant project , they need numerous different genes to work on .
Sometimes discovering an insignificant phenomenon or test results and anglicizing it can really make a breakthrough .
Hence , when an individual requesting genetic testing comes up with an interesting exploration , it may change the perspective in looking into the subject , for instance , treating cancer , AIDS or some hereditary diseases .
As a result , these individuals should not have the final say in hiding their results .
On the contrary , the results should be shared among scientists and researchers for the whole world 's sake .
In conclusion , individuals who request genetic testing should not have the final say in revealing the results for two major reasons : protecting their blood relatives from genetic disorders and helping the whole society for genetic researchs .
