" The use of surveillance technology such as RFID to track people should be banned .
"
In this 21st century , modern technology has advanced to a stage where radio frequency identification ( RFID ) is implanted into people to locate and identify them .
RFID is a chip that has a small antenna to transmit a vast amount of information from a human 's body to a computer using a scanner ( Sade , 2007 , p. 1 ) .
RFID enhances productivity in the healthcare system , helps to monitor ex-offenders and also helps to locate missing personnel .
Thus , due to the benefits brought about by RFID , it should not be banned .
Firstly , the use of RFID to identify patients enhances productivity in the healthcare system ( Sade , 2007 , p.2 ) .
The use of RFID can minimize the long registration time for patients so that they are able to seek treatment in the shortest possible time .
When a patient goes to the hospital , his medical records which are already stored in a RFID tag can be immediately traced using the RFID scanner .
In doing so , waiting time could be greatly minimized and many more innocent lives will be saved .
Hence , the use of RFID is greatly beneficial in the medical field .
Secondly , implanting RFID tags into ex-offenders aids the authorities in monitoring their activities .
Police will be alerted in the shortest possible time when these ex-offenders are in a position that may harm victims ( Rfid based proximity sensor and alert system for fugitives , sex offenders , missing soldiers and the like description/claims , 2008 ) .
This helps to save innocent lives and reduce crime in the country .
It also allows ex-offenders to have their freedom and at the same time , the police will be alerted when they commit a crime .
This gives the public a sense of security and hence , the use of RFID to monitor ex-offenders is beneficial to the society .
Thirdly , RFID can also help to locate missing personnel .
People who are embedded with the tag would be scanned and their location can easily be found .
This is especially useful for the elderly who suffer from dementia .
When they are not able to find their way home , their family members can make use of RFID technology to track them down .
Hence , the use of RFID greatly speeds up the tedious process of finding missing personnel and at the same time , minimizes wastage of resources .
In conclusion , with these benefits that RFID have brought to people , it is undeniable that using RFID to track people will only improve the current situation and hence , it should not be banned .
References
Sade , R. M. ( n.d. ) .
Radio Frequency ID Devices in Humans .
Report of the Council on Ethical and Judicial Affairs , CEJA Report 5-A-07 , 1-5 .
