Technological advances have brought along pros and cons ever since it entered our daily lives .
One of the many technologies innovated is the surveillance technology , mainly RFID ( Radio-Frequency Identification ) .
'Tracking ' , in this context , is defined as both monitoring and identifying the location , behavior , activities and changing information such as medical information .
Admittedly , personal privacy will be intruded .
Nevertheless , it has the ability to track criminals , improve the efficiency of our healthcare system , as well as to expedite the cracking of criminal cases .
Therefore , owing to the significant advantages of RFID , it should not be banned .
Tracking activities plays a crucial role in identifying terrorists and monitoring ex-criminals .
By implanting the RFID tags in both groups , their location will remain known to the police force and relevant authorities , thus allowing consistent monitoring of activities .
It has always been a common objective between countries to wipe out terrorism ( Rhea Wessel , 2006 ) so that world peace could be maintained .
Furthermore monitoring ex- criminals will not only forbid them from committing crimes again , but more importantly , allow the public to have a peace of mind employing them , subsequently making them feel accepted by the society .
Therefore , given the advantages of surveillance technology , it should not be banned .
Surveillance technology such as RFID can improve two components of our healthcare system .
Firstly , it cuts down on the waiting time to be attended to .
A scan on the tags allows healthcare personnel to instantly identify the medical information of patients .
Secondly , time saved on retrieving essential information of patients during an emergency could be put into treating the patients ( http : //www.verichipcorp.com ) .
Crucial moments could determine life and death .
Therefore , the RFID technology can improve our healthcare system 's efficiency .
Expediting the cracking of criminal cases is another point why surveillance technology should not be banned .
Tracking locations could never be more important in cases such as kidnapping ( http : //www.verichipcorp.com ) .
Crimes like this should be attended to in the shortest possible time as it may result in injuries or even death of victims .
Furthermore , it could lower the crime rate , thus benefiting all people .
Hence , surveillance technology can assist in cracking criminal cases .
In all , surveillance technology benefits us greatly in several aspects and thus should not be banned .
