Synthesis : Surveillance technology such as RFID should not be banned
The usage of surveillance technology such as RFID ( Radio-Frequency Identification ) on people or products has been a hot topic debated by both supporters and critics .
RFID tags has been introduced to the general public , but remains theoretical until the 11th September,2001 attack .
The idea came when a technology executive discovered that RFID tags may be used for identification if a body becomes disfigured or unrecognizable in an accident .
Thus , the RFID technology started to materialize and propagate in public which caused commotions pertaining to privacy and ethical issues raised from the use of such technology .
Albeit the risk of privacy invasion , RFID tags are potential devices which do benefit humans if executed under strict regulations .
First and foremost , with the RFID surveillance technology , personal safety in public places can be enhanced .
By having RFID attached to a person , especially children , their whereabouts can be constantly watched by their parents and increases the safeguarding of their children .
However , there are issues concerning the dependence of technology instead of parents giving full attention towards their children by their own effort , and thus decreasing their sense of responsibility as a caretaker .
But with RFID tags , their children can remain safe and sound by lowering the cases of injury or loss of devices which can be detected straightaway if such situations happen .
Therefore , RFID tags are efficacious devices in monitoring the situation of children .
Surveillance technology such as RFID also plays a pivotal role in health field .
Currently , a number of hospitals have begun to implement the attachment of RFID tags on patients in order to monitor and observe the patients from time to time .
It was also stated by Information Week ( 2005 ) , that RFID tags can be used to prevent newborn infants from being abducted by outsiders .
The tagging system is also a measure to deter the problems of having Alzheimer patients lost wandering in other places or patients collapsing outside of hospital area .
Signals will be transmitted to the hospital to alert the nurses of their condition .
Hence , with such surveillance technology , the risk of patients getting injured while getting lost outside can be reduced to a minimum .
All in all , it can not be denied that surveillance technology is important in securing a safe environment .
The impact of surveillance technology towards human lives is huge and can be frightening at times .
Moreover , the public has generated concern over the right of keeping their personal information in private .
Even though there are doubts and concerns towards the usage of surveillance technology for tracking purposes , it is still a central piece of the puzzle of human lives .
In a nutshell , surveillance technology such as RFID tags used to track people should not be banned .
