Public spending is defined as the amount of funding the government channels into the society from the monies it collects from the society .
This fund is generated through various economic activities , usually in the form of taxation .
The debate often revolves round how the government utilizes this fund , which is contributed by the citizens .
The total amount collected from an economy tends to be more or less fixed in the short term .
Therefore , if one group of people gets more , the others would get lesser .
Thus , by limiting the spending on the aged , it would mean that other sectors of the society would get more than before .
This essay will discuss the limit that should be imposed on the amount of funds that should be budgeted for the aged that would constitute a fair distribution of government resources .
This is due to the fact that the aged is not the only dependent group in society .
If there is a tendency to spend more than necessary on the aged , other sectors of the economy might find that they lack finances to function adequately .
Some might say that it is immoral to deprive the aged of the help they need .
They tend to support this argument by considering the contributions made by the aged during their hey-days and the level of their dependency in this season of their lives .
However , this school of thought focuses on only one aspect of the issues of society .
There is no doubt that some of the aged need help .
However , they are not the only dependent group .
A country is likely to also include the poor , the uneducated , the physically disabled , the intellectually underdeveloped , and many others who require constant monetary aid from the government .
Thus , it can almost be called an ill-informed decision when one claims that the government should take care of the aged without limits .
There is no doubt that we should ensure that the aged can age with dignity .
However , not only the aged , but who are dependent on the government 's help should also have the right to live with dignity .
Thus , while the government educates the aged about their rights and campaigns about health maintenance methods , the other sectors of society in need of help should not be left out .
Therefore , public spending on the aged should be limited so that other citizens of the country who are in need can also receive aid .
A second argument is that financial support for the aged is essential to maintain a certain level of standard of living for the aged .
It may be true that without help from the government , some senior citizens would struggle just to survive .
However , if the state takes care of the aged unconditionally , it would be a policy impossible to maintain in the long run .
Unrestrained expenditure on the aged can be likened to an endless pit .
Without clear guidelines , the elderly could easily abuse the system .
This is especially true when the cost of visiting subsidized public hospitals falls below that of visiting general practitioners , where the costs are borne solely by the patients .
Not having a limitation based on the results of means testing would lead to a large number of people applying for grants even when they are not in dire need of such concessions .
In Singapore , the government puts in place many rules and regulations for citizens to gain access to public aid like the Public Assistance Scheme .
This is to make sure that those who eventually get the money are those who genuinely need financial assistance , not simply because they fall into the right age category
( Stolberg and Zeleny , 2009 ) President Obama aims to modify America 's health care policy to one that 'provides security and stability to those who have insurance and cover those who do not , all without adding to the federal deficit' .
The New York Times ( 2009 ) states that the health care system in the United States of America ( USA ) today is 'full of waste and abuse' .
This is due to the fact that the USA is a welfare state and provides pension for the retired .
This financial scheme has resulted in the USA being the country spending most on health care , leading to a great strain on the government budget ( The New York Times , 2009 , 14 September ) .
In light of this , we can be sure that this excessive amount of money is not well-spent .
Therefore , public spending on the aged should be limited to prevent misuse of funds that could be better channeled back to the economy , where more government revenue would most likely be generated .
There are also others who argue that the aged should be entitled to unlimited funds as it is difficult to ensure that all the basic needs of the aged are met .
They would rather provide more so that all the aged are taken care of , rather than risk any one of them suffering due to insufficient aid .
However , this would likely benefit only a portion of the society and deprive the other sectors of the funds needed .
In the society today , there are certain industries , known as public goods , which require government involvement to exist .
For example , if the government does not invest in training an army of their own , no citizen will pay from their own pocket for it .
Such facilities benefit everyone in the country and it is difficult to exclude anyone from enjoying them .
Thus , everyone tends to wait for their neighbours to provide for them .
The wide spread of such a mentality would then result in the government having to provide these services .
Therefore , if public spending on the aged is not limited , there will be less funds channeled to projects such as the building of roads , the provision of street lights , the maintenance of the police force and cleaning of the streets .
With a restricted budget for these sectors , we may have to live with a lower quality of life and a less secured nation , which would also lower the living standards amongst the aged .
Thus , it is necessary to specify limits to public spending on the aged , so that sufficient funds can be channeled to provide other facilities for the nation as a whole .
In conclusion , caring for the elderly is only right and necessary .
However , it should be within limits so that other parts of society would not be deprived of the help that is necessary for current support and future development .
Everyone is dependent on government aid to varying degrees .
A good balance must be struck to ensure that as few people as possible are deprived of government support due to poor distribution of state monies .
