Living in the 21st century , consumption by any human being in terms of assets , properties and food have had a steady relation to both the research and development ( R&D ) segment , and current policies , which are necessary for an individual .
R&D and current policies allow people to depend on them ; to aid and benefit one 's lifestyle , especially for the elderly .
Beattie states that there are already policies in place for people to support themselves in their old age , such as the pension systems , provident funds , social insurance and saving schemes .
Employees dependent on pensions or provident funds even suggest a change in the benefits that they are obtaining .
Due to unpredictable economic growths , policy purchasers yearn for better benefits which are able to sustain till the end of the contract on these policies .
Those in desire need of elderly welfare are assisted by the social welfare personnel .
This is evident in the context of Asia ; many elderly treat these polices like their livelihood .
According to Ghilarducci and the Employee Benefits Research Institute , people are stressed by the changing economic growth and anxious as they are signed onto the retirement accounts .
It proves these policies are present for people to purchase and make use of to aid them in their again process .
In Singapore , the Central Provident Fund Board ( CPF Board ) is a saving scheme that covers working Singaporeans with a list of welfare benefits and offers a sense of security for their old age .
Also , the CPF Board reminds Singaporeans to save and stretch every dollar whenever possible so as to have comfortable lives after retirement in the future .
From the highlights of Channel NewsAsia [ 2009 ] , there are many countries with a looming demographic .
Some of these countries include Japan and Singapore , with the rate of the elderly population increasing rapidly and surpassing the younger population in the near future .
In view of this demographic , countries like Japan and Singapore have been establishing ways to curb the aging population .
In Japan , the government has a policy of offering incentives to families with small children so as to increase birth rates and build up a new family .
In Singapore , there is the reemployment legislation in 2012 where employers are advised to retain the elderly as the demand for their skills are needed .
In the meantime , Singaporeans are told to save early with the easy access of financial schemes and saving programs offered .
In addition , the technological invention segment has played a part in easing the aging process .
As Schoeni , Freedman and Martin suggests , the R&D segment has been expanding rapidly .
With the the advancement of medical technologies , illnesses such as cardiovascular and cataract diseases have lesser occurrence .
Medical technologies are still advancing and treatments are being catered to a wide array of medical fields .
Some of which include the knee and joint replacements , treatments for arthritis and rheumatism , and vision impairment , diabetic and stem cell research .
However , the presence of R&D does come with a hefty price tag .
Medical expenses are costly and patients , especially , the elderly need to seek for welfare assistance when necessary .
Sadly , for the elderly who do not seek medical attention , they either suffer bitterly or are possibly cared for by organizations like Peace Connect Neighborhood Link in Singapore .
Countries like the United States and Singapore are insured with Medicare and Medishield respectively .
We are insured despite the high medical expenses of new inventions in the medical fields .
It gives a well-balance medical segment , an advance health security cycle as we reach our retirement age despite the cost .
Moreover , with the growing number of well-educated people around , there is a high probability that people will purchase private insurance to care for their own well-being .
Manpower is essential in every organization .
From Malul findings , the elderly are counted as part of the workforce if considered age appropriate . However , with technology so advanced these days , the elderly in the workface may be faced with hiccups as they are not well skilled in certain aspects of the technology .
This is when the training and re-training of employees is crucial .
Furthermore , organizations offering subsidies to the elderly workforce helps to minimize unemployment rates and high turnovers .
At the same time , this allows the elderly to stay active for a longer period of time in the workforce .
specified that previously the retirement age was 70 in a certain country ; however , it changed to 65 years old .
Majority of these elderly are baby boomers who yearned to extend their duration in the workforce .
By lowering the retirement age , an organization could seek for cheaper employment in a less developed country . However , it may face a high turnover rate as the younger generations do not stay long in jobs , unlike the elderly .
Therefore , to have a mixture of young and old workers , a firm could have a cap on the benefits of an older worker so as to retain the elderly and decrease cost , while training the younger generation of workers in advanced skills that are necessary for an organization to excel . This will enable the organization to be more efficient. .
As to reinstate , the policies that each country provides and the current R&D have assisted and benefited the aging process in today 's society .
With the economy fluctuating , having on-going medical research and technology inventions , and people becoming more educated , there is definitely room for restructuring and improving the policies and R&D segment in the future .
