The world population is expected to increase from 200million to 2 billion between 1950 to2050 , especially for people aged 60 and above ( Somavia,2002 ) .
It is becoming an increasingly important issue for governments all over the world .
Measures have been implemented to slowdown the process of a matured society ( Peterson , n.d. ) and at the same time cope with the problem brought about by an ageing population ( Dobriansky,2007 ) .
In the following paragraphs , issues on whether the government should redirect public funds to other more important matters concerning the country , or focus on improving the health of the aged by growing the resources especially for them .
The concerns that will be discussed if funds should be put into funding education and its facilities , and the growth of the country itself is more paramount with regards to the country 's development .
Education is deemed one of the most vital matters concerning the public and it is of remarkable worth to the economy ( Dobriansky,2007 ) .
When majority of the funds are diverted into improving education facilities , the aged will not be able to save up enough money whilst actively working .
The reason for this is because bringing up children these days is expensive , which will result in a burden for parents .
So income earned by parents will be drained through educating children , and parents will have nothing to rely on when they age .
The government should implement schemes and insurance for parents to rely on instead of spending most funds on education facilities .
However , as stated by Afonso ( 2008 ) , he implied that when there is high social spending together with good education , it will result in optimistic income distribution .
Afonso 's view supports my stand that public funds being diverting into the education system is fundamental .
In this case , governments can help parents to save whilst bringing up their children , this provides sufficient support due to aid by government for educating children .
With support provided by the government to educate children , parents can save a substantial amount while allowing their children to receive education .
Public education in Singapore is almost entirely financed by the government except for preschool education .
Singapore has a compulsory scheme for Singaporeans to save money for health-related issues through Medisave ( StateUniversity.com , n.d. ) .
Medisave is a contribution by every employee of about 6.5-9 % of his monthly salary to his personal account .
Funds can be used to settle hospital bills of the individual or his immediate family members , reducing the problem of having not enough monetary resources ( Ministry of Manpower,2007 ) .
Economic Growth is another issue that should not be neglected when a country is concerned about her development .
There should not be a diversion of public funds because economic growth is dependent on consumption , investments , and government expenditure ( Alemohammad,2009 ) .
Economic growth can be brought about through consumption and investments , not necessarily government incentives .
This means that public funds should be given to providing for the aged as economic growth can be dependent on other factors .
Conversely , as stated by Mackenzie ( 2009 ) , Canadians benefit amounts to $ 17,000 from the public services from tax funds , about the same amount a Canadian working full-time would earn .
Since extensive monetary benefits are given out to Canadians , it should not be a problem for them to cope with ageing as they can save while benefitting from government incentives .
In addition , economic growth can come about through diverting funds into more valuable areas like education .
Education worth directly affects individual earnings ( Hanushek,2007 ) .
Skills obtained allow for higher productivity in the workforce .
Young adults will be able to secure a well-paid job in the future ; it will lead to higher consumption and investments ( Saltz,2007 ) .
Thus this leads to elevated economic growth and higher standard of living , and children will be able to look after their parents .
This means that through investing in children 's higher education , the country is able to compensate for the decrease in public spending on the aged .
Hence , public funds should not be allocated solely to helping the aged .
Therefore , there will never be a situation where funds should be restricted to just one area .
Spending of public funds should be diverted to various areas of the country depending on its country focus .
Hence , government should consider what is more important for the country 's development and direct the funds into that direction .
