Aging population
An aging population becomes an ubiquitous trend in many developed countries such as Japan .
The government confronts a series of financial and social problems .
The biggest challenge is to reduce the fiscal and economic cost of elder dependency .
Many policies have been proposed by scholars .
The idea that reserving a retirement fund in advance can help ease the aging process is regarded as an efficient and feasible method for the government ( Peterson , 2001 ) .
However , some still think that the younger generation and the government are responsible for dealing with the problem of an aging population .
If elderly people failed to accumulate enough funds before retirement , they have to rely a lot on their children .
However , the younger generation have heavy financial burdens to take care of their own families and sometimes are unable to support their parents .
For example , in a Singaporean middle class family , a young couple usually have two to four children and lives in a governmental or private house with mortgage .
They have to work hard to provide the basic necessities of life , such as food , clothes , education etc .
In this harsh situation , the elderly parents who have no income and no savings become a big financial strain .
When the health conditions of the elderly people become bad , the financial burden on the young becomes overwhelming .
In some cases , an expensive medical bill can even lead a prosperous family to bankruptcy .
When the young are exposed to both financial and emotional stresses , they can not concentrate on their work .
Finally , it negatively affects the society by decreasing productivity and economic growth .
Some people think that the government has an obligation to help the elderly by providing financial aid .
It seems that the young can shift the liability and solve the financial problem , but these excessive government subsidies will result in draining the public funds quickly .
The government has to increase taxes in order to fill vacancies .
Consequently , the tax payers , mainly the younger generation who are productive , will pay even more taxes .
In many European countries , the unemployed people receive unemployment benefits from the government .
On the other hand , the jobholders have to pay more taxes .
High welfare always comes with high taxes .
Relying merely on governmental subsidies does not solve the problem .
On the contrary , the government should compel people to save a certain portion of their income into special retirement accounts before they reach retirement age and allow the owners to withdraw the money when they retire .
The government could also give subsidies to encourage the public to do so , for instance , offering a reasonably high interest rate .
The Singapore government has been doing well in this respect .
All Singaporeans must save 5 percent of their total income while their employers contribute an additional 20 percent into a government retirement account .
The government provides a 4 percent annual interest rate which is relatively higher than many commercial banks .
There are two reasons for the Singaporean government to do so .
One is to give confidence to the public ; the other one is to help them to mitigate the effects of inflation .
Most Singaporean are expected to accumulate sufficient amount for retirement with the help of this system .
An aging population is a social problem as well as an individual problem .
The government has a responsibility to help and guide the public to plan their retirement life .
Furthermore , the public must take care of themselves .
Providing a retirement fund in advance is a long term project and this can only be achieved by raising public consciousness .
Public spending , in terms of taxes , refers to the sum of money charged by the government for specific facilities or services , levied upon incomes , property , sales , and more .
Some of the taxes include Income Tax , Property Tax , as well as Goods and Services Tax ( GST ) .
This strategy suggested is feasible to a large extent .
Public spending should be limited to a certain degree so that the budget would be diverted to different areas such as education , research and development , tourism and the transportation system of the country .
The most basic yet important area of the country 's development would be education .
In most countries , education is considered to be one of the fundamental sectors that the country 's government can develop and improve on .
It is the base system of the country that imparts knowledge to the people and keeps a majority of them employed .
For that reason , the process of education is considered to be essential for the development of our society such that every child has to go through a minimum of ten years of basic education .
It has also become such an indispensable part of our lives that to the majority of people , it appears to be a norm to complete the whole process of the education .
It is crucial that the country has a good education system for future economic development .
The Research and Development ( R&D ) sector allows the development of the country .
According to the Yearbook of Statistics Singapore , there has been an increase in demand for R&D by many companies .
As changes occur every day , modernization occurs , new technologies are introduced and people try to catch up with the rapid advancement .
In many cases , research and development is important to the countries ' businesses and industries to boost knowledge and skills .
For favorable progress , it is important for the business sector , universities , colleges and research institutes to collaborate in order to stimulate innovation , growth and modernization .
More needs to be done in order to draw us nearer to the fast changing know- how of the society .
The tourism industry attracts foreigners to spend , thus giving rise to an inflow of cash into the country .
To many countries , tourism is their only source of income and is therefore vital for them to develop in this area .
For example , Maldives and Seychelles only earn the opportunity for employment in the tourism service industries .
It includes hospitality services , such as hotels and resorts , transportation services , such as airlines , cruise ships and taxis , as well as entertainment venues , such as shopping malls , amusement parks and casinos .
Thus , government initiatives for the tourism industry are important , to enhance growth throughout the country by promoting the development of the industry and also to increase employment opportunities by creating more jobs available for them .
However , on the other hand , there should be limited , but adequate percentage of public spending allocated to the aged .
The reason being , many elderly are being neglected by their own children , and thus uninsured .
They might not have enough money to get their regular medical checkups done .
So , does this means that they will die ?
This problem will continue to get worse every year if there is inadequate attention paid .
Though it is important to solve the problem of the graying society , we should limit our public spending in this sector so that we can budget for other aspects of a country 's development , such as the transportation infrastructure .
A significant level of road traffic can be created due to the high density of an urban environment .
This can have a great impact on businesses and environmental factors .
Therefore , careful planning and development of the transportation system are crucial .
More money should be used to develop this infrastructure in order to support the moving of goods from one place to another efficiently and effectively .
Parking space is another concern .
For example , in Singapore where land scarcity poses a big issue , multi-storey carparks are built to allow more vehicles to be parked given the same land area used .
In conclusion , public spending on the aged should be limited to a certain percentage that is adequate for the welfare of the aged .
On top of that , public spending should also be diverted across different aspect of social concerns that lead to the development of Singapore .
By putting a limit for the spending on the aged , we can create more budgets to spend on education , research and development , tourism industry and transportation system as they are equally important to our nation .
