No , I do not agree with the statement .
Current researches and development/polices have indeed eased the aging process but only to a small extent .
The aging issues that today 's elderly face include active life expectancy , diet/nutrition , disease prevention , health behaviors and beliefs , health service utilization , mental health , long term care etc .
The technological advancement in medical science will be discussed to address some of the issues mentioned .
With investment in technologies , it provides new opportunities for medical interventions .
For example , Stem Cell technology greatly helps to aid the discovery of new medicines by improving the process of developing new compounds .
By adopting this technology , we can now develop medicines that are safer and more effective .
This is necessary to help ease the aging process .
Moreover , with recent advances in science , more treatments can be developed to treat disease .
These treatments will be helpful because people get increasingly susceptible to chronic illnesses .
However , with new development of treatments , it will mean that there will be an increase in health care cost .
This will lead to an increase in burden for the elderly .
In the context of Singapore , to address this issue , various financial health care schemes like Medisave and Medishield are implemented to help lessen the financial burden for the elderly .
Technology and its advancements have given medical science the forefront to ease the aging process .
Another example will be the invention of nutritional supplements .
Research has found out that by taking nutritional supplements on a daily basis ,it can provide significant health benefits for the elderly , reducing the possibilities of them falling sick .
There are current on-going research on the different types of dietary supplements that can reverse disease , improve the overall health of the elderly and help them to live a longer , happier life .
This in turn slows down the ageing process and promotes a healthy lifestyle .
However , some nutritional supplements have harmful side effects .
It contains addictives that can deteriorate the health of the elderly .
Preventive measures can be taken by referencing medical brochures/guides , or consulting the doctor on the suitable type of supplements to consume if one has a medical history .
Such well-tested medical products have helped to ease the aging process .
When people grow older , they have to cope with the physical , mental and emotional stresses of being old. .
These stresses will cause negative influences on health as it affects our bodily functions .
However , social policy can address such issues to make the aging process less painful for the elderly .
For example , the Singapore government has introduced a pilot wellness programme for the elderly Singaporeans in an effort to promote a healthy lifestyle among them and also engaged them socially .
The key components are mainly regular medical-check ups and follow up , regular exercises , and social networking .
By exercising , the elderly improves their overall health and helps to prevent chronic diseases .
Social networking helps the elderly battle against loneliness and makes new friends .
All these factors improve the overall quality of life for the elderly .
However , social policy has to be revised to address the changing needs of the elderly .
With effective social policy , it will help to slow down the aging process .
However , the easing of the aging process does not only depend on the above factors .
Other factor includes individual 's responsibility on maintaining a healthy diet/nutrition .
So what type of foods should the elderly consume ?
According to Neilmark ( 2008 ) , The foods that decrease inflammation in the body are called " anti-inflammatory foods .
" These foods help stop the aging of our cells and help restore youth and vitality to our body and mind .
Elderly should adopt The Best Longevity Diet Around .
According to Neilmark ( 2008 ) , he defined it as eat fewer calories .
Eat no processed foods .
Eat no fried foods .
Take an ultra-refined fish oil supplement .
Exercise moderately .
Stop stressing : your mental diet .
Remain calm emotionally : your emotional diet .
?
In conclusion , current research and development/polices has helped to ease the aging process but only to a small extent .
Technology can be used as a solution to cope with the current healthcare challenges we are faced with .
However , in the future , healthcare systems have to be reformed to deal with the increased needs of healthcare support required by the aged .
While the advancement in healthcare industry can help prevent diseases and other consequences of aging , medicine alone is inadequate .
A healthy lifestyle is important for the elderly to enable them to cope with stresses physically , emotionally and mentally .
It also helps to reduce the risk of disease .
