" Build a better mousetrap , and the world will beat a path to your door " , said Ralph Waldo Emerson .
The quote can be used to express the significance of the engineering design processes to generate innovations in making a useful product for society and industry .
Among the developing countries , Vietnam is one of the fastest growing economies in which engineering design processes for innovations is now playing a more and more important role .
There are certain problems which are still obstructing those processes , two of them are the weak law protection of patent registration and the lack of entrepreneurship skills .
Nowadays , it is not difficult to look for a fashionable " Adidas " or " Nike " T-shirt on a street in Ho Chi Minh City , the biggest city of Vietnam .
The reason is not because Vietnam is attracting worldwide fashion brands due to its fast growing economy , but because it is not ever easier to make and sell fake T-shirts in Vietnam .
The issue of patent violation has been raised critically in recent years by Government and the society .
There are several problems in the governmental administrative level have been listed as the kernel of the issue .
Firstly , the National Inspection Organ has lacked of skills and human resource in investigating and tracing patent violation incidents .
Secondly , even when the violators are caught , the fines for their serious guilt are sometimes much lower than their unrighteous benefits ; this leads to the fact that the offenders would rather pay the fines than give up their business .
Moreover , the critical contraband good problem has affected not only foreign companies but also the local companies with low quality products with lower prices .
This whole bunch of weak supports from the Government policy and law has lead to serious hampers in the local creativity of engineering design .
The effort for researching new social needs turns into the effort for importing foreign products .
These obstacles could make Vietnam become a technology dependent country in the area .
For recent decades , entrepreneur concepts have started budding those first steps in Vietnam for .
However , low skills in entrepreneurship are still making a main issue in training business mindset for young generation .
For instance , the e-commerce breaking out in recent years has made a large number of start-up companies in IT and media communication .
Most of the company- starter had been technicians before deciding to start their business with lacked and weak entrepreneurial skills .
Therefore , the approach of social and economical factors in the entire system of engineering design was omitted .
As a result , a lot of companies have had to resize or change their business .
In fact , the lack of entrepreneurship skills has caused missing stages in the process of engineering design for innovations .
In conclusion , certain problems are temporarily blocking the development of innovations in Vietnam .
However , from what can be observed in these recent years , especially after Vietnam joined World Trade Organization ( WTO ) , strong actions have been taken in reforming the law system as well as promoting the entrepreneurship in universities .
With a positive view , Vietnam is trying to shorten the gap between itself with the area and the world .
Several effects on the development of Newater
Eleven years ago , Singapore welcomed its first Newater plant , which was a turning point in the history of the development of Singapore 's technology .
Newater represents the technology that purifies used water to make it clean and drinkable again ( The Write Staff ) .
During the last decade , the number of Newater plants has increased to four .
Currently , a new one is under construction .
What is more , in the near future , 30 % of the supply of water in Singapore will come from Newater .
In the history of Newater , the government , the lack of water resources and the development of other technologies have had a significant influence on the development of Newater .
First of all , the government has played a determining effect on the development of Newater .
Concerned about the water supply situation in Singapore , government officials decided to focus on the Newater technology to meet the water demand in Singapore especially for the industry and for commercial use ( The Write staff ) .
Thus , the successful development of Newater is due to sufficient funding invested by the government .
With the support of the Singapore government , the technology of Newater has blossomed and the fifth Newater plant was successfully set up in the Chanqi area this year .
Besides the support of the Singapore government , a lack of water supply pushed the development of Newater .
The shortage of potable water has become a global problem over the years .
What is more , about 40 percent of the population around the world and more than 80 countries are dealing with the problem of the lack of water ( ) .
In the case of Singapore , shortage of water results from several reasons such as its geographic position , its climate and its increasing population .
Consequently , Singapore needs to import water from neighboring countries such as Malaysia to meet its needs ( Lee , 2009 ) .
These reasons contributed to the development of Newater .
With the pressure of water shortage , having its own water supply system became more and more necessary for Singapore .
That is how the resource shortage led to the development of Newater .
The government and the lack of water resources are not the only factors that have affected the development of Newater ; the development of other technology has also played an important role in accelerating the development of Newater .
In the 1970s , Singapore was already paying attention to the technology of its own water supply system ; however , the cost was enormous and the technology was immature such as the unreliable membrane is not reliable ( The Write Staff ) .
Meanwhile , there have also been some other breakthroughs in the technology which have helped the development of Newater .
To conclude , external factors will affect the development of technology .
The development of Newater is a good example to demonstrate this .
The government invested funds to support the research on Newater .
In addition , resource crises , especially the shortage of water , pushed the development of Newater .
Meanwhile , the development of other technologies made Newater possible .
All of these factors have had a positive effect on the development of Newater and made it succeed .
