Prior to the Industrial Revolution in the 19th century , the needs of people were just basic-food , clothing , air and last but not least , shelter .
Now , the needs have just expanded from the basic four needs to other needs such as entertainment , communication , and transportation .
However , the question is which need requires more attention than the others in this modern era ?
The answer would be transportation .
Well , in order to have better transportation , design processes are needed to fulfill the need .
Transportation which is cheap and safe , environmentally friendly and uses alternative source of energy , is most desirable .
One of the eminent challenges faced by modern transportation is to depend less on fossil fuels .
With the rate of usage of fossil fuels - at three billion barrels per year now - , it will not take long before fuels get depleted .
According to a presentation made by Osman Chughtai and David Shannon fossil fuels will run out in 17 years minimum or a maximum of 50 to 70 years .
Nevertheless , other transportation problems like producing too much pollutants such as nitrogen oxides .
Pollutants produced have been proved to have had an enormous effect on the Earth 's ozone layer , corroding the ozone layers and exposing humans to deadly ultraviolet rays .
To add to the problems stated above , the world currently needs better transportation , in terms of safety and functionalities as well as cost .
As an example , cars produced must be durable , meaning that the cars must be able to withstand great momentum struck on them .
Besides that , weather must not be an obstacle for good cars .
In addition , cars must be low in cost despite having all the functionalities .
Therefore , in order to counter all the problems , engineers need to go through design processes .
First of all , engineering processes provide the foundation for research to get a new state-of-the-art design .
Engineers have to identify the problems such as producing a transport that does not run on fossil fuel .
Then , they can brainstorm to come up with a new design that meets all the criteria for a better car .
Recently , there was groundbreaking news stating that engineers found a technology called H2CAR process , a process for producing fuels from plants or what they call the process-biomass .
( Venere , E. New biofuels process promises to meet all U.S. transportation needs .
Retrieved on 5/09/2009.http : //www.purdue.edu/UNS/x/2007a/070314AgrawalBiomass.html )
Besides research , development processes enable engineers to produce designs that will be tested on real ground .
Effectiveness , durability and functionalities of the designs will be tested .
In this case , transportation like cars must be able to withstand extreme weathers and must be aerodynamically shaped for maneuverability .
Car safety must be included in the blueprint of the car as well .
Previously , engineers managed to come up with a design called catalytic converter with a function to reduce the pollutants released due to combustion .
In a nutshell , design processes are the main essence for a better future transportation , in terms of fuel type , environmentalenvironmental friendliness , functionalities as well as cost .
This need must be taken seriously in order to secure a brighter future -- a future where people do not need to travel on bicycle or on foot .
Mobile phone industry in China needs innovation
" Chinese mobile phone users total 703 million " ( HYPERLINK " http : //thegovmonitor.com/world_news/asia/chinese-mobile-phone-users-total-703-million-3376.html " http : //thegovmonitor.com/world_news/asia/chinese-mobile-phone-users-total-703-million-3376.html ) . This was reported on 4th September 2009 .
But seven out of ten mobile phonephone users are not using Chinese brands .
How can Chinese enterprises compete against foreign mobile phone companies ?
Innovation !
History has witnessed how mobile phone markets have always been broadened by new features of the phone .
Motorola 8900 which was available in market in the year 1995 was firstly featured with a cover so that wrong press of button was avoided .
In the same year the first self-chosen ring tone was heard from Ericsson GH398 .
The first folding phone was Motorola 328C born in January 1999 . Nokia 7110 is the first mobile phone with a wap browser which was released in October 1999 .
Hagenuk CH9771 was the first mobile phone with its antenna inside the phone .
All these new features brought a great raise in revenue .
Innovation shows great power in mobile market .
As the mobile phone is built up by so many parts , there are various ways of innovation .
Of all the aspects of innovation , appearance and function weigh the most .
Appearance means much because people treat mobile phones not only as communication tools but also as a kind of beloved toys .
Various functions are important because different places have different conditions .
I phone has conquered the whole world but failed to enter Japan 's market because of two reasons : First , Japanese like to own a unique style of phone but iphone has only one style which would cause embarrassment when Japanese meet other iphone users .
Second , Japanese phones have many functions such as mobile-shop which can help them pay bills on their phone .
But iphone does not have them .
As for appearance there are four major designs : straight , flip , slide and rotation .
After rotation , what is going to dominate the market ?
There are new appearances to be designed .
Such as a straight phone with 3-row,4-column keyboard .
To protect the fragile touch screen , the keyboard can act as the cover and leave only a little part of the screen outside when not used .
It is both cool and convenient to have a camera which can rotate like a transformer to make it easier to take phones for the photo-taker .
Function design has an endless way to go .
Basically a smart phone can have music player , video palyback , camera , GPS , wi-fi and so on .
There are plenty of functions now but the newer the better .
A phone can act as a telescope in Birdnest during the Beijing 2008 Olympic Games by using the camera and its zoom function .
It can also design a diet for its owner to lose weight .
A phone can be a weatherperson , an e-pet or whatever .
As technology develops and society changes , more and more functions will be possible and wanted .
Innovative mobile design is important also because designers can dominate both and market .
A new design is protected by its copyright so that for the producer meet slight competition entering the market .
To conclude , China 's mobile industry needs to work on innovation of phones ' appearance and function .
Problems significantly hamperhamper innovation in engineering design processes for innovations . Along with the rise in living standards , people 's demands for goods increase .
At the same time , people pay more attention to the quality of the goods .
In order to meet the demands of modern society , we need higher efficiency and more advanced technology .
Thus , the innovations in engineering processes are more and more important .
But in real life many problems hamper engineering design processes for innovations .
The two most significant are the state of information communication which is not smooth and corruption .
In practical production , only the workers directly use production equipment .
The senior management and the boss , who have the right to change and introduce new equipment and technologies , seldom care about the real condition of production .
So the only people who know the problems of production are the workers .
They may meet a lot of problems and may want to change the technologies .
But they do not have the power to do so .
And the state of information communication is not smooth , workers can not relay the problems that they found in production to the people who have the power to make decisions .
Maybe sometimes the workers come out with good ideas to solve the problems , but they do not have opportunities to put the ideas into practice .
And of course , the workers would not get rewards .
In this case , after a long time the workers lose enthusiasm to think about how to solve the problems .
And the company loses its opportunities to innovate .
At the same time , it loses the opportunity to save costs and increase production efficiency .
Another very important problem in practical production is corruption .
It often causes more serious problems than other problems .
It is a very serious problem that exists in almost every area .
For leaders in companies and factories , if they are corrupt , they only care about their own benefits and ignore many others .
There are many cases of corrupt leaders leading their whole companies or factories to go bankrupt .
And there are also some cases which are more scary .
Some set up a company just to cheat ; all their actions are about cheating for money from consumers or other companies .
For the staff , if they are corrupt , they would not focus on their jobs any more .
Furthermore , they would envy others who have a higher position or make more money or make greater contributions .
In such case , they may create a lot of bad things , maybe to frame others , in order to get more benefits for themselves .
For workers , they would only care about how to please their leaders to receive more benefits and not care about production .
The worse influence is for corrupt people to affect the general mood of a company or a factory .
To conclude , there are many existing problems hampering engineering design processes for innovations .
And the state of information communication and corruption are two most serious ones in my home country .
We should seek ways to solve them .
In this era of globalization , engineering design has been emphasized by governments all over the world , such as the United States , Russia and France .
This is because the development of engineering design could bring many advantages to a country 's economy and society .
Currently , scientists perceive a future problem and launch some research to overcome it .
If we observe our surroundings , we can see many inventions with technological creativity such as computer , automobile and other electrical appliances .
Nevertheless , there are some problems which significantly hamper engineering design processes for innovations in my home country , Malaysia , and impact certain stages of engineering design .
Firstly , financial problem is one of the factors which constrains engineering design processes for innovations .
As we all know , if we want to improve our engineering design , we need to launch much research .
Therefore , Research and Development ( R&D ) plays a very important part in engineering design processes for innovations .
Subsequently , a lump sum of money to be used to launch all such research , but our government is not able to invest much money on all .
So , financial problem arises and constrains the engineering design processes for innovations .
Malaysia is a country which is still developing and not as wealthy as other western developed countries such as the United States , France and Germany .
Hence , we lack money to improve our facilities for research such as well-equipped laboratories and other highly technological instruments .
In fact , this will cause engineering design processes to be interrupted halfway because of lack of highly technological instruments .
For instance , if we want to design a race car , we need some highly technological instruments to do research on car engines and other parts of a car .
And although we have already found important information through research , we still can not continue analyses of design solutions because of lack of highly technological instruments to be used for investigation .
Other than financial problem , we are also facing the problem of lack of professionals in certain engineering fields such as mechanical engineering , chemical engineering and electrical engineering .
Much of the research engineering design carried out in modern countries been done successfully .
This is because there are many professionals in their countries .
In fact , the lack of professionals in engineering fields has resulted in the failure of some research .
For instance , some of the automobile research due to the lack of professionals .
The stage of analysis of design solution has been constrained because of limited knowledge and lack of professionals .
Hence , some forums on engineering design should be held between our country and other modern countries .
For instance , the forum on how to manufacture an eco-car can be held in order to help us exchange our opinions with the professionals from modern countries .
In a nutshell , financial problem and lack of professionals in my home country should be solved as soon as possible to improve our engineering design processes .
Hence , the private sector , the government and also citizens should work hand in hand in order to encourage more investment in engineering design research and produce more professionals in the field of engineering design in the future .
A Big Country With Little Innovation
Indonesia , a country with more than two hundred and thirty million citizens , is South East Asia 's largest country and economy to date .
Yet Indonesia still trails behind its neighboring countries such as Malaysia , Thailand , and even The Little Red Dot : Singapore , in terms of advancement in design-based technology .
It is commonly believed that the slow rate of technological growth in Indonesia is caused by two major problems which may hamper the innovative engineering design process .
Firstly , Indonesia lacks a culture of innovation .
According to statistics published by UNICEF in 2007 , only fifty percent of Indonesian citizens are urbanized , which means the other half live in rural areas with little exposure to the modern world and technology .
People living in traditional villages live very simple lives .
They keep their ancestors ' traditions , and sometimes prefer the traditional way of doing things to labor-saving modern devices ; for example ; some farmers prefer buffalo-driven ploughs to tractors .
Moreover , farmers still rely on government supplies and subsidies , which run into a lot of logistical problems , instead of innovating their own way of solving problems .
Besides , most universities in Indonesia are more teaching based based and less research intensive than those in Japan or The States ; that makes Indonesian university students less creative and innovative in problem solving .
As a result , Indonesian engineers usually provide less possibility of solutions in tackling a problem compared to those who are trained abroad .
The second problem that may hamper the engineering design process in Indonesia is due to its excessive and cheap natural resources , space , and workforces .
As mentioned above , Indonesia has more than two hundred and thirty million citizens , and its unemployment rate is considered high at 9.1 % ( Reuters , 2008 ) .
Thus , Indonesia needs to create jobs for its people ; one way is by developing its agricultural businesses , which have been a hot topic lately during the presidential campaign .
Prabowo Subianto , son of Sumitro Djojohadikusumo , former minister of economics for both Indonesia and Malaysia , during his vice presidential campaign opposed a solution to current Indonesian problems . He promised to create jobs by developing bio diesel producing palm plantation in Indonesia , which may absorb about 6 million workforces .
It is apparent that innovative and labor-saving devices will not work in Indonesia ; the new invention seemed to be more expensive compared to the traditional way .
The impact of Indonesia 's cheap resources on engineering design process is on its implementation stage .
After the invention is patented , there is nobody who is willing to buy it because in Indonesia 's case it is not cost efficient .
Another effect is demotivation of young engineers from designing new products , because the rewards the society gives them is not equal to their long-time hardwork .
In conclusion , Indonesia still faces several challenges in developing its design-based technology .
To tackle them , the Indonesian government has to work hard in developing an innovative culture in the society , and decreasing the people 's dependability on the government .
According to Khandani 's statement " What distinguishes engineers from painters , poets , or sculptors is that engineers apply their creative energies to producing products or systems that meet human needs " , all engineering designs aim to meet human demands to become successful products .
Now , when society develops , people are looking for new designs to satisfy their comfortable lives .
ThThesese new designs may be demands for entertainment , education or even something beyond our imagination .
However , in my opinion , one of the main concerns in our society is finding a new energy supply to substitute for the old ones which have been depleted due to human exploitation .
In order to solve this urgent demand , engineering plays an important role in finding other alternatives such as nuclear energy , solar energy and geothermal energy .
Evidently , energy has become vital and indispensable in our life , relating to most of everything we deal with .
Because of the influence of energy , natural resources have invisibly caused wars and conflicts between many countries over time .
The recent war between the United States and Iraq in 2000 might be considered to be a typical example .
Although the U.S. has been saying that this war is for anti-terrorism , or more importantly for maintaining peace the world , it is clear that one of the reasons why American troopers stay in Iraq is the benefits of petroleum .
This is a typical example of how important energy is since it has a great impact on our daily life .
Due to the non-renewability of natural " fossil " resources , the more demands society needs , the more exhausted these resources become .
According to the online newspaper Financial Times ( 2006 ) and USA Today news ( 2004 ) , the oil reserves in Trinidad and Tobago will run out in the next 20 years and the world oil reserves will become exhausted just in 40 years .
These figures partly show the urgent necessity to find a feasible alternative energy source which will never become exhausted .
The process of finding a new alternative energy source , which is not only renewable but also environmental-friendly , has been undertaken for a long time and regarded as an ultimate goal for engineering .
The most popular energy is nuclear energy .
It is extracted from usable energy from heavy atomic nuclei ( for example Uranium 235 ) via of nuclear reactions .
The first nuclear plant was built in Russia in 1984 whose initial electricity production was about 5000KW .
Nowadays , nuclear power is harnessed for many purposes in our daily life .
It may create electricity , equipment or even weapons like the nuclear bomb or nuclear power submarines .
However , the design of nuclear reaction has to meet many rigorous requirements to avoid nuclear releases as well as to isolate radiation from life .
All of these conditions have to be followed strictly ; otherwise it may cause immeasurable consequences .
For instance , one of the most tragic accidents involving radiation release was the Chernobyl disaster which happened in 1986 .
This disastrous accident resulted from weakness in design . Up to now , the neighboring areas still suffer from the radiation .
Another solution is the perpetual resources known as solar , geothermal energy , etc.The solar energy is drawn from sunlight 's energy by many solar panels which are designed to fit house roofs .
This energy is converted into electric or thermal energy to serve our life .
Geothermal power takes the thermal calorie in the entrails of the earth and translates into other energies which contribute an important role in operating turbines and machines .
There are three basic types of geothermal energy plants ( i.e .
the dry steam plants , flash steam plants and binary power plants ) .
Geothermal energy is considered as the most potential alternative for nonrenewable energy in the future .
Though the perpetual resources are always there for us , their use may be constrained by the lack of technology for control and delivery , and also by investment and willingness to pay .
Also , these resources may not be applied and used everywhere on earth due to geographic differences .
In conclusion , I contend that energy problem should be classified as first priority for humans to solve not only because of many huge benefits it provides for people but also because of the critical shortage of energy resources .
In this context , engineering design process meet these urgent needs by finding many feasible solutions such as nuclear energy , solar energy and geothermal energy sources .
Although this process has just had initial achievements , it promises a fully potential energy source in the future which may permanently serve human kind .
Nowadays , the petrol price has fluctuated a lot .
Thus , many countries spend more money and time on developing new resources which can be used as a substitute for petroleum .
Energies such as solar energy have been promoted to fulfill this purpose .
This can be seen through the increase in research and development of solar cars or other products .
The use of solar energy-related goods has been highly encouraged by environmentalists .
So , I would like to discuss the reasons for innovation in such technology based on economic , governmental and environmental factors .
First of all , as earlier mentioned , petrol price has been fluctuating in recent years . This makes many factories start to worry about the cost and profit they can earn .
Most of them feel unsecured because the cost of petrol may lead to low profit or even red deficit .
Thus , they are keen to find out more substitutions .
In the process we can see many firms and companies start to invest in solar energy areas .
As solar power is actually inexhaustible and reproducible , they can use it whenever they want and it is free of charge as well .
However , the start-up cost is pretty high .
It is because of the cost of batteries .
Presently , there is limitation on the amount of energy the batteries can store as we can only " use solar cells to generate up to 240 watts of electrical power in full sunshine .
As long as we can find a way to increase the amount of energy the batteries can store , the cost will not be much a problem anymore .
So I think , although they have to spend much more on research now , they can definitely save more in the long run .
Secondly , petrol resources are not evenly distributed around the world .
This means that some countries control more petrol while some may not have it at all .
This results in certain countries feeling unsecured as they are afraid that their potential enemies may use this as a weak point to harm them .
For example , their enemy may cut down the inflow of the petrol provided to their land .
Without petrol , the economy in the country will be affected badly .
Lastly , solar energy is free of pollution .
It is commonly known that burning of petroleum will release carbon dioxide , nitrogen and some other gases which will cause air pollution .
This will in turn cause many harmful results including acidic rain or global warming .
On the contrary , solar energy will not lead to such pollution .
And as solar energy comes from the sun , it can be regarded as reproducible and we do not need to worry about if it will be depleted one day .
In conclusion , I think we should decrease the use of petrol-related products and slowly switch towards using the products which need new resources .
Only if we show our interests in and demands for these products , researchers can have motivation and more funds to do their projects .
REFERENCE
Section 2 , Practical applcations , 2009/09/07 wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_cars # Limitations_and_challenges
Water Need Should Be Given Priority in Designing
Engineers are indispensable .
Their achievements influence the development of every industry .
As the application of engineering spreads , few can tell the exact range of engineers ' work .
But one task of all the engineers is common : to meet people 's needs .
People 's needs are so various that one prime need must be given priority to avoid distractions .
In today 's world , this need should be people 's demand for fresh water .
As is known , water is a resource that humans can not live without .
Its uses range from climate regulation and industry application to food processing and daily drinking .
Water is even the sign of life .
Scientists often use it as the first criteria to judge whether there is life on a new landed planet .
This means that water is probably the first thing creatures need to maintain life .
Therefore , water is also one essential need for people to survive .
A hundred years ago , water was never a concern ,
while today it is different .
Some people even assume that the next world war will be fought because of limited fresh water on the earth .
In order to ensure humans ' survival and world peace , engineers should respect humans ' need for water most when designing products .
One aspect engineers should work on to meet people 's need of water is to reduce pollution in the engineering process .
Pollution is one main reason for water scarcity .
To be exact , there is never a lack of water on earth , but pollution damaged most of the available water sources , such as rivers and lakes .
Pollution in water is often caused by waste emission generated in industry processes .
To solve this problem , the best way is to emphasis environmental friendliness when engineers design machines or develop new procedures for industry use .
This can stop pollution in water more thoroughly than government 's fine on water pollution .
In addition , engineers can design a device that can save water .
People are using water everywhere in life other than in industry .
Therefore , if a device can avoid wasting water in the daily life of each person , it will surely save a considerably large amount of water .
Small devices like taps , water coolers , and washing machines , can all be the targets of engineers .
Engineers should give importance to water-efficiency together with other efficiencies regarding designing devices , so that enough water can be conserved to meet people 's needs .
To sum up , engineering should give priority to people 's need of water first , as water is necessary for human survival .
In order to highlight this need , engineers should emphasize environmental friendliness and water saving in designing .
For the next 10 years or more , Singapore have a high percentage of population consisting of the elderly .
There are a few factors leading to an ageing population like low birth rates and increase in the cost of standard of living .
With the increase in the number of elderly , there would be a need for safety areas , thus products or services should be designed to meet this need .
For example , one of the current market products is called " MEMSwear " which is produced by National University of Singapore engineers .
This product is a smart suit that is equipped with an array of microsensors which are able to detect falls suffered by the wearers and to send alerts to their caregivers .
Besides these functions , the engineers have also included an " impact-reduction " system to reduce the damage done on the wearer when he or she falls .
For the product , we have seen that the engineers have made use of engineering design processes to meet the need .
Firstly , they have defined the problem , which is ageing population , and they have seen the need to invent a product which could give extra safety protection to the elderly .
Secondly , they have brainstormed on the preliminary criteria for a better design for the product ( Khandani , 2005 ) ) .
For example , for the first version of the product , they have not included the " impact-induction " system .
Without this feature , the wearer might suffer a serious accident if he or she falls .
Thus , through the use of engineering design processes , they have come out with a better design of the product .
Next , this is another product which works alike as the previous product .
But other than the features that the " MEMSwear " has , this product has additional functions ( Khandani , S. ( 2005 ) ) .
One of the functions is that upon receiving an alert when the user has a serious fall , it would dial for ambulance immediately .
This would greatly reduce the consequences of the fall if actions are taken within a shorter time .
Another additional function is the implementation of a temperature sensor .
For instance , in the case of a fire , the temperature sensor would be alerted and will send warning alerts to their caregivers or call for Civil Defense Force immediately .
Furthermore , when considering the design of the product , there is a need to make special considerations that are suitable for elderly use .
Engineers would have to use the engineering design processes to list out multiple solutions the designing of product ( Khandani , S. ( 2005 ) ) .
For each solution , they would have to analyze and select one of the best solutions that suits most of the criteria listed .
In order to make sure the product works well , engineers have to test it before they launch the product .
In conclusion , we have seen that the problems of ageing population could get more serious in the next few years , thus there is a need to design a product that could help to reduce the risks and impacts faced by the ageing population .
Through examples of these two products , we could see that both of them have made use of engineering design processes to meet the need .
And thus , they proved that it is really important to go through engineering design processes when inventing a new product .
Human activities on Earth have depleted Earth 's valuable yet limited natural resources , thus damaging the Earth 's environment .
This causes Earth 's natural resources to be depleted and modify its environment so much that it is no longer suitable for human life .
Therefore , humans have to give priorities to conserving Earth 's natural resources and protecting its environment .
This can be achieved by completely setting aside already available engineering processes , modifying and improving these old processes , or correctly identifying the reasons for the rise of that need .
Firstly , engineering processes that are available now and are widely used can be abolished while new ones can be introduced to perform the functions of their precursors and at the same time fulfil the need .
For instance , humans have always depended on one of Earth 's natural resources , fossil fuels , as an important source of energy .
However , due to human s ' overuse of it , fossil fuels are expected to be completely depleted in the year 2050 .
Therefore , engineering processes of technologies that extract energy from fossil fuels must be superseded and new ones must be introduced to ensure a constant supply of energy for humans .
For example , western powers like countries in Europe and the United States are planning to construct large scale solar energy farms in areas in Africa like the Sahara desert to replace generating energy from fossil fuels .
Since solar energy is a renewable source of energy and therefore can not be depleted .
Furthermore , the burning of fossil fuels produces harmful substances like carbon dioxide and smoke particles that can destroy Earth 's environment .
However , clean energy sources like solar energy do not cause these problems .
Therefore , we can see how setting aside old engineering processes and embracing new ones can satisfy that need .
Secondly , instead of removing available engineering processes , they can also be modified so that their original functions are still available but at the same time satisfy the need to preserve natural resources and protect the environment .
For example , transportation systems like cars require fuels like fossil fuels which are processed from a depleting natural resource , fossil fuels .
Furthermore , greenhouse gases like carbon dioxide are produced from these cars which contribute to the notorious greenhouse effect .
To solve this problem , engineering processes like the designing of the car 's engine can be changed .
For instance , electric cars by General Motors use electricity to power the car 's engine instead of fossil fuels .
This satisfies the need as electricity can be generated from renewable sources of energy like solar and wind energy .
Furthermore , greenhouse gases like carbon dioxide will also not be emitted .
Thus , we can observe how modifying available engineering processes can satisfy the need .
Thirdly , the need can be fulfilled by correctly identifying and analyzing the reason for the rise of that need , so that correct decisions can be made through engineering processes .
For example , CFC gases in the past are a by-product of many of our industries .
These gases caused the destruction of the Earth 's ozone layer in the atmosphere which caused more harmful ultraviolet , UV rays to penetrate the atmosphere , and consequently health problems like skin cancer to humans due to these UV rays .
Therefore , a worldwide policy was implemented to ban the emission of CFC gases into the atmosphere by industries .
Thus , we can see how making correct decisions to prevent pollution to the environment can fulfill the need .
In conclusion , to ensure a sufficient supply of natural resources and a healthy environment for us and our future generations to live in , engineering processes can meet our needs by removing and introducing or modifying available engineering processes and making correct decisions through these processes .
According to Khandani ( 2005 ) , engineers design products or systems that meet human needs .
Out of all the human needs in the world , clean water should be given priority compared with others .
Despite the fact that the amount of water on earth is quite large , nevertheless , we can only drink a very small part of it .
It is because most of the water in the world is sea water , which is not potable at all .
In addition , due to global warming , the sea level rises .
Therefore , some precious sources of drinking water , like underground water , are polluted and not drinkable any more , which makes the situation even worse .
In some regions in the world , such as the Middle East and Africa , the shortage of clean drinking water is very serious , which sometimes causes wars .
To solve this problem , there are two ways in which engineers can contribute .
The first way is to design a system to recycle used water .
Water we daily use can be divided into two categories , for drinking and not for drinking .
For example , water we use to flush toilets , to irrigate farmland and to wash cars is not necessary to reach the same hygienic level as the drinking water .
Hence , we may use recycled water to do these jobs so that we can save more clean drinking water for people .
Actually , this idea has already been adopted by many countries to relieve the pressure caused by the shortage of water .
Moreover , some developed countries , such as Singapore , have mastered this technology so well that recycled water can be drunk directly , which really helps a lot to solve the problem of shortage of water .
However , this method may not be suitable for developing and undeveloped countries because it costs a lot of money , and the technology required is also very high .
The other way to get drinking water is through desalination of sea water .
As mentioned before , the amount of sea water is truly vast ; therefore , humans can certainly take sea water as another source of drinking water .
However , the process of desalination of sea water is very difficult .
It requires highly advanced science and technology , and of course , it is very costly .
Another limitation of this method is that it can only be applied in seaside countries , like Singapore , which means that it is not the first choice of many inland countries .
But since it also has its advantage , like the huge and widespread source , it is still worth trying .
According to Khandani ( 2005 ) , the net result or purpose of most engineering designs is to produce a product that generates a profit for the company .
Therefore , since the two methods mentioned above are both costly and difficult to apply , they can be restricted by the economic and the market and thus , they may be not able to solve the shortage of water in a short period .
But what is important is that , at least , these two methods give us hope .
It is this kind of hope that motivates humans to develop , to improve , to pursue our dreams , and finally to have such a beautiful world today .
Hope is the most significant contribution which engineers have contributed to the world .
The environment-friendly car is a current human need which should be given priority .
Humans need to travel from one place to another easily .
The current car 's technology , the fuel injection , has satisfied that need , but has not satisfied the environment 's need .
Humans need a car which is not only able to transport them easily but also is friendly to the environment .
It is the doctors ' job to apply their creative energies in designing a solution which meets humans ' needs .
First of all , the current car 's technology , the fuel injection , has satisfied humans ' need to travel .
For example , the time taken to travel from one place to another with a distance of a few hundred kilometres has been reduced from 2-3 days to 2-3 hours ; as a result , humans are able to travel instantly .
This indeed makes human s ' means of transportation rising to another level .
Second , in contrast with the benefit fuel injection has contributed to human life , it has , in fact , polluted the environment .
This is due to fuel processing in the car .
For example , fuel injection is exhausting Carbon Dioxide ( CO2 ) as a result of incomplete burning of fuels .
Carbon dioxide is a greenhouse gas that traps the earth 's heat and contributes to global warming .
Third , humans not only need to travel but also need a pollution -free environment to live in .
In view of this issue , engineers are needed to design a solution .
According to Khandani ( 2005 ) , products or systems are designed by engineers to meet human needs .
For years , engineers have experimented on designing a solution to this issue .
For example , Japan 's engineers have experimented for about 10 years before they successfully designed an eco-car which makes use of electric energy .
This eco-car has no fuel tank , therefore , it produces no emissions at all .
On top of that , Japan 's eco-car is as fast as the fuel injection car .
Lastly , Japan 's engineers had followed engineering design processes Khandani ( 2005 ) to design their first eco-car .
They started by defining the problem of the fuel injection system .
They argued that the fuel injection system 's problem lies in the fuel it uses .
Therefore , Japan 's engineers started to look for alternate fuel for their eco-car .
They gathered information in order to arrive successfully at the right fuel source ; subsequently , they decided to use electricity as the fuel .
The road to success is not smooth ; likewise , Japan 's engineers had gone through a lot of challenges and tests before they arrived at the final prototype of Japan 's first eco-car .
Humans need to care about the environment 's condition in order to preserve it for the new generation .
The new generation deserves to live in the same environment as we do .
To conclude , by using engineering design processes , engineers can design products that meet human needs .
Healthcare is a basic essential in every country .
It compromises of the people 's living condition , availability of medical treatment and prevention of disease .
Emphasis on healthcare services differs from country to country .
For instance in Singapore and Japan , healthcare is emphasized on the elderly due to their aging populations but both execute their policies in different ways .
Hence , we will look at the principle of healthcare of the elderly in respective countries and the solution to the healthcare needs of an aging population .
The aging community has become an eminent issue in Singapore .
With a replacement rate of 1.5 children to 2 adults and an estimation that by 2030 , 18.4 % of the population will be made up by the elderly , it is no wonder why Singapore government is promoting reproduction in young couples .
As the population ages , the main users of hospital services will be the elderly .
Therefore , improvement in healthcare services for the elderly is essential .
Mobility of the elderly is a factor as well , as they have problems walking and moving around .
According to a survey in 2004 , Singapore is one of the unfriendliest countries towards the wheel chair bounded .
Hence , there is a need for us to impove the healthcare services of our older citizens .
In Japan , nearly one quarter of the population is made up of the elderly .
This is mainly due to the speed of industrialization in Japan .
Being one of the economic giants , Japan industrializes very fast at an early stage .
This causes an imbalance between work and family .
The fast paced society forces citizens to place work as priority over family resulting in a declining population .
In addition , in Japan , pay increases with the age of the workers .
Hence , companies tend to seek younger employees causing the older workers to lose their jobs and their health pension benefits .
Since the number of elderly is increasing , it is important to cater to their needs in terms of healthcare .
The first concern is the living condition of the elderly .
Home care facilities such as hospices , day care centres and nursing homes are built to look after the elderly especially when their family members are unable to do so .
For example , in Singapore , one room apartment with specially installed emergency buttons and lifts is catered to the elderly .
These apartments are created in such a way that they minimize the risk of the elderly injuring themselves .
The second concern is the mobility of the elderly .
Shopping malls and other common places should be equipped with more ramps and handicapped -friendly escalators .
Furthermore , on trains in Singapore , certain seats are allocated for the elderly .
Last but not least , health benefits for elderly should be protected .
They should be offered free medical check-ups and treatment if necessary .
In conclusion , healthcare services should not be neglected especially in countries which face an aging population .
More need to be done to improve our healthcare sector so as to achieve a healthier and wealthier society .
Over the past century , numerous research breakthroughs and creative innovations have allowed engineering design processes to meet various human needs .
According to Khandani ( 2005 ) , engineering designs are systems that are introduced by humans through combining different technologies and innovations to satisfy a particular human need creating ability for humans to complete a task faster or more efficiently .
To produce these systems , design processes are carried out over a period of time , ranging from months to years , and they are conducted based on a series of steps .
For example , water supply has been a main concern for the Singapore government as Singapore has no natural sources of water .
Consequently , after years of research and design to alleviate this problem , the NEWater technology was invented .
This technology allows used water to be reusable after undergoing treatment through microfiltration and reverse osmosis .
Even though engineering design processes have been aiding humans in meeting many of their needs in the past , many others have yet to be satisfied ; and the need to tackle pollution is one of them .
Pollution has been an ongoing problem for the past few decades or so and thus far , little has been done to alleviate this problem .
Global warming , as a result , is becoming more and more an issue of rising concern as little has been done to eliminate or substantially reduce pollution .
Temperature has been increasing due to the excessive release of greenhouse gases ; and sea levels have been rising due to the melting of ice caps in the North and South poles .
Time is running out and to protect the sustainability of life on Earth , necessary actions have to be taken immediately , and if not , as soon as possible , and the help of engineering design processes should not be left out .
First and foremost , vehicles have been a main source of pollution and a large contributor to the emission of greenhouse gases .
In the past , vehicles used to emit harmful gases such as carbon monoxide .
Subsequently , engineering design processes have made possible the invention of catalytic converters which convert the harmful gases emitted by vehicles into non-harmful gases .
On the flip side , although the problem of emission of harmful gases has been , vehicles today are releasing carbon dioxide , which is a greenhouse gas , instead .
Consequently , a new engineering design process has to be carried out to rectify this problem .
After years of research , then comes the idea of inventing an environmentally-friendly car , also known as an ecocar .
For example , a group of Engineering and Design students from Singapore has invented its first environmentally-friendly car which does not emit any amount of carbon .
This is an example of a great breakthrough of an engineering design process which will be able to tackle the problem of pollution .
Another area of concern that is contributing much to the pollution of the environment is energy generation .
Power stations , also known as power plants , are common sources of energy in most countries and they make use of the combustion of fuels to produce energy in powering up the whole city .
Due to the combustion of fuels , pollution occurs ; and taking into consideration that many countries have adopted the use of power stations , the effects of polluting the environment occur on a large scale .
Therefore , cleaner sources of energy generation have to be discovered and engineering design processes can do just that .
An example of a clean method of energy generation would be the invention of solar technology .
Solar technology makes use of heat and radiation from the Sun to produce useful forms of energy ; and this is made possible by engineering design processes .
To conclude , pollution is an ongoing , serious problem in which swift actions need to be taken .
It is a human need to neutralize this situation because Earth 's and human 's sustainability is at stake .
With engineering design processes , the benefits of gaining control over pollution are tremendous .
However , engineering design processes take a certain period of time as factors such as safety and other side effects have to be put into consideration too .
Moreover , we humans can not be totally dependent on engineering design systems only .
We have to be socially-responsible as every living person has a part to play in tackling pollution .
Throughout the years , there has always been a debate on whether technology shapes society , a technologically determinist perspective , or society shapes technology , a socially determinist view .
One such technology that is closely related to this debate is the invention of the automobile .
Without this invention , we would probably still be riding the bicycle to work or school .
Looking back at history , we can see how this important technology has been shaped by societal factors as well as technological factors .
Due to the influence of these factors , gasoline-powered cars have won over electric cars for years .
Firstly , societal factors like the expansion of cities favor gasoline cars over electric cars .
As cities grow bigger , it becomes impractical to have an electric car for travelling .
For example , gasoline-powered cars can travel an average of about 300km on a full tank of petrol as compared to a maximum distance of 150km for a full charge on an electric battery .
In big cities like the United States , travelling to and fro from work can easily surpass 100km .
Also with the expansion of society , time becomes money .
No one is willing to spend 8 hours a day waiting for their car to be charged fully before they can make use of it .
Another societal factor is the increase in individualism among people .
Everyone now wants to own a car for convenience and for individualism 's sake .
In one family , there could be three cars ; one for the father , the mother and the son .
Take Dubai for instance . They now have an average ratio of 571 cars to every 1000 people .
Therefore , this affects automobiles as people purchase more gasoline powered cars .
The reason is that car manufacturers , in order to retain their market share of gasoline powered cars , will invest time and money to promote gasoline-powered vehicles over the unproven market of electric cars .
A social stigma that electric cars are only meant to be golf carts or less is hence created , and this leads to people purchasing gasoline-powered cars .
Next , technological factors like currently available technology and limitation of resources have also helped shaped automobiles .
With current technology , more hybrid cars are showing up on the market .
Hybrid cars involve either part gasoline and part electric or part gasoline and part compressed natural gas ( CNG ) .
This is made possible only with the advancement of technology as compared to the past .
For instance , the regenerative brake system has been invented whereby you charge your battery just by braking .
Car manufacturers like Chevrolet are cashing in on this possible new market , and coming up with new models like the Optra Magnum CNG in 2008 .
With a cleaner and efficient hybrid car , more people are opting for the switch .
The gasoline-powered car has finally seen a worthy competitor .
However , technological restraints like limited resources have been a set back for hybrid users .
Looking at Singapore for example , there are only 5 CNG refueling points around the country .
To get your vehicle refueled would be troublesome if the nearest CNG petrol station is far away .
This constraint makes consumers think twice before purchasing a hybrid vehicle .
Also , the fact that hybrid cars are a relatively new technology , car repair shops might not have the knowledge to repair hybrid cars yet , and any repairs must be sent back to the car manufacturer .
This makes it inconvenient if the shop is located far away from the consumer .
In short , these few factors have played an important role in shaping the automobiles that we know today .
Imagine if there are no technological restraints and that we could create a self replenishing battery .
The possibilities are endless , but it proves one point .
Technology and society co-exist and affect one another .
Even until now , we are shaping many other technological inventions .
Only the future can foretell the impact of these factors on technological advancement such as in the automobile industry .
Who knows , hybrid cars might actually manage to successfully dethrone gasoline-powered cars in the near future .
Electronics such as lights and cars have become essential to human beings over the past years .
However , these electronics though wonderful , consume a huge amount of energy .
Given that the global price of fuel is on the rise , users of these electronics are incurring higher cost .
One current human need that should be given priority for engineering design is to have cos-saving electronics .
Firstly , the problems with lights is that , in order to save electricity , the user will have to manually turn off the lights upon leaving the area , which is rather impractical in places such as offices , toilets and classrooms which require the lights to be constantly turned on .
The idea of electricity conservation on usage of lights was to have the lights automatically turned off when the area is empty .
As a result , the idea sparked off the concept of integrating motion sensors to lights .
The challenge in having a motion sensor light to automatically turn on and off the lights with the presence of a human being was how to accurately identify the presence of a human being in the area monitored by the sensor .
To overcome the challenge , the motion sensors use infrared energy to detect human beings .
In addition , these sensors are also highly sensitive to human body temperature , therefore resulting in a highly accurate detection .
Today these motion sensor lights are used almost everywhere , in offices , toilets , classrooms and even homes .
Secondly , the recent price hikes in petrol fuel have caused human beings to pay a higher amount of money for their car petrol as compared to previously .
To overcome the price hikes , an alternative to petrol fuel is needed .
The outcome of intensive engineering design was to replace petrol fuel with ( CNG ) Compressed Natural Gas .
These natural gases are widely available on earth as compared to petrol fuel which is getting limited as oil reserves get depleted .
In order for a car to be powered using CNG , there are certain modifications that needed to be done .
For example , new fuel storage was introduced , and took the name of Integrated Storage System .
Another example is the modification of the engine .
The natural gas from the storage cylinders flows into a fuel line when the engine is started .
The gas is then ignited by a spark plug , thus powering the car .
In Singapore , public transports such as taxis and buses have converted to CNG .
In addition , according to Channel NewsAsia , there is an increasing number of private cars owners converting their conventional petrol fuel-powered cars to CNG cars .
Engineering designs have improved the designs of lights and cars , which used to consume a huge amount of energy in the past .
To sum up , with the depletion of natural resources and high electricity and fuel cost , engineering designing should be given priority to cost saving electronics .
Engineering design is the process of creating a system or products to meet the desired needs of people .
Usually , engineers face difficulty in designing a product or coming out with ideas demanded by the public .
An engineer needs to define the problem , gather pertinent information , generate and analyse multiple solutions and finally , test and implement the solution .
However , the two most disturbing problems that may hamper engineering design processes for innovations are the inability of engineers to generate multiple solutions to convince their superior to implement their products or ideas and the failure of constantly creating a product that is in demand .
Firstly , in the aspect of generating multiple solutions , engineers often face the problems of lack of funds and inability to convince their superior that their idea is feasible .
In most cases , their design will be rejected because the product or idea is not conventional .
Their idea or product is a totally new concept which people may find hard to accept because of a traditional idea or product that may have been etched in their mind .
For example , in the Singapore National Service , military officers , using their portion of dominant influence , typically make most of the important decisions about innovation .
In addition , low ranking cadets usually fail to convince high ranking officers that their innovative products or ideas may improve the military .
One example is the introduction of unmanned combat air vehicles by the engineers in the military .
This unmanned combat air vehicle might have been potent enough to replace the ubiquitous manned fighter in the near future .
However , due to the higher officer not having enough trust over the air vehicle being piloted by a human , this unmanned combat vehicle project did not succeed in being implemented .
Instances such as the above example will significantly affect the morale of the engineers .
Hence , it is imperative to address the issue of engineers unable to convince their superior to implement their products or ideas .
As engineers , if their ideas or products face constant rejection by their superior , they will stop coming up with new ideas or products as they see no purpose in coming up with new ideas or products and constantly opposing their superiors .
Thus , superiority in companies will significantly hamper engineers ' morale and their design .
Secondly , the other problem that restricts engineering design is the lack of confidence to implement ideas or products that are in demand .
Although in the initial stage response to their products may be good , when it comes to implementing their ideas or products , the response may be different .
Engineers spend a lot of effort in developing these products , but the final products that they design may not be of popular demand .
Society always strives for useful and economic products .
Products that are not practical and expensive will face rejection .
For instance , in the 1960s , Singapore developed a phone that was able to see the other caller .
This type of phone faced rejection because it was expensive and users found it infringing on their privacy .
As a result , sales of these phones were low , affecting the morale of the engineer who designed it .
Facing multiple failures may cause engineers to be disheartened and put them on high alert as they will be more careful when they want to design a product .
They will tend to feel disappointed because they need to solicit a lot of funds , putting in their utmost efforts when developing the products , but only to find out that their products face rejection by the public .
This will seriously restrict their innovation because they may be afraid to face constant failure .
The " best " design solution is always hard to develop because it is one that most completely fulfils a client 's requirements .
Therefore , engineers may just stop at gathering pertinent information , and not go into generating multiple solutions as they worry that their products may not be in demand as expected , which again may hamper their design processes for innovation .
In conclusion , it is usually the lack of ability to convince their superiors and the constant rejection by the public that significantly hamper engineering design for innovations .
Traditional mindsets should be changed and let engineers have a chance to develop their ideas .
Furthermore , engineers should do their research and marketing of their products effectively , such that products that they develop will be of market value .
Scientific technology has been developing rapidly since the first industrial revolution .
Meanwhile , many new kinds of innovative inventions come out almost every day , thus changing the way people live .
It is a remarkable fact that technical innovation is viewed differently by different groups of people .
A wonderful invention to a group of people may be disliked others .
In general , the justification of the utility of a specific technology or invention depends on the specific opinions of different group of people .
Space technology is a good example to explain the existence of different views .
Space technology is a kind of highly innovative , highly composite and also highly costly technology .
The beginning of space technology was in America and Russia .
Then it quickly spread out all over the world .
Nowadays European countries , China , Japan and India all have advanced development in space technology .
Toward this new technique , two opposite opinions exist nowadays .
Governments and scientists think it is worth to spend money and people working on this because it will benefit the whole country .
However , many people think that it is a waste of resources which can be used to improve people 's living conditions .
If we look a little deeper into the causes that lead to the opposite solution , we will find that the focus that specific groups of people pay attention to is , obviously , quite different from each other .
From the governments ' and scientists ' point-of-view , space technology is essential because it is the fundamental thing we need to do to protect our countries and fulfill future needs .
They pay much attention to keep technological developdevelopment moving and concentrate more on huge issues , like military demand , and the future .
That is also the reason why every country tries its best to improve space technology .
Former President of America Reagan even announced the star wars program , although it was given up at the end .
On the contrary , civilians who state the opposite idea think the same issue another way round .
They focus more on current living conditions and the environment .
Whether people can go to the outer space has nothing to do with them .
They simply pay their attention to the surroundings that need improvement to make better living conditions .
With the high cost of space technology development , they will think government focus on this is a kind of waste .
In their opinion , government should spend these money and resources on places which can benefit us .
So , it is not surprising that not all people were satisfied when Chinese Government proudly announced the success of the launching of the Shenzhou-5 spacesuit into the universe .
To civilians , they regard suffering people who live in starve and thirst , or the traffic system that influence people 's daily life .
In conclusion , judgments of technical innovation or development always differ because they are made by different groups of people .
All in all , the differences do really derive from different thinking perspectives .
Because people tend to think about things associated with their own experience and life , different opinions emerge .
Hundreds of years ago , people used to go out riding horses , illuminate the house by candles and start fire using firewood .
And we now go out by buses , light the house by electric lights , start fire using lightersand so on . Nowadays , people live in a very convenient world .
But few may notice that we are facing a serious problem behind all these inventions we are using .
To run all these things , we need energy .
And the shortage of petroleum is the most important issue that we must address .
Why is petroleum very important ?
Petroleum can be extracted and refined to produce fuels including petrol , paraffin , and diesel oil .
Without these extracted products from petroleum , cars can not run , planes can not fly , and ships can not be launched .
The world may not run any more .
What What is more , petroleum is a liquid mixture of hydrocarbons which is present in suitable rock strata and is not reproducible for now .
It is said that after 60 years , the world will run out of petroleum .
How are we going to solve this problem ?
There are two ways to solve this problem .
One way is to conserve and save petroleum .
Engineers have come up with some solutions to saving petroleum .
The greatest consumption of petroleum is in the transportation operation .
One of the engineer 's solutions is to mix alcohol and petrol together to provide energy .
This solution is now being tested and implemented .
In Wuhan , one of the biggest cities in China , all taxies are operating using this mixed fuel .
Another solution , which is almost the same concept , is the Hybrid-Electric Vehicle .
This kind of vehicles uses both electric power and fuel and is different from the previous version .
It combines the electric power system and fuel system together .
When the vehicle starts , it consumes electric power .
After the speed of the car reaches a certain range , it will switch to fuel power system .
When using fuel power to start the car , the fuel is not fully burned .
That is why we can smell strong petrol when the car starts .
The concept of power system is to let fuel fully used in order to save it .
However , conservation alone can not solve the problem .
The other way is to develop new energy resources to replace petroleum .
Hydrogen fuel cell , solar power and nuclear power are the three hottest topics that have interested engineers most .
Research on fuel cell on vehicles was started in early 1960s and it has continuously developed until now .
Most car makers have come out with their own hydrogen fuel cell-powered vehicles .
But hydrogen fuel cell vehicles are still in the testing and implementation phase .
There are some prototypes running on the road .
But for the finalized product , the cost should be reduced and the efficiency of the cell should be increased .
Solar and nuclear power are the more advanced technology .
Solar power is in the experimental phase .
The key point in increasing the efficiency of solar power is how to isolate the sunshine .
If this challenge can be solved , the potential of solar power is prodigious .
For nuclear power , it is using the power generated by nuclear fusion .
Nuclear fusion is the same way as the sun in generating its power .
Research on nuclear fusion has been going on for decades , but the progress is not very obvious .
In brief , the energy problem is one of our most serious problems now .
So we need to work on it step by step and follow the right rules to arrive at the best solution to this urgent problem .
We live in an era of great change , an increasingly global society as a result of rapid growth in information and communication technologies .
However , the above only holds through for those who are not stricken with poverty .
The needs of poor people , most of whom are based in developing countries , are endless .
The need for basic infrastructure ranks high on their priorities .
This is because basic infrastructure is the basis for any country to develop essential facilities like transport , housing and education to help the poor .
The engineering design process is an effective way through which the needs of these people could be met comprehensively .
According to Kandani ( 2005 ) , the very first step in any engineering design is to identify the need and to define the problem .
The word 'need ' refers to a man 's desire for a certain product or system .
This need is usually identified by the society and may vary from society to society .
Thus , needs which are considered a necessity to some might actually be a luxury to others .
For example , infrastructure is a real need for those living in the rural villages in Asia but not for the nomads in Africa , although both groups are affected by poverty .
The nomads would prefer to conserve the forests and wildlife so as to be able to carry on with their nomadic lifestyle .
This example clearly illustrates the importance of establishing the need accurately so that engineers would be able to work effectively towards solving the problem .
The second step of this engineering design process is to gather essential information .
In this step , engineers analyze the existing solutions and pick out the pros and cons .
Economic , environmental and safety factors are also analyzed .
Many developing countries have made big plans on establishing infrastructure in the rural areas in an attempt to bridge the gap in the standard of living between the urban towns and suburban villages .
However , these plans tend to get hit by delays after delays because of various reasons .
So it is vital for engineers to collect as much information as possible so as to not repeat the mistakes and go down the same slippery slope of their predecessors .
Once this is done , engineers can start to formulate multiple solutions .
This step urges engineers to temporarily throw the rulebook out of the window , open up their minds and explore many different ideas and possibilities .
Dr. Kandani suggests that a team with professionals from different fields be formed .
This team can work together and share their knowledge and expertise to come up with a few solutions .
The most logical step after coming up with a few solutions is to pick the best one .
This is actually the decision-making process , after studying the various solutions .
For instance , if a school is being built , based on the land available , few designs would have already been thought off .
Certain schools might be able to hold more students while not proving to be as stable as others that hold fewer students but are very much stronger .
So it is in this step that engineers make the decision of which design to adopt while weighing in all the factors to come up with a viable solution .
The final step in the engineering design process is to test and implement the solution .
This step is to essentially win the approval of the consumer as well as picking on possible flaws .
Ironically , this step is one that is followed by most . However , they do not bother to pick out flaws , thus in the end the consumer uses a flawed product .
Possible flaws should be identified so that the product can be improved on later .
In conclusion , I would like to recommend the engineering design process because it is very complete in its steps to provide a solution to those in need .
The establishment of basic infrastructure in developing countries through engineering design will give the poor an avenue to successfully escape from the vicious cycle of poverty .
The world today is experiencing global warming which is caused by the burning of fossil fuels and deforestation .
The solution to this problem is the harnessing of an alternative form of energy called kinetic energy in wind .
An example of a product created for this purpose is the wind turbine and it is created using the three main steps in design process to address the problem which are problem definition , information gathering and testing and implementing of solutions .
The first step in the design process is problem definition .
Following this procedure helps to generate more solutions to the problem addressed .
Tapping kinetic energy in wind is a good solution as wind is abundant due to the frequent changes in the atmospheric pressure .
This step announces to engineers that the Earth is in grave danger , thus giving them more motivation to think of a solution .
For example , by defining the problem as the fast decreasing quantity of fossil fuels , engineers gain insight into creating a product which can be used to tap kinetic energy in wind .
Referring to the earlier models of windmills like those built in Sistan , Iran , from the seventh century , which were used to grind rice grains , engineers used the same concept to create wind turbine which converts kinetic energy in wind into electrical energy .
The second step in the design process is the gathering of information .
The credibility of the problem needs to be addressed after it has been defined .
The important factor which determines the efficiency of the wind turbine is the general wind flow in the area where the wind turbine is built .
Since the wind turbine heavily depends on the wind to generate electricity , it is important to study the wind flow pattern before the wind turbine is built .
For this study , past weather forecasts and also the internet play vital roles in providing information needed to improve the efficiency of the wind turbine .
The overall gain in electrical energy needs to be calculated to decide whether the building of wind turbine is worth its value .
The last step in the design process is the testing and implementation of solutions .
The testing and implementation of solutions is closely related to the analysis of the design solution .
The main factor which contributes to the analysis is marketability .
For example , the Matilda built at Goland , Sweden produced a surprisingly high sixty-one gigawatts per hour of electricity in fifteen years which produced more energy than the other typical wind turbines .
However , the Matilda was demolished on June 6 , 2008 .
In conclusion , the main three steps in the design process help to create a guideline for the engineers to follow .
Problem definition requires knowledge of wind and thus making full use of it .
In terms of information gathering , the efficiency of the wind turbine is of paramount importance in determining whether it really solves the problem .
Lastly , the testing and implementation of solutions consists of marketability , ergonomics and safety which serve as a check on whether the product is deemed suitable to solve the problem .
Nowadays , engineering design products are everywhere .
Engineering systems play important roles in all fields , for example , entertainment , healthcare as well as education .
Although they are essential for all fields , engineering products and systems in healthcare and medical fields should be given the highest priority since health is the most important thing for all human beings .
Designing of medical products which can make all human beings healthier is obviously important .
Moreover , some medical products like " Fall Detection System " and " Posture monitoring system " can even help people save life in some ways .
On the other hand , people normally spend much more time for entertainment than healthcare .
As a result , there are mass products for entertainment because of high demand .
Instead , healthcare products should be widely available and used .
There are many healthcare products which are available in research organizations but not widely available in the current market .
For example , " Fall Detection System " can detect the fall of persons , especially elder people , and can send instant messages via sms to relatives so that they can get immediate help in critical situations .
As mentioned in the " Global action on aging " website , the number of senior citizens is rising taking care of them imperative .
It is also mentioned that since the number of elderly people is increasing , the burden of caring is also increasing for young people .
Hence , engineering should consider this situation and come out with solutions which will help the elderly and make youth work without worry .
Although there are R&Ds for healthcare products for monitoring and taking care of the elderly , these devices are not widely used in the market .
So , in order to address this situation , engineers should think about ways that can make the design process meet the needs of the market .
One example of a medical system is " Posture Monitoring System " which can monitor body posture all the time and continuously warning the user to maintain the best posture .
Recently in 2009 , Nanyang Polytechnic won a merit prize in the Tan Kah Kee Young Inventors ' Award competition in Singapore through its posture monitoring system . There are also research papers and prototypes of posture monitoring system by R&D from other countries but are not widely available in the current market .
One example of engineering products for the disabled which is mentioned in The Straits Times by Grace Chua is a chair that turns sound into vibrations , invented by NUS PhD student Suranga Nanayakkara This help deaf people experience music and even aid them in speech therapy .
In order to make engineering design products meet needs , first of all , a clear and unambiguous definition of the problem should be defined .
Problems should be widely and clearly defined by engineers , the elderly as well as adults so that more innovative products and ideas come out .
Moreover , it is also necessary to make sure that there is enough information to generate clear problem definitions that addresses the real need .
Once alternative solutions come out , engineers need to analyze and decide on the best suited solution to implement .Governments and organizations are also responsible in supporting the R&D process in order to gather information needed , generate multiple solutions , analyze solutions and test as well as implement solutions which are the necessary steps for the design process .
In conclusion , engineers should try to identify ideal situation in the market for their products , for example , the " Fall Detection System " which can take care of the elderly and the " Posture monitoring system " which can help people of all ages to maintain best posture with the help of government and organizations as well as consumers .
And the goal can also be achieved by developing suitable design engineering process for healthcare systems and products .
A human need is a necessity that humans need in order to survive .
One main necessity is food .
According to the World Food Program 's 2008 report , 25000 people are dying every day due to famine and related issues .
A large portion of the deaths comes from Third World Countries like Africa and India .
By using the Engineering Design Process introduced by Seyyed Khandani , a professor at Diablo Valley College , we can reduce famine .
Some factors that contribute to famine famine include political , technological and environmental issues .
The World Food Program ( WFP ) has been providing food and aid to areas affected by famine .
By using the engineering design process , the first step is to define the problem .
The definition of the problem is straight forward in the beginning : the people are starving , so they must be provided food .
However , for Malawi , the WFP and the World Bank figured out a solution and found out that it is better to donate cash to them ; based on their research , they found out that the country has food resources , but the poor can not afford them .
In the 1990s , the WFP introduced donation of cash and vouchers , and one of the pioneer countries that received this is Malawi .
Thus , providing cash did not only help to solve the famine , it also improved the financial situation of the farmers .
Furthermore , the WFP saved time and cost collecting food and delivering it to the affected areas .
In 1970s , the WFP provided food to India to temporarily solve famine .
During this period , they analyzed the situation to generate other solutions to permanently solve the famine .
According to the design process , the second step is to gather related information , then generate possible solutions .
The first possible solution was to provide genetically modified seeds and fertilizers to farmers , so that they would obtain higher yield .
Before this solution was implemented , they did a further study , and realized that the solution would not work as the farmers were using traditional farming methods which are not yield efficient .
Hence , the WFP provided machines and farming education to the farmers in the 1980s .
These aids improved the famine situation as it dropped by about 20 % in a WFP 1990s report ; On the other hand , these solutions not applicable to all lands in India as different areas have different types of lands .
For the dry lands , the WFP had to do further researchresearch on water irrigation methods .
One of the solutions was to construct a drainage system from the Indira Ghandi canal to irrigate the dry lands in the region .
Some events like drought , flood and earthquakes cause famine .
These types of events are unavoidable .
Nevertheless , events like deforestation and overgrazing have also affected fertile lands and caused yields to go down .
Governments spend millions and billions of dollars on entertainment and military expenditure yearly , but ththis large amount of money could have been put to good use in helping their own people .
India has increased military spending by 50 % in 2008 , bringing the amount to 40 billion dollars , although 35 % of its people are still affected by famine .
The famine caused by these situations is preventable .
The large amount of money could be invested in the agriculture sector , like using technology to plant seeds that will grow on dry land which will greatly solve the famine .
In conclusion , the WFP can do more research and analysis , like creating genetic modified seeds that can survive in dry or wet land , or an indoor farming center that will shelter the crops from natural disasters , to resolve the famine issue .
In addition , governments can try to allocate more budget to agriculture and research centers than to the entertainment sector , which is not right when people in their own country are suffering .
The last step in the design process is to test and implement the solution .
Taking a small step forward will reduce famine .
Poverty is unavoidable , but famine is preventable .
Thus , we should do more to help the people are suffering from famine .
Communication is an important part of human development . It allows ideas and information to be disseminated effectively .
One of the milestones in human communication is the invention of radio which changed the way we communicate in an obvious and physical way .
Radio allows the transmission of data over a distance literally through the air , which is not possible by the conventional cable lines .
Although the primary use of radio when it was first invented was for communication , alternative uses of radio have been developed and applied .
Two main driving factors that shaped the innovation of radio are economic and military demands , leading to the usage of radio beyond pure communication .
The value of radio being able to transmit and receive information over a distance wirelessly and cheaply has been the attention of scientists and inventors .
The first radio set was able to transmit only simple signals , but still it was valuable enough to be used by in maritime work .
Due to its simplicity , Morse code was adopted as the preferred language used on radio then .
By sending Morse code sailors were able to communicate with other sailors or to controlling towers on land when they were out in the open sea .
Hence , safety of sailors had improved as they would be able to signal for help during emergency .
An example would be the sending of by the Titanic to the nearest ship requesting assistance before it sank . It illustrated the usefulness of radio as a tool for communication in situations where line communication not possible .
Sending of Morse code via radio set was further popularised by telegraphy which transformed the use of radio into a service much like the postal service .
Telegraphy flourished as it was relatively reliable and much faster than postal service , encouraging more resources to be channelled into the development and research of radio technology .
Another value of radio was its ability to perform mass communication .
As the average cost of production declined steadily , the radio set was mass produced leading to the birth of radio broadcasting .
Broadcasting allows single directional flow of communication where important information can be disseminated to the mass quickly and effectively .
The other factors that have influenced the development of radio will be military demands .
The need for communication between joined military operations across forces and formations lead to the development of powerful signal set .
To prevent enemies from tapping on their communications or disrupting their signals , technology such as " anti-jamming " was developed by the military .
Besides improving on communication , military demands had also led to the invention of radar which uses radio wave in detecting distant objects and getting information such as their location and movement .
The technology of radar was soon transferred to civil usage such as by the commercial planes and ships due to its usefulness in navigation .
Another development of radio by military is guided weapon which arises from the need to raise accuracy of weapon in decreasing the chances of damaging and injuring civilian or allied forces .
In conclusion , radio is an important technology that is still being developed and improved continuously .
From its communication values to other discovered usages , economic and military factors have played a positive role in its overall development .
The invention and development of radio have bettered the society in numerous ways .
A need refers to what is required in order to do something or achieve some state of being .
'Human needs ' , for example , have been taken to describe requirements which must be satisfied if harm to an agent is to be avoided .
Overpopulation is one of the current human needs or challenges that should be given priority .
Size or density of the population affects overpopulation .
In the world where human populations are growing , we should focus on solving the problem of insufficient land to maintain life on earth .
Houses today are stronger , and some of them can withstand natural disaster .
For example in Japan , a country where earthquakes happen often , their engineers try to solve the problem of constructing buildings that can withstand earthquakes .
By using the Khandani Principle , engineers gather pertinent information about earthquakes and manage to implement a solution after several tests have been conducted , called Seismic retrofitting method , where Seismic retrofitting is the changing of an existing building to a structure that is more resistant to ground motion and soil failure due to earthquakes or seismic activity .
Engineers try to solve overpopulation by combining many houses into one building , thus building multi-unit housing , or also known as attached dwellings , has been initiated .
Apartments , barracks , tenements and terrace houses are good examples of multi-unit housing .
Engineers applied the Khandani principle that time ; they defined the problem and gathered enough information to make sure the buildings would not collapse .
For example , in Singapore , where land is very small , engineers built a lot of condominiums and apartments to solve the problem of insufficient houses and managed to save some of the land for other purposes .
However , in the future , the population will further increase , and building more multi-unit housing can not solve the problem effectively .
In my opinion , engineeengineers should focus on upgrading the buildings .
They should build multiple level basements for multi-unit housing and building since we do not really use a lot of the underground space .
Building multiple level basements may cause some other potential problems and engineers should try to solve these .
Engineers have to analyze every possible problem that may occur like water seepage , internal condensation , underground virus and bad acoustics when building more underground levels .
That is why in building more underground level , we need to use the Khandani principle ( 2005 ) that requires engineers to gather a lot of pertinent information from any sources available before implementing it .
In addition , engineers can also improve the stability of buildings so that more levels can be built above them .
The stability depends on the wideness of the base level , the material of the structure and the method of building the structure .
Engineers can increase the width of the base of the structure to support an extra level of building built on it .
Engineers can improve the structures by using stronger material like diamonds , gold , etc. and finding more suitable methods for building a structure .
Nobody can create a perfect solution with just one try .
Engineers need to test the solution before they start to use it .
Hidden problems can be found out by testing them under real conditions
( Khandani , 2005 ) .
In conclusion , with Khandani 's engineering design process , engineers can generate a perfect solution to solve overpopulation .
If we compare the house 10000 BC to the modern house today , the engineering design process is apparent .
If in the world we do not have such process , engineers may generate solutions that are ineffective or may cause harm to other life forms .
There are many human needs in the world and the engineering design process can help to meet those needs in a better way .
The issue of the depletion of earth 's natural resources has been raised repeatedly throughout recent times .
The earth 's natural resources are not well distributed across the globe , and hence some countries face the problem of the lack of certain natural resources .
Singapore , due to its small land size area , also faces the problem of the lack of natural resources .
In particular , the issue of the lack of water has been the headlines for many times .
In order for Singapore to be self-reliant on water , there is a need for Singapore to create portable water resources for its people .
Singapore had tried a number of ways in its bid to shift towards self-reliance on water .
This includes desalination and damping up of rivers to form water catchment areas .
However , these methods are still short of providing for the growing need of water by its people .
In recent years , the nation 's engineers have come up with a purification process which can purify waste water into portable water for use .
The product is called New water .
New water is treated waste water that has undergone stringent purification processes using advanced dual membrane and ultraviolet technology .
The product can be bottled for consumption , or be mixed with reservoir water and will then go through the usual water treatment to produce drinkable water .
Currently , New water is supplying Singapore with 15 % of its water demands .
There are plans to scale up the project to contribute 30 % of the water supply by 2010 .
The quality of the product is even assured by many international experts .
This is indeed a product of a system which is engineered to meet the human need for natural resources .
The design process of the system has undergone 5 design process stages as illustrated by Khandani in his Engineering Design process paper .
Firstly , the team of engineers working on the New water project identified the problem which is the lack of water resources for Singapore .
Singapore has been buying water from Malaysia , its neighbouring country , in order to supplement its own water supply .
However , the water agreements with Malaysia are expiring soon in 2011 & 2061 .
The agreements have been providing for 40 % of the country needs .
Therefore , the engineers identified the need for Singapore to shift towards self-sustainability in terms of water resources .
Secondly , they gathered pertinent information on the technologies and usage of water that is purified from waste water .
However , the first masterplan was shelved because of the great cost and unreliability of the process .
The cost incurred will offset the benefit that it may bring .
Hence , the team decided to wait for further technological advancement before building its first plant .
They eventually built its first plant after the technology of dual membrane purification matured and the production cost came down .
Thirdly , prior to the implementation of the New Water technology , there were also multiple solutions to the problem of lack of water resources in Singapore .
Solutions included desalination of sea water and damping up more rivers to increase the water catchment area .
The desalination of seawater would require large amount of fossil fuel to run which is another natural resource that Singapore does not have .
Furthermore , the desalination plants would also leave a larger carbon footprint .
Despite these , a desalination plant was still built because of the growing demand .
The damping up of rivers to form water catchment areas was in fact being implemented .
Marina barrage , the newest kid on the block , was formed by damping the marina channel to form a large water catchment area capable of meeting 10 % of Singapore 's need .
However , as Singapore has limited land , we could not go on forever creating water catchment areas from our land .
Therefore , New Water was decided as a solution needed to meet the need for water of the nation .
Finally , in May 2000 , the first New Water plant was completed .
Currently there are 4 New Water plant in Singapore with a fifth on its way .
Together , they will be able to meet 30 % of Singapore 's need .
Bottled New Water was also given out during National events , promoting its use in our daily life .
In conclusion , New Water has been an engineering design which was designed to meet the human need for water particularly in Singapore .
Throughout human history , there are a lot of successful products which have great effect on human life , like television , the cell and so on .
It is not only their high level technology that makes them so successful , but also the fact that they meet the needs of the people .
The electric car , which was first invented by General Motors Company ( GM ) , is such an interesting case .
The invention of electric cars is both a success and failure .
We can analyse it in both social and technological aspects .
The electric car is the product of social reasons .
As we know , an ordinary car 's fuel is gas which has been used since the first car was been produced .
While there exists a problem that the burning of gas gives off poisonous gases and a large amount of carbon dioxide which causes serious air pollution .
Furthermore , as it is mineral resource , the supply of gas is becoming less and less which directly leads to the rise of the price .
Because of the reasons stated above , people want to invent a kind of vehicle which can use cleaner and cheaper energy instead of gas .
That is why the electric cars came into being .
Another direct social reason is that in the early 1990s , the California and Arizona state governments had raised a policy which said at least 10 percent of the cars produced in the automobile companies should be environmental friendly , in other words , nonpolluting .
This promoted the research into electric cars .
These are the social reasons that did favor to electric car .
While , there are also some negative social sides .
Thanks to nearly a hundred years developing , the foundation of the gas industry was quite strong .
There were a lot of big gas companies tried a lot of methods to promote their products in order to push electric cars out of the market .
For example a gas company even asked for the President of America , Bush , to appear in their advertisement .
So you can imagine the difficult situation electric car 's companies met at that time .
The technological aspect is also very important .
At that time , the electric car was mainly made of aluminum which gave the car lighter weight and the shape was aerodynamically styled which could reduce the air resistance .
Both of the two features provided the electric car faster speed .
As it was powered by electricity , there was less noise .
Driving such a car could be quite an enjoyable experience .
While , technology was not fully developed at that time and the battery could only support the electric car to run at most 100 miles .
Furthermore , most of the gas stations did not offer the service to charge the electric car , so it is very inconvenient for people to travel long distance .
So , the electric cars could n't be widely used .
While recently the companies of electric cars have realized the importance of social and technological factors and they start to fight back .
In social aspect , the environment situation becomes more serious than twenty years ago .
The crude oil production rate reduces .
The price of gas goes higher and higher .
Again people become interested in electric cars and the companies also take these advantages to promote their products .
They also invited some superstars , like Tom Hanks , to help advertise the car .
In technological aspect , new kind of battery has be developed .
The travelling range has been expanded to 500 miles , nearly five times farther than before .
Many functions , like GPS and ABS , are also applied to the electric car .
The performance of electric car can be as better as normal car .
Through the case of electric cars , we can see that whether a product can be successful or not is decided by both the social and technological factors .
The change of these conditions directly influences the position of the product in the market .
So when engineer produce a new product , taking these two aspects of factors into consideration is important .
Global Warming
With the development of technology , people have more comfortable and beautiful clothes to wear , more enjoyable entertainment to participate in , more delicious food to eat and more convenient transportation .
However , one of the most important factors seems to be forgotten by human beings : the place we live - the earth .
Nowadays , as our Mother Earth r becomes hotter , human beings ' living condition is greatly threatened by global warming , the issue which is discussed fiercely among scientists .
As engineers we must also take this responsibility to protect our Earth Mother .
It is commonly known that global warming is caused by recent industrial activities years . To be precise it is due to the emission of green house gases ( GHG ) .
However , this idea is not acceptable for some people ; they consider the climate change as the natural phenomenon .
Actually , if we refer to the figure of " Temperature VS CO2 Emission " , we can straightaway reach a conclusion .
We can surprisingly find that the two curves match each other , in other words , it implies that the growth of temperature has some kind of tendency toward the growth of the emission of CO2 .
So , it is hard to say that there is no relationship between these two issues .
In recent years , due to much more frequent industrial activities , the curve of emission of CO2 consequently jumps to a very high point . So does the curve of temperature .
Nowadays , the rising temperature has received much more attention because of some sudden , striking events , for instance , the melting ice in Antarctica , the rising sea level .
As mentioned above , the rising temperature is due to higher emissions of green house gases , so the key to global warming will focus of this issue .
Firstly , we can make use of natural energy instead of fuel.As we all know , burning fuel will emit a lot of green house gases , including CO2 .
However , if we use natural energy , we can not only reduce the emission of green house gas , but also save our resources .
Let us look at the example from America , Denmark and Holland .
These countries are famous for using wind energy to produce electricity , and wind energy still has a lot of potential to be made use of in many other areas .
Water energy is also a kind of natural energy which can be exploited by human beings , such as in China .
Day by day , these kinds of natural energies will finally show their advantages and occupy an important place in our industrial development .
Secondly , we think that countries must set up a system to sacrifice their economy - to control the frequency of industrial activities .
The Kyoto Protocol signed in Japan is the best example .
In this protocol , the member countries have to reduce a certain amount of green house gas according to the amount of green house gas they produced and the most acceptable way is just reduce industrial activities .
Thirdly , increasing planting areas is also an efficient way to reach our goal , as plants absorb CO2 .
In conclusion , the threat of global warming has come . We engineers need to face it bravely and design products against the climate change .
We have only one Earth Earth . We must never lose her .
As our society progresses human beings get stuck in a dilemma of energy .
On one hand , the energy resources we use now , which are mainly fossil fuels , will be exhausted soon if we continue to consume at the current rate while the use of fossil fuels triggers a series of environmental problems .
On the other hand , the development of society calls for larger and larger amounts of energy , which makes us in desperate need of energy .
In order to develop our society without exhausting all the fossil fuels or sacrificing our environment , we have to find new energy resources to take the place of traditional fossil fuels .
In this case , solar energy stands out as our first choice .
Engineering design plays a significant role in the use of solar energy , especially in solar heating .
In the first stage , engineering design mainly contributes by clearly defining the problem and gathering pertinent information .
In fact , humans had begun to utilize solar energy to heat water as early as 3000 years ago .
However , the efficiency of solar energy was very slow .
The question of how to make an efficient and effective solar heating system is addressed by engineers .
In order to find the solution , engineers spend large amount of time to collect the relevant information , from which they can generate iinspiration , while drawing lessons from the previous work .
Though this preliminary stage appears simple , actually it not only takes a lot of time and calls for patience , but also is the crucial fundamental stage of the solution .
Then engineers come in at core step , that is , the generation of solutions .
First , engineers will decide to make a solar collector which can effectively collect solar energy from the surroundings
Because of the efficient heat conductibility of metal , engineers use a huge piece of metal which is painted black to collect the solar energy .
After that , they build the circulation equipment to make water flow below the metal so that the metal can transmit the heat to water and then people can use the heated water .
Using this solar heating system , engineers also designed certain products widely used in our daily life , such as the solar water heater .
That is not the end of engineering design .
What engineers will do next is test the system and make possible improvements .
Although solar energy has certain advantages compared to other kinds of energy , it has an inevitable disadvantage .
The solar energy is limited by various natural conditions , such as day and night , seasons , and places .
It is not stable enough , so people may not be able to use solar energy to heat water whenever they need .
To improve the solar heating system , engineers have added accessorial energy equipment to it such as an heater .
This improvement makes it possible for people to get hot water fast and conveniently even when there is not enough sunlight .
That is the end of the engineering design in the solar heating system .
To make an efficient and effective solar heating system , engineers carefully define the problem and collect important information about this issue . Then they generate all the possible solutions . Finally they test the solutions and make changes to improve the solution .
Besides the solar heating system , engineering design is also used in other fields .
With the help of engineering design , the wish to get out of the current energy dilemma will no longer be a dream .
The Human Need that should be Given Priority
Currently , people depend more and more on technology to improve their lives , which stimulates the development of science and technology in reverse .
However , among so many kinds of human needs , some of them should be given priority because of their urgency .
In my opinion , we should pay most attention to the development of clean energy such as solar energy .
The reason why we should focus on the research of solar energy is that the atmospheric pollution caused by the consumption of fossil fuels is severe , and there is enough solar energy to be used on Earth , , and the diffusion and adoption of solar energy product is satisfying .
In fact , the research of solar energy can be traced back to 1900 .
Although at that time they only focused on solar power plants .
Later , because of the decrease in petroleum and natural gas , scientists paid attention to solar energy again .
today , the process of solar energy research is still quite difficult .
Because of the severe pollution problem , we have to focus on the development of solar energy .
Nowadays , there are already various kinds of solar energy products in the market .
For example , people use solar energy converters to heat up water , which will save an amazing amount of energy acquired through other ways .
Besides , the usage of solar panels should become more and more important in the future .
It is said that if we can cover a place of 40,000 square miles with solar panels , the demand for electricity of the whole world will be satisfied .
Also , solar energy is inexhaustible and we can use it without worrying about polluting the atmosphere , which really solves the problem caused by the consumption of fossil fuels .
In some places of the world , people are accepting solar energy products such as solar energy converters as they think that they are fashionable and pollution-free .
For example , in rural and pastoral Tibet , solar energy converters have replaced conventional pollution-prone fuel .
But in cities such as GuangDong and ShangDong provinces in China , people are not so willing to install solar energy converters though the government has forced some buildings to install the converters to save energy and reduce carbon emission .
As for the solar energy panel , the situation is better .
Some residents in America covered their roofs with solar energy panels and those panels will provide 50 to 80 percent of power consumption in their houses .
Moreover , since the price of solar energy panel is decreasing recently , more and more consumers will think about the usage of solar energy panels .
In the 1980s and 1990s , the research of solar energy fell into the low tide because the price of petroleum fell and solar energy products were too expensive and there was no important breakthrough in the development of solar energy products .
However , since environmental pollution has become one of the most important topics in the world nowadays , we also should pay more attention to clean energy such as solar energy .
The usage of solar energy product will not only save large amounts of energy and solve the problem of energy crisis but also give us a clean world with little pollution .
With the development of the society , our demand for the various commodities keeps increasing .
We want to make our lives more comfortable and convenient .
However , without enough energy to manufacture the products , how can our desire be satisfied ?
Therefore , the current human need to find endless energy source is becoming more and more urgent , so it should be given priority .
To satisfy the current human need , we should use Roger 's Engineering design process to work out a solution .
This process contains five steps : define the problem , gather pertinent information , generate multiple solutions , analyze and select a solution , test and implement the solution .
As we know , most of the energy we are consuming is fossil energy such as coal and oil , which is limited .
If we just depend on fossil energy , how can we live on after hundreds of years years ?
Obviously , it wanted the oil in Iraq .
This war warns us that if we do not solve the energy problems , more wars may be declared in the future .
That is really disastrous and horrible .
However , there are many other kinds of energy sources on the earth such as nuclear power , water power and solar power .
Now the problem is how to use these power sources as substitutes for the fossil energy , which means how to convert these power into the energy that can be used by us such as electrical power .
To solve this problem , building electrical powerhouses may be the best choice .
The reason is that electrical power is clean , easily transported and easily stored .
Therefore , different places can share the energy source .
The problems brought by the unbalanced energy source distribution are solved .
Although making use of nuclear power , water power and solar power seems feasible , there are some reasons that make solar power the most appropriate .
Nuclear power can be very clean and can generate large quantities of electrical power .
Nevertheless , it can generate such huge power that it is very unsafe .
For instance , in 1986 , a nuclear powerhouse in Soviet Union exploded , which destroyed many buildings and claimed many people 's lives .
The strong radiation of the explosion even influenced all of the North Hemisphere .
What a tragedy it was !
We can not guarantee there will be no such kind of explosion any longer if we rely on nuclear power .
Using water power can just slightly reduce the pressure on the energy .
That is because the consuption of energy is so large nowadays that even though we make full use of water power , it is still far less than the consumption .
Undeniably , the technology of solar power conversion today is still not perfect .
Many improvements should be made to increase the conversion rate and lower the cost of the equipment so it can be utilised .
Nevertheless , this does not affect solar power to be the most ideal energy for the future .
Compared to other sources , solar power has three big advantages .
The first is that it is very clean .
Actually , the sunlight is electramagnetic waves .
During the convertion to electrical power , there is no emission of poisonous gas or water .
The second is that soalr power is very safe .
Unlike the nuclear power or water power , we never need to worry about the explosion of the powerhouse nor the collapse of dams caused by the strong water stream .
we already have built some solar powerhouses but we have never heard anything unfortunate happen .
Last but most importantly , solar power seems endless .
Only if the sun disappears will the soalr power be used up .
However , as we know , the life of the sun is more than billions of years .
Therefore , for the three advantages above , we can find it really meaningful to develop the solar power technology
Furthermore , during the development of solar power technology , we should pay more attention to solving the difficulty of the pervasion .
This means that we will apply the technolgy to every household so that most solar power shining on the earth can be converted .
Lowering the cost of the application is also very important , otherwise nobody will be willing to adopt this technology .
In conclusion , to maintain the sustainable development of our society , we should give priority to the current human need to develop more energy from various of human society .
Among the diverse energy sources , solar power has the brightest prospect for its non-pollution , safety and infinitude .
Hence , it is really worthwhile to develop solar power to make our society development sustainable .
Moreover , during the development of solar power technology , we should try to increase the efficiency of the power convertion and lower the price of the products .
From a luxurious entertaining appliance in the early stage of development , television has become an indispensable and ubiquitous thing within every household nowadays .
With millions of viewers around the world , it is used for various purposes not only by broadcasters and institutions but also businesses .
Television had to go through a very long way of development with reciprocal influences on society .
Advertising has become the most effective way of promoting sales of products .
The use of them is the most influential factor contributing to the development of television .
These costs are the financial backing of broadcasters ' programming .
Another way is to weave advertisements into shows .
This practice has begun in film .
For instance , a character may be driving a particular type of automobile , wearing a certain kind of clothes , or eating at a particular restaurant chain .
A brand or trademark is sometimes used .
I strongly believe that the benefits television brings to our society are undeniable .
Meyrowitz , a professor of communications at the department of Communication at the University of New Hampshire in Durham , deduced that television is the " secret-exposing machine " , and it opens up the " biggest secret of all , 'the secret of secrecy ' " to children .
It is even claimed that television has replaced printing to become the main way to access information .
Researchers suggest that children who were exposed to educational programs , positive models preferred reading books , were more artistic and got higher grades .
Nowadays virtually all the broadcasters have at least an educational program of their own .
That 's because of the high demand from parents , institutions and educationists .
However , television also has more negative influences on our society than positive ones .
A lot of findings showed that people tend to imitate the language and behavior which are inappropriate in society .
Children addicted to television are associated with obesity , passiveness , health problems and sometimes bad grades .
Inappropriate contents are deemed as another type of danger to the youth .
Violence , sex , drugs abuse , nonsense comics , etc. cause a lot of controversies over the right age of watching them ; and the youth are subject to parental television control , especially when it influences their self-esteem and body image .
With concerned parents , a child can greatly benefit from television programs programs , whereas the child may encounter inappropriate contents if the parents let him or her freely use television .
Adults who spend too much time on TV viewing seem to be dissatisfied people because they try to look for happiness in those programs after a hard struggling day .
However it is usually short lived happiness .
In addition to this , broadcasters often have some shows and programs addressing women in the new century .
Television played a vital role in the feminist movement .
It is disputable whether television has been changing the norms of society .
In conclusion , television has obviously contributed a lot to determine and shape our society , owing to the strong links between its development history and the human 's .
That is the reason why we always have to improve it , to nurture it .
We have to balance the pros and cons as well as the relationship of television to our present and future generations .
In the 21st century when people around the world get more opportunities to interact with each other , the ability to speak and understand other languages has become more and more important .
Most people choose to hire a translator .
However , well-trained ones are hard to find and they are not always available at times when you need them immediately .
Moreover , some people feel that their privacy is not safeguarded with a translator involved .
Thus , we have initiated this product called " N-in-1 Auto- translator " which can help solve all those problems mentioned above .
In the following paragraphs , the design process of our product will be illustrated to show how we fulfill people 's need to communicate with others speaking different languages .
First of all , in the engineering process of this Auto-translator , we will keep modifying and upgrading until it fully serves its purposes .
According to Khandani , in the final testing and implementing process , we will make sure that it can translate exactly and clearly right on the spot .
For the after-sale services , we would establish an official website for the customers to acquire necessary information and post their feedback
For instance , we will upload different language packages online so that customers speaking specific languages can install the software in their Auto-translators and make use of them .
Though we can not have all languages , we have the ones that the majority is requesting .
We will keep upgrading and modifying our software until our customers are satisfied .
Having talked about the modifications , we have made efforts to minimize the cost , change the charging method and improve the portability .
As a brand new product which people do not have much faith in , it has been made reasonably affordable .
As batteries are not environmental friendly , we have made use of the DC chargers instead .
This is very convenient for the customers and they do not have to change batteries all the time as the lifetime of the chargeable battery is purposely made longer .
In addition , we have made the device more portable by minimizing the size and weight .
For example , our device has many components consisting of a scanner , speaker , printer and recorder .
This allows our product to be multi-functional in contrast with an electronic dictionary which has many limitations .
Customers do not have to bring them all .
Instead , they can just selectively plug-in any component they need in order to make it much more portable .
From this example , we can see that we engineers always think from the customer 's point of view and try our best to fulfill their needs .
Moreover , we should also take care of the interests of small groups of people .
Our target customers are businessman , travelers , international school teachers and students and other people who have needs to understand other languages .
However , after reviewing all the feedback feedback on our official website , we found that the blind also need it .
After numerous research , we found that they recognize things by touching , smelling and hearing .
Thus we made modifications on our device such as the Braille-mini- printer .
This mini-printer can print in Braille so that they can understand by touching the paper after they scan the documents in other languages .
We can see that just a little change can benefit a large number of people .
To sum-up all the points mentioned above , we would conclude that engineering design processes can meet people 's needs by qualified products and services , continuous modifications and the attitude to think for customers .
There is an old saying which goes " The customerr is god .
" We totally agree with it .
We engineers must always keep ourselves upgraded and think for the customers all the time so that we can make upgrades and modifications to meet their needs .
While one is looking for A , he may discover B accidentally along the way , and this process is called the serendipitous discovery .
It is very different from the normal technologies we have , which resulted from developments aiming to solve specific questions .
They are also different from each other in terms of level of success and how well they solve a problem .
Nonetheless , despite so many differences , they are also similar in that they are both important and can only be discovered by prepared minds .
One obvious difference is how each technology is discovered .
normal technology is found and developed by following certain procedures .
For example , a problem or need is always first identified , and then people start to brainstorm and think of solutions to the problem .
They always have a clear purpose or goal in mind which leads them in a certain direction to resolve the puzzle .
However , for technologies found through serendipitous discovery , they show complete randomness .
They are absolutely unexpected .
While one is solving some physics question , he may derive a solution for a biological problem in an approach which no one has thought of before .
There is nothing like a plan or preparation for this .
Hence , the two technologies differ from each other greatly in the ways they are discovered .
Another difference between them may be the desirability .
Most of the time , serendipitously discovered technologies gain more recognition and greater success in terms of economic or scientific aspects , compared to the average normally developed technologies .
This is just like what Lawren Block said , the thing one found while looking for something else , usually suited his needs more .
The reason behind this is that serendipitous discoveries cater to solve the problems in more ingenious ways , as they may be the result of some unknown happenings , and they are produced by following some rules of nature we have yet to gain an understanding of , which are mysterious but also powerful .
A simple example would be the success of Dichloro- diphenyl-trichloroethane ( DDT ) , compared to other insecticides .
Nonetheless , apart from the differences , there are also similarities between these two kinds of technologies .
One major similarity they share is that both can only be discovered by prepared personnel .
As Louis Pasteur said , in the arena of observation , opportunities favor only the prepared minds .
This is indeed very true .
When people see some new products or discoveries , especially those close to our daily lives , sometimes they can not help but ask themselves why , when they experienced some similar things , they failed to turn them into innovations or products .
In our daily lives , it is true that we may experience this or that kind of things , but it is only those careful ones , prepared ones , those who always pay more attention to tiny things happening around them and treat these things seriously , come up with ingenious discoveries .
One needs to be prepared to identify a potential serendipitous discovery , as well as to develop a normal technology , so that one does not miss out any important details and gains success in the end .
All in all , technologies discovered through conventional means and those discovered by chance are quite different in the aspects of how they are discovered and the general impacts they have .
However , they also share some similarities like they can only be found by prepared individuals .
In the end , though they may be so different , it is quite obvious that they are equally important and necessary for our lives and even the progress of mankind .
Thus , we should always be on the lookout , and think more about things around us . Always be prepared .
Engineering is a field of specialization where new products are being invented or where old products are being upgraded or modified .
However , it is always a tough path to undertake as there will be problems arising during the design process .
The main processes during an innovation 's design involves identifying the problem , researching new methodology , developing the new or upgraded product and finally promoting sales of the product .
In fact , problems often occur during the two most critical parts of the designing process which lie during the research and development sections .
In Singapore , innovations and inventions due to engineering are still currently in the early stages .
The main involvement in the designing process for innovations includes modifying and upgrading existing products .
The improvement of the reverse osmosis process that created NeWater and the development of the 'eco-friendly ' vehicles are examples
These ideas and products came from other countries and Singapore merely took the products and took it to suit her own needs .
For instance , the weapons and equipment used by the Singapore Armed Forces ( SAF ) originated from countries like Germany and the United Kingdom .
The possible reasons that Singapore lacked the initiative to come out with a brand new product could lie in the lack of resources support and the general mindset of Singaporeans .
Firstly , the lack of resources support could significantly hamper the research and development process in engineering design for innovations .
Singapore is a small country in terms of resources and technology capabilities .
As a result , during the research stage of an engineering process , a lack of materials and funding could cause the designing process to fall through .
Funding and materials are crucial during an engineering design process as trials and equipment are required to gauge and judge the progress and outcome of a development .
Often , some engineering processes lie within a thin line away from some juristic rules .
These rules and regulations are especially strict in Singapore . As a result engineering is often restricted by these limitations which could hamper some bold yet useful innovation ideas .
For example , although Singapore is ranked among the first few countries in development of products in Asia , nevertheless engineers in Singapore have to regularly keep track of the new technologies by discussing with their counterpart from leading countries like Japan and the United States of America .
The lack of knowledge prevents engineers in Singapore from coming out with brand new ideas for innovations .
The other problem faced by Singapore is the lack of courage for Singapore engineers to come out with a creative and new innovation .
This problem can be attributed to the upbringing of Singaporean kids .
Children in Singapore are brought up in a very 'safe ' and stable environment where everything is provided for .
Instructions on every single detail are given . As a result , Singapore kids are deprived of the chance to think independently .
As they are brought up in such an environment , they naturally will develop a mindset that it is better to follow rules as it will be much more stable and fool-proof rather than trying to think out of the box and create or do something bold .
This is an underlying problem as these kids who will grow up to be engineers will not be able to come up with exciting innovations .
In conclusion , these two main problems basically hamper the research and development areas of engineering design process , Singapore engineers can only at the moment upgrade or modifies existing innovations .
Thus they are the reasons why local Singaporean engineers have failed to come out with a stunning innovation yet .
A serendipity find is defined as accidently and unexpectedly discovering something fortunate .
One technology that was discovered by serendipity is the sound-powered telephone .
Unlike a serendipity invention , a product or system that is created or developed , not coming from accidents , but through a series of engineering design processes is a research invention , and a technology developed via research is the mobile phone .
For these two technologies , there are several similarities and differences in the aspects of their usages , the power supplies they need , the communication efficiencies and health concerns .
Firstly , compare the usages for both the sound-powered telephone and the mobile phone.They are similar in that both are used for communication .
However , the ways they are used are different .
The sound-powered telephone is now widely used in naval vessels , and also in emergency communication systems for high-rise buildings , airports and ski lifts etc , whereas a mobile phone is designed for calling contacts .
Unlike a sound-powered telephone , extra functions are included in a mobile phone , such as games , music and a camera for use .
Secondly , the sound-powered telephone differs from the mobile phone in power supplies needed
The speaker 's voice , through its microphone unit , supplies necessary power for operating the sound-powered telephone .
Batteries or power connections are not required.The circuit is always live , thus a user simply begins speaking rather than dialing another station .
On the contrary , the mobile phone can not operate without the use of an external power . Normally a battery must be included and charged , so that the mobile phone can be switched on .
Thirdly , in terms of communication efficiency after the connection is established , the mobile phone provides better efficiency than the sound- powered telephone .
on a sound powered phone system , only one person can speak at a time or the signal will become hopelessly garbled . However , a mobile phone 's system allows both sides to input analog signals into the circuits at the same time .
Lastly , for engineers , designing a safe product is a big concern .
The mobile phone emits electromagnetic radiation , which may harm one 's health if used for long period of time .
However , the sound-powered telephone does not pose any health risks to human beings due to its relatively simpler circuits compared to the mobile phone .
In conclusion , both technologies are electronic devices . Their main function is the same , that is , to provide people a way to communicate .
Although the sound-powered telephone is less efficient than the mobile phone after the connection is established , it functions as an emergency communication device more often than the mobile phone because it does not require an power source in order to operate it .
The mobile phone has more sophisticated structures and theories than the sound-powered telephone . Hence , the mobile phone emits harmful radiation to users .
In any case , both technologies have greatly improved the convenience in communication in our life .
For the past few centuries , engineers and scientists have been working together , resulting in numerous great discoveries and inventions benefiting mankind in various aspects .
However , as science and technology evolved , they also brought numerous problems .
In this essay , I will be focusing on the environmental issues that were brought about by the improvement of science and technology and how engineering design processes can meet the need
From the late 19th to early 20th century , there was an outburst of great discoveries and inventions , coupled with worldwide expansion of industrialisation , creating many machines to aid human needs , and wants .
The sudden out-break of these events caused several negative impacts on Earth .
One of the most prominent examples is global warming , a result of the existence of greenhouse gases .
Global warming causes an increase in the average temperature of Earth , which results in major problems such as melting ice caps at both poles , rising sea levels , heat waves and depleting ozone layer .
During the golden period of invention of machinery and industrialisation , machines running primarily on fossil fuels emitted large quantity of greenhouse gases during incomplete combustion of fuels .
These harmful gases have resulted in the vast pollution of the globe .
And , the situation continues to worsen .
The Kyoto Protocol , a treaty signed among the countries to lower the emission of greenhouse gases to the environment which started in the 1990 's , was quite a success .
However , even though there was a decrease in the percentage of the greenhouse gases emitted worldwide , the greenhouse gases still exist in our atmosphere , depleting our ozone layer .
Engineers , on the other hand , invented a product called the catalytic converter that helps to convert the harmful gases to gases that are less harmful to our environment before releasing them out to the environment .
This was a better solution to the problem .
Currently , as engineers , we should work on an advanced model of the catalytic converter , with a higher efficiency and better compatibility with different models of engines which may emit harmful gases .
Even though the process might be time-consuming and expensive , the improved version of the converter will be very useful to us .
Alternatively , we can look into the possible problems that might arise before the release of the product .
During the brainstorming stage , engineers should look at the product from various angles ; the possibilities of doing harm to the environment while creating and testing the product product ; the ways to dispose of any toxic or radioactive wastes , and the possibility of exploitation of product on immorality purposes .
In conclusion , engineering design processes can meet the need of solving global warming by the improvement of catalytic converters and execution of cautious planning before any other procedures .
Prevention is always better than cure .
Safety is a primary need for all inventions even to this date .
However , safety has been overlooked or neglected on many occasions and this has harm to its users .
One example would be the injuries caused by can openers .
In order to overcome such injuries and keep users out of harm 's way , we need a logical design process to design a can opener of high safety standards .
According to Khandani ( 2005 ) 'Engineering design process ' is a sequence of steps to design a product in a systematic order .
The five main steps are to define the problem , gather information , generate multiple solutions and analyze and select a solution and finally it .
To help achieve the objective of designing a safe can opener , engineering design process can be used to analyse the problems of existing can openers , and discover areas of improvement .
Existing can openers include lever type can opener , rotating wheel can opener and butterfly opener .
The first stage of designing a product would be to define the problem using three key points .
They are to identify and establish a need , develop a problem statement and establish criteria for success .
The first two points have already been looked into by previous manufacturers .
However , the criteria of success has to be relooked at for a safer product .
A new can opener has to be safe , light , environmentally friendly and cheap .
After defining the problem , the data relevant to the need , safety in this case , has to be gathered .
statistical research to find out how many are affected , on which part of the user the injuries occur , when do injuries normally occur and who are the affected has to be done to get a better idea of the situation .
Besides that , material research has to be done to understand to what extent can the material harm the user and what alternative materials are .
For example , the lever type can opener is made of cast iron , which makes it bulky for users who end up injuring themselves in an effort to use it .
In addition , interviews on affected users can be done to understand how the injuries occur .
Manufacturers should also be interviewed to explain their reasons for overlooking the safety aspect if they had done it knowingly .
Once all the information has been collated , the third stage of design process would be to generate multiple solutions .
Multiple solutions can be from the users as well as manufacturers .
In design process , existing ideas are torn apart to find the fault in them .
For instance , in the lever type , its unprotected knife-like sickle is too dangerous for domestic use .
As for the rotating wheel , the necessity to pierce the can first is a nuisance for users and the butterfly opener produces sharp edges on the lid .
Thereafter , new ideas , tools and methods are combined to propose a new solution .
Such synthesis will seek to improve the weakness of previous solutions .
The evaluation of proposed designs would be an overlap of the suggestion given by users and manufacturers and the information gathered .
Four main analyses are used for designing a safer product .
They are functional analysis , ergonomics , safety analysis and market analysis .
Being safe is the primary need of the product .
However , the functionality will determine the ultimate success of the product .
The three existing products have satisfactory function ability .
The first electric can opener was able to remove lids from more than twenty cans per minute without any risk of injury but was not put into practice because it was not handy .
Klassen Enterprises of Centreville introduced a wall-mounted electric model which was safe .
Unfortunately , this complex design was unpopular among users .
In functional analysis , the practicality of the product is put to test .
Next would be the ergonomic analysis of the product .
A safety device has to be able to fit the hands of the people utilising it to provide comfort and confidence in handling it .
Design process looks at the geometric properties of the human body to determine the dimensions of the safety product .
A good design will be able to fit ninety percent of its users .
Currently the lever type is mainly suitable for adults due to its large handle and considerably high mass .
As for the wheel type , the pliers-type handle allows a firm grip of the can edge and suits most users .
The butterfly opener is easy to grip but its metal frame makes it uncomfortable for the user .
The third analysis , safety analysis , would determine which product has a leading edge over the other products .
The human need of safety is still not addressed in many can openers .
The lever type opener has a sharp edge which exposes the user to potential hazard and the other two openers leave sharp edges on the lids of cans which are threat to safety .
The new product has be devoid of sharp parts as well as be able to not leave any sharp edges on the lid .
In design process , engineers have to keep records of calculations and methods used and foresee other ways people could use the product .
As a result , safety considerations must be included in the manual of the new product .
Description of inherent dangers should also be displayed on warning labels .
To make profits , market analysis has to be done .
Just like the existing openers , future products have to be evaluated against criteria such as sales features , cost of manufacturing and advertising .
Failure to do this will results in unpopular products like the wall-mounted electric model mentioned earlier .
After analysing alternative solutions , the most suitable product has to be chosen .
Design process uses the decision process to select the best solution .
Firstly , the desirable attributes such as safety , function ability , marketability and ergonomics are ranked in order of importance .
Followed by this , a value factor is assigned to each attribute .
For instance , in this case , the success of safety is twice as important as the success of market analysis , a value factor of 20 will be given to safety and 10 to market analysis .
Value factors are assigned on a of 0 to 100 relative to the importance of other criteria for success .
Next , a rating factor is assigned to each new solution .
This will indicate how well the proposed product satisfies the particular criteria .
For example , if a product satisfies the criteria of safety to the maximum it will be given a rating factor of ten and if it satisfies the criteria of marketing by only half , it is given a rating of 5 .
Substantial knowledge of the product and its users will allow engineers to make an accurate evaluation which involves rating safety factors and value factors .
The value factors are multiplied to the rating factors and summed up for each product .
The proposed solution with the highest score will be chosen as the best design .
The final stage in design process is to implement the solution .
This would include prototyping , concurrent engineering , documenting and applying for patents .
These procedures would have already been done by existing products .
The new product for opening cans will have these four processes before it is introduced to the market .
One such product currently in the market which is safe for opening cans , handy , environmentally friendly and ergonomically stable is the one touch can opener .
It leaves the lid of opened cans without any sharp edges .
It is battery operated and uses a magnet to attach on to the lid while cutting the edges away using an ultra fine blade .
Unfortunately , it is not very affordable and hence not marketable enough .
Future inventions would have to give more importance to the marketing aspect of it .
It can be seen that the design process is tedious , time consuming and sometimes even never ending .
No effort will be futile if executed in the right direction .
Design process suggests a safe path for engineers to take to achieve success .
The never ending need for safety to humans is an obligation for engineers of tomorrow to fulfill .
Increased confidence in consumers is seen whenever safety is enhanced for products .
In the case of can openers , making opening of cans hazard free will be able to draw a large consumer audience .
Constantly placing an emphasis on safety will serve as a reminder for all other manufacturers to meet and will in turn benefit mankind as whole .
When you go shopping , do you usually see the same kind of products which almost have the same functions or even same appearances ?
According to the research done by U.S. Customs and Border Protection , in 2004 the total amount of illegally copied products is 1.39 million and 63 % of products come from China .
In China now , a huge amount of products do not contain any innovative elements and the manufacturing companies just copy the existing patterns .
As these companies manufacture products which copy the basic design from others , the product design process is no longer present for innovations .
There must be some reason .
Obviously , copying ideas and reducing manufacturing cost should hamper the innovative design process .
Some companies in China usually copy basic ideas from others and make use of them for themselves .
In recent years , lots of small companies have appeared in southern China .
These companies found their own brands and manufacture all kinds of products such as IT products .
However , all these companies do not do innovation design .
They imitate world -famous companies .
For example , some cellphone companies in GuangDong province imitate famous mobile phone such as Nokia and Apple .
In 2008 , the production of this kind of phones was more than 80 million in China .
These phones have the exact appearance designs as big names . Even Even if you look at them for the first time you can not identify which are produced by NOKIA and which are copied .
The negative consequences are obvious .
Because of copying basic ideas from others , the first stage for design is no longer for innovations .
Secondly , reducing manufacturing cost hampers the innovative design process as well .
In order to reduce input and gain more benefits , some companies pay very little attention to design process because that design process always costs lots of money .
Therefore , they have to simplify their products or just copy them from others .
Even though there is an innovation idea , designers will not consider it .
As a result , design process just follows the previous pattern and no innovation is created during the design process stage .
As mentioned above , innovation design process will be hampered if companies copy ideas from others to reduce manufacturing costs
In some sense , innovation helps humankind to move forward .
It is so important that innovation design should be present anywhere .
In today 's global competitive market , a product 's functionality is not the only thing customers are looking out for .
Products must not only serve their functions but must look good on the surface .
No doubt there are products with solely excellent functions out on the market .
These products are appreciated by few .
It does not take long for one to realize that products must have their own unique design in order to be relevant in the market .
Engineering Design Process , written by Professor Seyyed Khandani from Diablo Valley College in Pleasant Hill , California , aims to guide engineers and aspiring designers to design their product through a sequential thinking process .
Engineering Process Design brings the reader across different aspects of engineering design , such as the marketability of the product and the testing of products .
Designing itself is a creative process and in some cases , readers may find certain aspects of Engineering Design Process are not applicable at all .
In Singapore , the small elastic market and the lack of facilities and flexibility for product testing may hamper the design process .
According to Khandani ( 2005 ) , the purpose of designing is to generate profits .
Afterall , who will want to waste their efforts on something that does not reap benefits ?
This is one of the reasons why engineering design process is not all that easy in Singapore .
With only a population of 4 million , Singapore has a relatively small market .
The remuneration is simply not enough to lure players into the market to produce and design their products .
Engineers will often find themselves limited by the consumers ' needs .
In addition , engineering design process in Singapore is often faced with Singaporeans ' preferences for foreign goods .
Firstly , foreign goods are often established brands which appeal to the local market .
Secondly , certain goods , especially technological products , are much cheaper when imported from overseas .
In recent years , with the explosive number of online shops emerging and the increasing popularity of B2C ( business-to-consumer ) websites such as Amazon.com , it is not difficult to purchase foreign goods .
This has resulted in the low demand for locally designed products and often discourages engineers to continue in their innovations .
Before the product is implemented , it is important that the product is tested first .
Singapore , a small country has only 650 square kilometers of land area .
Much of the landscape is covered by skyscrapers and public housings .
The lacks of land area to build suitable facilities to test products is an obstruction to engineers .
Since 2004 , the National University of Singapore 's ( NUS ) , School of Engineering 's Formula Society of Automotive Engineers ( FSAE ) has been building racing cars and representing Singapore in competitions against other universities from other countries .
Associate Professor Seah Kar Heng commented that one of the difficulties faced by the team is the lack of a suitable venue to test drive the cars .
Beside the lack of facilities , engineers are constrained by the strict regulations imposed by the Governement .
The team from FSAE could only test- drive their cars within NUS ' compounds and in the United States where competitions were held .
Currently , there are only laws governing the use of conventional cars on public roads .
The team from FASE will have to seek approval from different agencies which is often very time-consuming .
In conclusion , Engineering Process Design is a comprehensive guide for engineers who have no idea about how to go about designing a new product .
However , in Singapore , engineers will find that they will meet some problems that may hamper the design process .
Due to the small market in Singapore and Singaporeans ' preference for foreign goods , many may give up their innovations eventually .
For those who successfully designed their products , they are met with another problem-- the lack of facilities to test their products and the inflexibility of the Government 's regulations .
Engineering design process is a tedious one and by analysing the problems that hamper it , one may be able to make the process a smoother one .
Engineers Design in Renewable Resources
Our world is experiencing amazing changes every day .
It can not be denied that some people in certain areas are still struggling around the poverty line . However , , most of the citizens of the world believe that our living conditions are becoming better and better .
But behind the prosperity , we are facing some great challenges , or , put another way , some urgent problems which may affect the rise and fall of mankind .
Among those problems , the limitation of resources is a source of concern for our society .
Engineers are playing an important role in finding and using renewable resources such as wind power and solar power to satisfy the increasing demand of resources .
Firstly , scientists and engineers have been focusing on using wind and solar power for decades .
Many solutions have been tested and implemented .
The most well known examples may be the solar water heater and wind powered electrical generator .
These two inventions can not only meet our daily needs , but also protect the environment and save the existing resources like coal and petroleum .
To put it more specifically , the solar water heater can take the place of other kinds of water heaters run on coal gas .
So , besides the reasons above , it is also very cheap to use these renewable resources so users can get a lot of economical benefits from that .
Secondly , some of the technologies are still being tested .
Engineers are trying to generate multiple solutions to some problems .
And these problems are mainly caused by restriction and immature technology of wind and solar power .
For example , scientists and engineers have found that the wind speed and hours of sunshine are not steady so that the generating energy is also not very steady .
These two resources are restricted by geographical position and climate .
Besides , the efficiency of converting wind power is very low .
So the focus of engineers is to design and test new technology .
For instance , the car is one of the most important transportation means in the world . However , , new research has proven that the existing extra petroleum can only be used for another eighty to ninety years .
Engineers are trying to solve the problem of what we will use after the petroleum runs out .
Thus a new kind of solar-powered car has been invented .
But even engineers have reached limited success . The solar-powered car they can produce is still far from the standard of civil transport
So engineers still have a long way to go to test and find solutions to make better use of wind and solar energy .
Last but not least , engineers are trying hard to make their dream a reality .
They have plans to build a power house in space because it is easier to get more solar energy and convert it into electricity more efficiently .
They are still gathering the pertinent information .
With their great efforts , I will not be surprised to see a totally different world in the future .
So to sum up , we have a bright future for renewable resources and the problem of limited resources will worry people no more .
" The world is coming to an end in the 2100s ( 22th century ) !
" Is this statement a false prophesy or a reality that has yet to come true ?
Natural resources around the world are being depleted at an alarming rate which has led to numerous debates and interventions by environmentalists , in a bid to reduce the amount of resources extracted and employed by mankind .
However , not all readily available natural resources can be used directly from their raw form .
One such example is the purification of water to make it potable .
Water is an essential part of human life .
Everyone needs it for survival and also for many other applications such as industrial usage .
Even though water is readily available , however , the process of purification to make it portable is tedious , technologically intensive and most importantly , expensive .
According to statistical figures from a United Nations Organisation ( UNO ) publication , the global population consumes approximately 3000 cubic metres of water daily .
As a result , there is an increasing need for newer , greener and more cost-effective purification methods so as to provide massive amounts of clean and affordable drinking water for all parts of the world , especially in less-developed countries .
Hence , the ever-increasing need for cheap portable water should be given high priority in global research and development initiatives .
The following case study illustrates the importance of modern technology and engineering design in water purification process , especially in countries that do not have self-sustainable water supplies .
Engineering design and modern technology assists these countries by first identifying the specific problem and in the process of doing so , possible solutions will be generated .
The final stage of the design process involves the testing and implementation of a particular chosen solution .
For example in Singapore , the government recognised that she has to be more self-reliant and self-dependent on her water supplies so as to mitigate any difficulties faced in times of contingency and emergency .
In addition , being a small 'island ' country surrounded by close neighbours , the idea of desalination of sea-water to meet her water demands is not a viable long-term option .
As a result , NEWater , a sewage treatment plant , was set up a few years back to look into the possibility of converting 'used ' or sewage water into clean drinking water via reverse osmosis technology .
As such , large emphasis and investments have been invested into this initiative since then .
Through the application of the engineering design framework and modern technology , purifying sewage water seems to be highly viable and successful .
According to statistics from the Public Utilities Board ( PUB ) , NEWater will meet 30 % of Singapore 's current water needs by 2010 .
This example shows that through the proper implementation of engineering design framework and application of modern technology , the current human need for securing clean and cheap drinking water can be achieved with a high degree of success .
In conclusion , engineering design process and modern technology will no doubt aid in solving and realising various human needs such as that of water purification .
However , prudent and appropriate usage of the world 's natural resources still has to be practised religiously and conscientiously as engineering solutions do not guarantee complete success in any application .
As a result , both human and technology have an important role to play in the quest of satisfying human needs .
According to E.M. Rogers , writer of " Diffusion of innovations " , in general , there are six stages of innovation-development process .
They are awareness of the needs or problems , basic and applied research , development , commercialization , diffusion and adoption and finally consequences ( Rogers 2003 ) .
During the process , there are many factors that would affect the outcome of the development project .
Some of them are determined by the technology perspective or social factors , whereas some include government involvement .
One important technology that Rogers mentioned is the innovation of the refrigerator in 1930 for electric and gas refrigerators .
When people did a comparison on both types , the latter has a better advantage over the first . and they were expecting the gas refrigerator .
But it did not capture the consumer market .
The main reason for this was because of the investment , consideration and decision made by the corporations involved in this project .
They believed that they would make more profits from electric refrigerators and thus marketed it to the public .
As a result , it turned out that technology in electric refrigerator was available to the consumer instead of the consumer 's choice .
Another example of a social problem leading to government and scientist involvement is the safety issue with automobiles in the United States .
In 1960 , the annual fatality due to vehicles reached 50,000 and drew the government 's attention to the safety ie on the transport system .
A survey was conducted between the specialized researchers ' and public 's view of the traffic safety problem .
It was found that the research team did n't agree with the public view and claimed that it was an individual-blame perspective .
As a conclusion from conducting researchers , professors , government officials and insurance company executives , the research on safety measure became due to system-blame perspective and thus engineers redesigned auto vehicles and restructured highways .
As a consequence of both the above cases , , the technology did not become the way the consumers expected and the solution for solving social problems was redirected .
It did not follow the stages mentioned above for the successful completion of the process .
Most of them varied along the process due to several factors and thus led to a different type of innovation .
From my point of view , no matter what the sequence of innovation-development process , as long as there is a new invention , it was invented to benefit all mankind .
Reference : Rogers , E. M. ( 2003 ) .
The generation of innovations .
In Diffusion of innovations ( pp.136-157 ) .
New York : Free Press .
Technology has improved so rapidly in the past century that men have tread into outer space and harvested enormous amounts of energy from minute quantities of nuclear material . Yet there still exists the problem of food shortage .
This problem is very serious in many Third World countries in Africa as well as Asia .
For example , in countries like Sierra Leone and East Timor , one person and one child die every five seconds due to starvation .
With such worrying statistics , food shortage is definitely a problem which should be addressed as soon as possible .
If the world is not growing enough food to support its population , the process can be speeded up through the development of Food Science and Bio- Engineering .
Certain types of food such as rice and fruits can be genetically modified to grow faster and increase food yield .
Animals such as cows and chickens can also be genetically altered to grow faster and produce more milk or eggs respectively .
By designing and engineering certain genes of these plants and animals , food production can be increased to meet the increasing needs of poor countries .
However , as food has to be consumed by the human body , there are very strict restrictions and quality control on food or animals that undergo genetic modification .
As such , with many factors to consider , the process of modifying the genes is not easy .
Engineering design processes are able to meet the challenges of this job .
A part of engineering design processes is to constantly generate new ideas to improve on current ones .
Like what Seyyed Khandani said , " You start with existing solutions to the problem and then tear them apart-find out what is wrong with those solutions and focus on how to improve their weaknesses " ( 2005,p11 )
By constantly improving on the process , gene modification modification can be improved to the extent of meeting the strict requirements for human consumption .
Engineering design processes also involves branching into different areas of study and combining existing technology to create new ones .
In fact , Food Science and Bio-Engineering was developed by combining ideas from the science and engineering sectors .
Seyyed Khandani mentioned a process called synthesis , which is to integrate ideas , equipment and processes to create new solutions ( 2005 , p11 )
The benefits of new technology to increase food production through genetic modification are endless .
New technology could increase the variety of food capable of being genetically modified , replace existing gene modification methods with cheaper alternatives and even allow vast improvements on food yield from current processes .
There are strict regulations and quality control for genetically modified food before it can be used for human consumption .
Engineering design processes are tedious , complex and require much creativity for the generation of new ideas .
Therefore , genetically modified food created from such processes would be able to pass the strict requirements and thus able to meet the needs of reducing food shortage in Third World countries .
In spite of the increase of research and development in recent years , a significant amount of discoveries and innovation are still being made by people outside of laboratories .
These kind of unconventional environments are commonly referred to as skunkworks environment .
However , we would define it more broadly to include all research done without external aid .
Though the environments are very different , there are also many similarities between them .
Conventionally generated technologies are conservative while innovations created in a skunkworks environment are revolutionary .
As mentioned by E.M. Rogers in his article The Birth of the Laptop Computer at Toshiba , Tetsuya Mizoguchi ,who came up with the idea of developing a mobile computer , had to go " underground " after his proposal was rejected by his superiors .
As his idea was unconventional , his company did not want to allocate resources to this unknown territory .
In order to continue his research , he secretly used money from his company and transferred engineers from other projects to carry out his research .
After 2 years of research , they created their first prototype that progressed to change how computers around the world were used
Indeed , the huge impact brought about by Mizoguchi is shown by IDC 's forecast that laptops would represent 66 percent of corporate purchases , with 71 percent of consumers opting for a notebook instead of a tower by 2011 .
( arstechnica.com )
In contrast , conventionally generated technology such as NEWATER progressed much slowly .
The research on NEWATER started in 1998 as a joint initiative between the Public Utilities Board ( PUB ) and the Ministry of the Environment and Water Resources ( MEWR ) .
( http : //www.pub.gov.sg/NEWater ) Its aim was to find a way to provide a sustainable means of providing water for industrial use and consumption for places where water is scarce .
This research took very long to carry out and commercialise as it has to go through a long corporate structure for approval .
Also , care was taken to ensure all the water treatment procedures were widely acceptable .
Although it has resulted in a resounding success , the technology has not been widely implemented due to patents of the technology being filed by the parent companies .
On the other hand , neither conventionally generated technologies nor discoveries made in skunkworks have an absolute success rate .
For example , the engineers of General Motor 's ( GM ) R&D unit in Detroit were able to create aesthetically pleasing and highly efficient automobiles that ran entirely on battery power ( Rogers 2003 ) .
However , limitations of the technology and failures of publicity resulted in a weak adoption of the new technology .
Similarly , bio fuel studies made independently by many researchers found that it could be used to replace fossil fuels .
One of the techniques involved in developing fast-growing trees that can grow to full size in just 10 years to generate the bio fuel .
( { http : //biofuelguide.net/ } [ HYPERLINK : http : //biofuelguide.net/ ] ) Similarly , lack of publicity and technological constrains prevented it from becoming a popular technology .
In conclusion , in spite of the various inherent differences of conventionally generated technologies and innovations from skunkworks , revolutionary or conservative , both share various similarities such as providing possible but not definite solutions to our problems .
It is by complementing each research 's advantages that we may be able to discover ways to solve future problems .
The Innovation-Development Process , as defined by E.M. Rogers , essentially 'consist of all the decision , activities and their impacts that occur from recognition of a need or a problem through research , development and commercialization of an innovation ' ( Rogers , 2003 )
This process is further broken down into 2 perspectives , technologically or socially determined .
One good example of a social construction of technology would be the video call function of a phone .
AT&T picture phone in the late 1960s was invented and marketed as an additional function on top of voice call capabilities of a telephone .
It allowed user to 'see ' each other as they talked .
This innovation was not one that had been thoroughly surveyed before the Research began , and users ' feedback was that it was bulky , controls too unfriendly and picture too small ( { http : //www.corp.att.com/attlabs/reputation/timeline/70picture.html } [ HYPERLINK : http : //www.corp.att.com/attlabs/reputation/timeline/70picture.html ] ) .
The society could not accept the new product of the market due to several socio-economical and governmental factors .
Firstly , the picture phone aimed to allow both users on the phone to feel closer to one another , as they could now see each other over the phone .
However , it was this very concept which backfired , as users of the phone felt privacy intrusion to their way of life .
The concept was not easily accepted by the more conservative society back in 1960s and hence it failed its primary purpose .
Secondly , it was not economical to own such a phone , as data transmission was not as developed as it is today .
It was far more expensive to own and upkeep such a phone , and even with the monetary ability to own such a machine , technology at that time did not allow for a smooth transmission of data to the phone , as pictures were transmitted once every 2 seconds .
This generally played a part in the decline in product demand in the market and hence less consumers were willing to fork out the money for the phone .
Thirdly , the governmental priorities were not on the development of Information Technology ( I.T .
) in the 1960s , when the majority of the world 's super powers were still in the production and manufacturing industry .
This resulted in little government funding during that era and thus little improvement in the I.T .
front .
It was not until the 1990s that governments across the world poured in vast amounts of resources into researching faster and better broadband networks . This in turn saw the sharpest rise in broadband speed and decline in cost of becoming a broadband user .
In a broad sense , the shift of governmental focus allowed for the booming of video calls function as it is now much affordable .
In conclusion , the world today is better equipped with the relevant infrastructure and network to facilitate the use of such a device , a 'picture phone' .
This spin off effect from such development has proved to us that social determinants have definitely been playing a huge role in moulding the development of our technology .
In modern society , what we can see and hear surrounding us is always about technology and science .
Humankind has been inventing more effective and useful equipment by applying advanced techniques .
For example , since the first airplane successfully flew in the sky , people have been master of the theory of flight which makes the dream that people can fly come true .
Then , in the following years , many better planes were produced to satisfy peoples ' requirements .
According to Rogers ( 2003 ) , technology is defined as a design for an instrumental action that reduces uncertainty in the cause-effect relationships with achieving an advantage or useful result .
In fact , the majority of these technological innovations can not be reliable without human creativity and research .
However , some technologies were invented serendipitously .
Generally speaking , intended research to pursue development is similar to serendipitous discovery in terms of the aim and contribution to human society .
The main difference between the two kinds of invention is the process and the effort .
First of all , the aim of technology which was developed with research is to explore some useful things and attempt to reach the unknown scientific area in order to solve the problems in the real world .
For example , people have spent a great amount of money to reach Mars to explore the mysterious outer space even though the probability of helping make improvements for the Earth is low .
However , this is doing research for improving human 's standard of living and making life more convenient and comfortable .
Similarly , serendipity is the effect by which one accidentally discovers something fortunate , especially while looking for something entirely different .
Hence , the result of serendipitous discovery also helps explore unknown things and places .
In addition , both technology that was discovered by research and serendipitous discovery contribute to the human society .
However , in terms of process and effort , the research to develop new technology is different from the serendipitous discovery .
Specifically , the majority of technological innovations are developed by scientific research based on knowledge , research and application in practice .
Achievement requires a lot of work and thus would take a long time .
Even so the result is still unpredictable .
In contrast , serendipitous discovery seems very fortunate because people receive unexpected things which are always beneficial for human society .
For example , Sir Alexander Fleming discovered the first antibiotic penicillin when he was doing research on biological materials .
Similarly , DDT was discovered by accident in the 1930s , when a Swiss chemist , Paul Muller , was trying to find a way to protect woollen clothes against moths .
Hence , serendipitous discovery is more convenient and fortunate but it is much more difficult than doing research to develop innovations .
In conclusion , people always try their best to make inventions to solve problems encountered in real world .
Continually doing research on different scientific areas is one main aspect to discover what humankind desires .
However , it is true that people sometimes find new things or make inventions unexpectedly , which is considered as serendipitous discovery .
Both fulfill useful functions in human society .
For instance , DDT was widely used as a mosquito killer during World War II .
Truly speaking , people may prefer serendipitous discovery for its convenience fortunate as well as the same award , though it is more difficult to achieve .
Innovations are made every single day and we keep progressing .
But the most interesting part of innovation of technologies often turns out to be the set of events/situations which leads to the innovation .
Innovations may be planned to meet a purpose or to complete an objective .
These are the conventionally planned research based innovations .
Few technologies get innovated serendipitously .
They happen through work of wisdom combined with blind luck .
Comparison and contrast of two technologies innovated in these two different ways gives us many interesting features of innovations to ponder over .
A classical example for a technology invented serendipitously is the discovery of Warfarin , the most effective rat poison in the world
In the 1930s , many farmers in the U.S made their cows feed partly on sweet clover hay for it was regarded as vital for sweetening acidic soils and preventing erosion .
In due time , it was found that the cattle herds were dying rapidly .
When the cattle blood was analyzed in the lab , a hemorrhaging agent called Coumarin was isolated .
Further experiments and tests helped the bioscientists to discover the beneficial effects of this agent for surgery and other purposes .
The ultimate result was obtained when renowned professor Link discovered another use of it as a rodenticide .
It proved to be very effective against rats and became a huge success .
The main aim was to find the cause of death of the cows but it ended up resulting in the discovery of an efficient rodenticide .
( Generation of innovations : E.M Rogers )
The incident which we recall when we think of a research oriented innovation is the issue of automobile safety in the United states .
In this case , the issue gained high priority in Congress , thanks to the help of Ralph Nader 's " Unsafe at Any speeds " .
The policy makers blamed something or the other for the increasing number of accidents and deaths .
The research people tried to refine the system instead .
They formed new public policies and federal law was passed against the issue which forced car manufacturers to build safer cars and highways authorities to ensure safer roads .
In this case the innovation was preplanned .
( Generation of innovations : E.M Rogers )
When we look at these two technologies which were innovated differently we find that research based innovations are according to the famous proverb " Necessity is the mother of invention " .
The driving force becomes the desperate need for solving a problem .
However in the case of the serendipitous innovations , there is no exact driving force .
Sets of experiments accidentally yield results which prove to be significant .
Who would have thought that an apple would be enough for a man to develop the concept of mechanics and gravitation ?
The technologies innovated in this fashion were never meant to be innovated .
But today , without them , our survival seems questionable .
It is hard to conclude which type of innovation outshines the other.Infact it makes no sense as both are special in their own ways .
But it is important for us to acknowledge these innovations , respect them and strive to do many more things to make life better ! .
Engineers have been designing products or systems to improve our daily lives life .
The process that they used is called the engineering design process .
The process has constantly developed new technology that helped to solve problems of human like making travel to countries faster and comfortable by planes .
Engineers have been trying to solve a human problem for many years .
That problem is to make drinkable fresh water available to everyone in the third world countries .
The engineering process involves defining the problem , gathering pertinent information , generating multiple solutions , analyzing and selecting solutions and testing and implementing the solution , as quoted from Kandani ( 2005 ) .
First , we will look at how the problem should be defined in the engineering process .
Water covers 71 % of the earth 's surface and water from the oceans take up 97 % of the total percentage of surface water .
( Wikipedia ) Even though water seems to be everywhere , only a very small percentage of water is drinkable .
There are also many places in the third world countries where drinkable water is not available due to lack of rainfall and pollution in the water sources .
These places which face water shortage for a long time will face dehydration , diseases due to lack of fresh water and infertile soil for plantation .
Second , in the design process is to gather pertinent information on why the problem still exists as stated by Khandani .
Third world countries ' governments know that there is a need to solve the water shortage problem .
However , developing new and clean water technology needs large amounts of money .
This money can be put to better use like getting medication for their people .
Another possible reason for the problem could be pollution from industries .
Inland water sources are being polluted by factories which dump chemical waste products into the water sources , which make the water source unfit for drinking .
Third , is to generate and select possible solutions in the engineering design process .
Since inland water sources are being polluted and not fit for drinking , oceans , which cover a large area on earth are another possible option .
However , seawater is not drinkable as it contains a very high level of sea salt and impurities .
Therefore , to make seawater into drinkable water , engineers decided to use desalination .
Desalination is a process that collects extracted water from sea salt and impurities through boiling .
The extracted will be furthered purified for usage .
In order to make the extracted water fit for drinking water standards set by World Health organization ( WHO ) , engineers will include a process that add nutrients into it .
Another possible solution can be creating more water catchment areas by planting more trees and building reservoirs .
However , this solution can only help to solve the problem in the long run if only the water catchment areas are free from pollution .
The result might not be an immediate effect , as it takes time for natural rainfall to fill up the reservoirs .
As a result , building desalination plants near the sea can help to solve the shortage of water immediately .
Lastly , Engineers can do some testing on desalinating seawater into drinkable water after they have drafted a cheap and affordable desalination process for the third world countries to purchase .
The results from the testing will be sent to WHO for approval for desalination plant to be built for producing drinkable water in the area .
If the technology is newer than the previous old desalination process , the engineers might be able to get it patented so the price for this new technology will be affordable to everyone .
In conclusion , the engineering design process aids engineers in developing newer technology to help meet the needs or solve the problem of the global population .
This process is applicable to producing clean water from seawater , which helps solve water shortage problems in certain countries .
The process is able to identify the problem , understand why it is still not solved , produce solutions to it and get it work in an engineering way .
In the context of the innovation development process , the development of technologies may be viewed from either a technologically determinist perspective or a socially determinist view , also referred to as the social construction of technology ( Rogers , 2003 ) .
The construction of technology believes that the innovation of technologies is limited and controlled by social factors .
One technology that was socially shaped was the invention of automobile cars .
Automobile vehicles played an important role in this modern world as humans rely heavily on them as a main type of transport for travelling .
This technology is shaped by various groups of engineers according to social constraints .
Firstly , the rise of the automobile industry started as early as the nineteenth century and the First World War acted as a catalyst to speed up the research and development processes of automobile vehicles .
This was so as during the war , there was a rise in demand for automobile vehicles to transport soldiers and supplies to the front line .
It was also used for combat purposes .
Funding and incentives were given to companies to improve automobile technology as whichever countries with the more advanced technologies had a higher chance of winning the war .
As a result , faster , more durable and improved energy efficient vehicles were developed during the war period due to the demands from the military .
Secondly , the development of automobiles vehicles were encouraged and limited by government policies and regulations .
As more roads were constructed over the years globally , it benefited the automobile industries .
Most places are accessible by roads . This in term boosted the sales of automobiles .
With the rising sales of cars , consumers had more demands ; manufacturers spent more money on research and development so as to give their customers more choices .
Besides constructing roads , governments gave tax rebates to companies that were heavily involved in research and development projects .
Speed limits and safety regulations set by governments are also factors to be considered when designing and developing new technologies .
Automobiles manufacturers took advantage of these situations and limitations to evolve their products technologies to another level .
Finally , all the research and developments of technology depend on economic factors .
This is so that no investor would be willing to fund a project that does not make money .
Hence , when engineers make improvements to enhance the technological aspect of automobile vehicles , they have to consider the interests of the company .
The technical aspects of cars depend heavily on production costs .
If the production cost increases , carmakers would either see a reduction in profit or potential buyers of the product would see an increase in the price .
These two scenarios are not desired and this is the reason that cars are still running on petrol rather than powered by electricity or natural gases despite the fact that they are cleaner energies .
In conclusion , the research and developments of technology depends on social constraints such as economic factors , military demands or government policies .
Hence , technology is actually a product of society and is influenced by the norms and values of the social system .
The greatest priority of companies is to ensure that projects that they are involved in have great profit potential .
Never Stop
Toshiba is the first brand to have laptops known by many people .
But did you ever know that the invention of the laptop was not supported by the top executives of Toshiba at that time ?
Indeed , there are always some innovations which were created in a skunkworks environment .
However , many other innovations were created in a conventionally generated environment .
This essay will focus on two examples of these two environments respectively and analyze the differences and similarities of these two different environments .
The first example is the engineer of Toshiba who wanted to create a laptop ( Rogers , 2003 , pp 144-146 )
Although he discovered the urgent need of smaller and portable computer in Japan .
However , at that time , Toshiba 's marketing situation was not good and the company did not want to risk a new concept of product .
Fortunately , Mizoguchi did not give up .
Otherwise , our laptops may not be as good as they are now. .
Moreover , he diverted funds and found engineers himself to fulfill his idea of creating the laptop .
After two years of hard work , they finally worked out their laptop .
However , Toshiba still did not accept the laptop because they did not think it could have good market share .
The good thing was that after all his hard work , he finally proved to Toshiba that his invention was very useful and sold very well .
After that , he became one of the chiefs of Toshiba .
On the other hand , conventionally generated technology , like the development of electric cars in California and Arizona , was regulated by government ( Rogers , ( 2003 ) pp .
87-89 ) .
Companies had to do research on how to manufacture them and make them be loved by consumers .
Although the whole process of making the car is very tough , the engineers were supported by companies , the government and society all the way .
After briefly knowing the cases of both situations , let 's examine their differences first .
The first difference is that engineers working in a skunkworks environment did not have much support from public or organizations , while conventionally generated technology received a lot of help from society and companies .
The second difference between these two cases is that the idea of innovating the laptop came from the inventor himself , while the electric car issue was a requirement by the government .
This difference may not be necessary , but it is quite obvious that people in skunkworks environments are more likely responsible for their own ideas .
The similarities between them come next .
First and the most important is that those innovations all promoted development of the society .
Secondly , no matter how much help they had received , they all did their best to present their best works .
No matter what difficulty they faced , they did their best to deal with it and finally solve it .
In conclusion , the first difference between a skunk works environment and a conventionally generated environment is the differences between finances , technology , equipment , resources and people 's attitude towards them .
The second difference is the source of the idea .
The similarities are those innovations all promoted the development of society and they did their best for the creation of their product and dream .
With the spirit of innovation and passion for innovation , our life will become better and better .
References :
Rogers , E.M. ( 2003 ) .
The birth of the laptop computer at Toshiba .
In Diffusion of innovations ( pp.144- 146 ) .
New York : Free Press .
Rogers , E.M. ( 2003 ) .
Opinion leaders and mavens in the diffusion of electric cars .
In Diffusion of innovations ( pp.87-89 ) .
New York : Free Press .
In Singapore , innovations in engineering design have been in the cold when compared to leading countries like Germany or Japan .
In my opinion , there are two problems that have led to this situation : Our education structure as well as the shallow engineering heritage that we have .
Firstly , the education structure in Singapore is too rigid and does not promote the creativity of students .
The majority of our Singaporean kids will go through primary school and graduate with a PSLE certificate certificate , follow that up with a secondary school education in either the express , normal academic or normal technical stream .
This streaming system however , however , was largely based on the students ' abilities to cope with the standard subjects on language , math , science and humanities instead of the interest of the students in terms of arts , science or other humanities like literature .
As a result , there was an unhealthy emphasis on the children 's results in the standard subjects which they learned .
Parents wanted their children to score well in order to advance to university and have a bright future .
In their eyes , creative students who want to make it into the arts stream were just rotten apples who could n't do well in their standard subjects .
Indeed , this was very discouraging for the young minds .
As a result , creativity , which is the key to innovation , is n't developed since young for many Singaporeans .
Secondly , we have a shallow engineering culture in Singapore .
Aside from having many labor intensive industries during the 1970s , our focus of engineering was more towards money making opportunities rather than research and development .
Germany has been famous for their innovative and precise engineering in their automotive industries since the 1920s .
Japan on the other hand , is famous for its creative and remarkable ideas for anything that it manufactures
Singapore , however , is famous for our clean and green country , which was basically the work of blue-collared workers cleaning up the streets during the early hours .
Singapore 's emphasis on commercial gains rather than innovations was largely influenced by the fact that we were a trading hub since British rule .
Chinese merchants , Indian spice traders and Malay rubber traders involved in the trading market were the backbone of our country 's growth .
On the other hand , the Europeans had the Romans who created the wheel while the Japanese made the Katana for their Samurai .
Therefore , we can not blame our forefathers for not being innovative when it comes to engineering .
Our innovations came in the way that they tense business instead .
In conclusion , even if we are able to solve the education structure problem , it will still take a few more generations of Singaporeans before we can start to see results for our engineering innovations .
We are after all , a very young nation when compared to the rest of the world .
Perhaps in future , there will be Singaporeans who can create engineering wonders to revolutionize the world .
We will then be able to catch up with countries like Germany or Japan and be labeled as a country with innovative engineering .
In the past few centuries , humankind has taken giant leaps in technology .
The creativity and need for ever improving lifestyle have led to new inventions to ease our lives .
These new inventions are discovered when there is a need or a problem ; and when an invention would help solve the problem .
However not all innovations are popular , even though the product would have a technological use , it may not be socially approved .
Therefore an innovation can not simply be put into the market and expected to be sold , even though it would have a use .
Even some of the products we use everyday are socially determined , for example , the electric refrigerator .
During the 1930 's two types of refrigerators were at the prototype stage , one the electric refrigerator and the other the gas refrigerator .
The gas refrigerator was superior to the electricrefrigeratorin several ways .
The gas refrigerator uses an ammonia refrigerant which is vaporized by heating with a gas flame .
Then therefrigerantdissolves in water , hence cooling the refrigerator .
On the other hand , an electric refrigerator has a compressor that condenses the liquidrefrigerant and releases the heat , which wasabsorbedby therefrigerantwhen itvaporized , into the outside surrounding .
( Rogers 2003 )
The gas refrigerator , though using the same principle as the electric refrigerator , has a few advantages over the electric refrigerator .
The electric refrigerator has acondenserand motor to drive it , in contrast a gas refrigerator does not contain any mobile mechanical components that could breakdown , and hence would require less maintenance .
This would mean it would be less expensive to maintain agasrefrigerator compared to an electric one .
In addition to this advantage the gas refrigerator makes lessnoisethan the electric refrigerator as well .
( Rogers 2003 )
Typically , one would expect the gas refrigerator to capture the consumer market .
However it did not , the main reason being that powerful companies such as General Electric , General Motors , Westinghouse and Kelvinator spent huge sums of money on research and development .
These companies realized that larger profits can be made by selling electric refrigerators and they aggressively marketed the product .
Even though smaller companies tried to compete in the market with the gas refrigerator , they could not stand the might of companies such as General Electric .
Hence the use of gas refrigerators never popularized and instead today we continue to use the electric refrigerator despite it having several flaws .
( Rogers 2003 )
In conclusion it can be noted that this technology was determined by companies such as General electric rather than it being the consumer 's choice .
Also it goes to show that for a product to be approved and accepted by society , it should be socially determined rather than technologically determined .
Obstacles of engineering design processes for Innovation
As we all know , engineers build this beautiful world .
They apply the complicated theories and knowledge to practice to benefit our life .
It is the engineers who have done the greatest job and made the biggest contribution to human beings .
Although my home country , China , has been developing very fast and achieved tremendous success since the implementation of open and reform policy , especially in the field of engineering design processes of innovations , there are still a lot of problems or obstacles lying on the way to further success .
Among all the problems , corruption and education rank as first and second .
According to the Oxford Dictionary , corruption means that dishonest or immoral behavior of activities .
In my home country , a large number of great ideas or inventions are made almost every day , but few of them are put into practice to benefit us .
What is the reason ?
Corruption .
In some cases , when a research group comes up with a new plan or idea , he has to report to his boss to ask for fund to develop the idea .
Then the boss has to report further to a boss on a higher level , then all the way up .
Finally , the report reaches the " super boss " , but if corruption exists , the standard for the " super boss " to judge whether this idea should or should not be developed further is whether it can benefit himself , instead of the majority of people .
If the research group is lucky enough to get the fund , the money has to be passed all the way down to the group through a lot of institutions in between .
As the money is passed from one to another , it will become less and less , the other goes to the bosses ' own pockets .
Finally , the research group gets the money , but no use anymore , because the remaining money is not enough or the arrival time of money is too late .
When such things happen again and again , people will have no desire to innovate because they know they will not succeed .
Just in this way , corruption hampers the execution stage of engineering design processes for Innovation , killing numerous of engineering design processes for innovation .
The other problem which hampers the engineering design processes for Innovation is the education system .
As we all know , China has the largest population in the world , so students suffer a lot in order to get into a higher education institution .
They are forced to focus on how to get high marks , but not care about the creation .
PRC students are said to be " full marks , less ability " .
They just repeat what others have done before , and have little idea what innovation is about .
Of course , repetition can not lead us to innovation .
This is the big problem that hampers the thinking stage of engineering design processes for Innovation .
Although the government is try to improve it , so far the result is not satisfactory .
In a nutshell , the two main problems what hamper the engineering design processes for Innovation in my home country are corruption , which will probably kill the innovation in the process of execution , and education , which makes the youth less creative that their peers in other countries .
These two problems are very difficult to solve in a short time , but we can improve a lot and make the engineering design processes for Innovation better and better .
Human need is something that is necessary for humans to live a healthy , convenient and comfortable life .
Are the needs that meet/fulfilled human need come from no way ?
The answer is No !
Have you ever observed your surroundings , for examples telephones , computers , fans , iPods etc. Those all came into being through the creative application of technology , and do not appear from nowhere .
The majority of the engineering designs are categorized as inventions-devices or systems . they did n't exist before or are the improvements over existing devices or systems .
Those inventions or designs are processing under a term called : Design activity .
The solution to the design problem requires step-by step methodology , and normally the activity is an iterative process .
Next I will illustrate more in detail how engineering design processes can meet that need by using one of a current human need that should be given priority - Eco Car .
Basically engineering design process includes of five-step process .
It is usually used in a problem-solving works for design problems .
As the example given by Khandani 's article , Wright brothers are actually gone through this five-step process , to show that design problem may require backtracking and iteration .
The five steps used for the solving design problems are :
* Define the problem
* Gather pertinent information
* Generate multiple solutions
* Analyze and select a solution
* Test and implement the solution
10 students from our school , NUS also involving in the Eco car design .
On 17 Aug 2009 , they successfully launched the first Singapore-designed urban concept car with zero carbon emission .
Let 's talk about how they use the five-step process to work out such an impressing job !
Firstly , definition of the problem .
Before we can develop a problem , we need to recognize the need for a new product , system , or machine .
We all know that the vehicles are running by the petroleum fuel , because of the rapidly increasing of the petroleum prices due to lacking of the material , and it is predicted will running out in few decades , this issue leads us to look for a new material to replace petroleum has become enthusiastic among the engineering fields .
Besides , establish criteria for success is important as well .
We should consider the preliminary criteria before move into next stage .
For examples , the design must be low cost ; the design must be user friendly etc .
Collecting information is the next thing we are focusing on .
We need to collect all the information that relevant to the problem .
In this stage , developing a problem statement is necessary .
A broad definition will help in the sense of allowing you to look at alternative solutions .
We should keep asking ourselves questions , in order to discover mistakes and also to help in redefining of the problem , such as : is the hydrogen is only the material we need to consider ?
What are the existing solutions to the problem ?
etc. Searching for information resources for examples , using internet , electronic catalog or indexes will also broaden your view on your design problem .
Thirdly , generate multiple solutions .
In this stage , creativity plays an extremely important rule here because in generating new ideas that may solve the problem .
We could start with an existing solution to the problem , and from there can find out more weaknesses about our design/product and focus on improving the weaknesses .
For examples , the top speed of the Eco car can only reach 40km/h , which is consider " slow " for a normal driver .
So how can we improve from this issue ?
Thus , combine new ideas , methods , finding more weaknesses could help in producing a totally unique solution to the problem .
When it comes analyzing and selecting solution , here we need to decide which solution is best suited for implementation to the problem .
Analyzing the best solution is essential before deciding which design solution to implement .
For examples , functional analysis .
We need to ensure the given solution will function the way it should .
Even even though it meets all the criteria but fails at one of them , it is still considered a failure .
Product safety and liability , we also need to consider the Eco car that we design does n't cause injury to humans , property damage and environmental damage from the use of your design .
Besides that , economic and market analysis , to analyze how people feel in this Eco car , are they willing to pay for a car the top speed of which is only 40km/h ? Lastly is the decision making and give rating to each design alternative against the stated criteria .
For examples , safety : 30 percent , efficiency : 30 percent etc .
Now we 've reached the final stage - test and implement the solution .
There are several considerations to be considered , such as prototyping , concurrent engineering and the distinct activities that might happen during implementation like , documentation , applying for patents .
Finally testing and verification , you have to test all steps in the process work .
Because without having a proper testing at all stages in the process , you may find yourself in trouble later on .
As a conclusion , follow the engineering design process is an important guidance as it can guides your design into more details of implementing ideas , more effective way of problem solving .
Design activity is cyclic and iterative , it will continually repeat to the five step processes , until the best design has appeared .
There are several issues that may affect negatively an engineering design process .
Two main problems faced by Singapore engineers are financial issues and social factors .
Singapore is a modern globalized city utilizing cutting edge technology for its growth and development .
Thus , much emphasis is placed on the designing engineers to develop innovations to further improve the well-being of our society .
Even with strong government support in nurturing designer engineers , the problems are still very much prevalent .
For large scale engineering design processes , a huge amount of resources is required .
A large amount of money is required to purchase these resources .
Financial problems may start to arise at the start of the design processes .
An aspiring innovator will usually face financial problems and find it hard to kick start their research .
Thus , he or she has to find companies or organization to finance their work in return for partial ownership rights over their research .
Without proper funding , designer engineers will find it hard to complete their innovations given the iterative nature of their work .
Furthermore , funding is required to apply for patents .
pursuing patents is not easy as they take a long time period of time to process , requiring large amount of money .
The engineers have to be confident about their innovations and understand the improvements their work will have on society .
( Khandani 22 ) .
Even if the financial problem is resolved , the innovations have to be socially acceptable .
This applies to the design processes as well .
That is , the design processes must not goes against proper ethnics and morals , nor result in any negative third party effects .
For example , some processes of bio-engineering are involved with life human cells research and the use of living test specimens .
These may offend the general public as these actions are seen as 'playing god ' , going against common religious beliefs .
Engineering processes that result in environmental issues will also face pressure from environmental groups or the government .
Another social reason would be the government factor .
In Singapore , there are several policies governing the ongoing design research processes .
Engineers are required to seek approvals before carrying out their work processes to meet safety regulations .
These may result in crucial time loss .
Time is a pressuring factor for designer engineers with date lines to meet .
Tedious 'red tape ' in all the government processes would slow down the progress of research , resulting in lower working quality and efficiency .
In conclusion , the social and financial factors are main issues hampering the design processes of engineers .
The problems are even more so in the Singapore context .
However , realizing the importance of designer engineers in today 's society , Singapore government has implemented measures to encourage innovative engineering .
Development funds are set up and the many guidelines for designer processes are clarified .
It helps to alleviate the situation , but the problems will still continue to persist .
Technology and inventions are not strangers in this fast developing world .
Things that people had never imagined 2 centuries ago have become a normality nowadays .
In 1876 , Alexander Graham Bell invented a telephone .
Today , we can not live without a hand phone whereas people from 1900s did not have one for their own .
Furthermore , sharing of information has never been easier with the invention of Internet after another century , in 2000s .
All these inventions have been contributed by a lot of people of different expertises .
Most of the time , new technology and innovations are being developed based on existing technology while some individual or group may discover technology serendipitously .
There are certain similarities and differences between those two methods of discovery .
We will discuss computer technology compared to the discovery of penicillin which is a serendipitous discovery .
For every discovery or technology to be accepted by consumers , it has to meet the demands of users .
This is the same for both technology via research or a serendipitous discovery .
An example of this is the discovery of penicillin in 1928 which was one of the earliest antibiotics available in the market .
The use of penicillin extended from killing disease-causing bacteria to saving lives in the battlefield during the World War II .
Therefore , this discovery was a success and used by people all around the world .
This fact illustrates that not only the discovery has to be successful but also it has to be accepted by society .
Technology developed through researches has often been influenced by economical and profitability factors .
Most of the products created in computer technology are based on this factor .
For example , the companies have been developing different models of electronic devices every month to boost their sales .
According to Rogers ( 2003 ) , although gas refrigerators has overwhelming advantages ( no moving parts , no noise ) the extensive investment in R&D by big companies had made electric refrigerators better products .
On the other hand , a serendipitous discovery does not depend on those factors .
An individual or a group of researchers can make discoveries which may be useful to society without following the influence of companies and investors .
Other major differences between the two technologies are the availability of funds for research and the facilities used by researchers .
Technology developed through researched usually has ample funds allocated to them whereas the individual researchers will have to find the fund for their own .
Nowadays , Computer Technology has become so popular that every potential research will be funded sufficiently and thus researchers can produce more innovative ideas and products .
In conclusion , technology , whether it is discovered accidentally or purposely , is the main ingredient of new innovations and products .
We have to make the technology useful to society because they are the main users of the end-products .
In the end , a serendipitous discovery will be just as good as echnology discovered by research as long as it serves the purpose of contributing to the society and making lives better .
Energy source is the key factor that will affect the development of any country .
It is required especially for industries , agriculture , and even domestic uses .
However , due to the large consumption of energy , most countries are facing serious energy crisis .
One of the reasons may be also due to the increasing population and resulting in people consuming energy more than the amount of energy produced .
This serious shortage of energy is affecting industries as well as the daily lives of people .
Therefore , it is crucial to find possible solutions to solve the problem before it gets fully depleted .
Many countries now are trying to increase the cost of energy to prevent people from misusing them .
Although some countries are still keeping up with the rapid increasing of energy demands , there is still a need for other alternatives to prepare for the future .
Some possible solutions will be utilizing sun energy , wind , coal , geothermic and bio energy , which in principle are renewable .
However , among all this possible solutions , most of them are not suitable to be implemented due to high cost and the availability in large scale .
For example , coal is cheap but it causes pollution .
Extra work has to be done in order to reduce the amount of pollution produced to the minimum ( Khalid Chandio ,2009 ) .
Several design considerations have to be well-planned such that low design cost , design safety and preventing harm to the environment .
Analysis is the key to process design .
Among all the suggested solutions , it is crucial to analyse all the solutions before making a decision .
After brainstorming all the possible solutions , solar energy stands out as the best solution .
According to an article by Musse Mohamud Ahmed ( 2003 ) , he says that solar energy is world-wide recognised renewable energy sources , cost free and clean energy .
Environment impacts are also negligible .
However , one problem that may hinder this invention is the use of costly equipment and the selection of the wrong peak sunshine data .
Therefore , exact calculations for the solar power production are very important before any actual implementation of solar energy scheme to ensure proper performance and reduce cost .
Cost depends heavily on the size of solar power system .
Weather conditions are important for high performance as solar energy depends largely on the sun .
Cloudy weathers will produce lesser power as compared to sunny weathers .
Engineers need to calculate the required solar panels needed for certain hours use of energy .
Selection of solar energy components is another issue that engineers need to take into consideration when using solar energy .
To conclude , solar energy proves the best solution to solve energy crisis in term of cost and high performance , except for the cost of the solar power system .
Proper choosing of solar power system is therefore very important .
Solar energy also stands out in terms of commercial purposes due to environment impacts .
This will result in negligible pollution produced .
Hence , solar energy provides a remarkable invention to the earth .
" Education is not the answer to the question .
Education is the means to the answer to all questions " , William Allin did define the final purpose of studying , which becomes more and more essential in this 21st century .
Education is such an indispensable part of our lives that need improving to catch up with others ; overall , it should be given priority and development .
Although our common education system is generally sufficient , it still contains some shortcomings that spread out all over the world .
In developing countries , education is even a far-away concept though a lot of governments ' and outside donors ' have been made .
As a glance : " In sub-Saharan Africa , for example , the average student-teacher ratio in primary school is 47 to 1 , compared with 17 to 1 in developed countries .
And that masks even worse conditions in the early grades , where this ratio can be as high as 100 to 1 .
As a result , too few of these new students are mastering the basic skills necessary to begin lifting themselves out of poverty " ( Hewlett Foundation ) .
The education issue also involves the cost of schooling , " Even when schooling is ostensibly 'free ' studies have shown that parents incur other direct costs such as activity fees , uniforms , paper and pens ( including texts and excise books ) , transport , lunches , expenses for boarding and others which often result in the exclusion of poor children from school " ( Chimombo , 2005 ) .
Other problems are equity and gender issue , cultural and religious attitudes , efficiency and quality .
In developed countries , the cost of study and also the efficiency of education are the main points which considerably need observing .
" Another observation in the report that we find is those with college degrees are facing the highest unemployment in two decades since records started being kept .
With college costs going through the roof and in many cases , costing nearly $ 50,000 a year at private schools many are asking whether some college degrees are even worth pursuing " ( Mybudget360 , 2009 ) .
In short , the education shortcomings mainly focus on the equipment and management issues .
The problem seems to need help from social workers , but indeed , it also relies on engineers .
Processes to solve the above design problem include several steps .
According to Khandani , they are defining the problem , gathering pertinent information , generating multiple solutions , analyzing and selecting a solution , testing and implementing the solution .
Specifically , when focusing upon the education problem , it can be inferred that the key words are " cost " and " efficiency " .
Then perhaps a multi-purpose tool is the good starting-point .
The tool should be sufficient to reduce the cost and enhance the efficiency .
For example , it could be an interactive learning device , an all-in-one electronic book , a real-time network or even a virtual intelligent teacher .
Whatever it is , the tool must be affordable by either governments or best individuals , helpful to students ' studying progress and feasible for popularization .
Also and importantly , it should be a new and creative invention .
To achieve this aim , a large group of engineers are recommended to establish and work together .
People coming from different places all over the world will bring along their own view for the issue , understand what their country 's need and contribute both their academic and social knowledge .
Co-operation among engineers will make an innovation in the end when the abstract idea is turned into physical equipment .
Education today should be given more priority and improvements .
That could be carried out by engineers who hold the key to solve design problems .
" Design activity occurs over a period of time and requires a step- by-step methodology " , said Khandani .
