In Diffusion of innovations ( pp.144- 146 ) .
New York : Free Press .
Lightbulb and Microwave oven
Have you tried to live with fire as your light source and use fire to cook or heat food ?
It must be terrible .
Fortunately , Thomas Edison created the lightbulb in 1879 and Percy LeBaron Spencer discovered microwave energy after World War two .
It is amazing that Edison picked up a fifty-year-old idea and made it come true , while Percy brought the microwave oven to light by an accident , indeed .
These two wonderful discoveries have many similarities and differences .
In the first place , the two inventors discovered lightbulb and microwave oven in totally different ways .
Moreover , the idea of a microwave oven was totally new , while someone had worked on the lightbulb before Edison .
Finally , the inventions and innovations of lightbulb and microwave oven are really great creations for human beings .
First of all , Edison and Percy made the two considerable discoveries in two completely different ways .
Edison achieved this unbelievable task by thousands of different experiments .
To choose the suitable filament for the lightbulb , Edison tried more than 1600 kinds of materials with different heat-resistance .
The result showed that platinum was the best material to be used as filaments , which was not satisfying due to its high price .
After many setbacks , Edison decided to use carbon to make the filament .
On the other hand , Percy chanced on microwave energy by pure coincidence .
When he did some experiment focusing on radar waves , the melt of a candy bar in his pocket surprised him .
After deeper research , Percy concluded that microwave heating could raise the internal temperature of many foods far more rapidly than a conventional oven .
In addition , Edison did not 'invent ' the lightbulb actually , while Percy is the first person who discovered the microwave energy and invented the microwave oven .
In contrast to conventional belief , Edison just improved upon an old idea which had been thought out 50 years ago .
Since he was interested in electric appliances , he picked up this idea and made several improvements to it through various experiments .
After improving the vacuum inside the globe , he produced a long-lasting and reliable light source .
In contrast , there was nobody who discovered the energy of microwave before Percy .
After he found out this big secret and went through careful trials , Percy developed the microwave oven into practical eventually .
Thus , he is definitely the inventor of the microwave oven .
Last but not least , the lightbulb helps us say goodbye to darkness and the microwave oven provides us a very convenient way to heat food .
Both of these two remarkable inventions help us to lead a much better life now .
Because of the lightbulb , the big world becomes brighter and more colorful .
Also , we can read , write and do many things in the night .
The lightbulb has brought us easier and more convenient life .
In the same manner , the microwave oven has become one of the many modern conveniences .
It provides us a better way to heat food .
Not only can it save time but it can also be operated in a safer manner .
In conclusion , the lightbulb and microwave oven are both great discoveries .
However , they do have many difference and similarities .
First , Edison and Percy made the two considerable discoveries in two completely different ways .
Moreover , Edison just made improvements to the lightbulb while Percy invented the microwave oven .
Finally , though they are different in many ways , both of them do contribute a lot to help us lead a better life now .
Anyway , we must thank Edison Thomas and Percy LeBaron Spencer who made these two extraordinary inventions .
Nuclear Weapons - a socially determined innovation
15th August , known as " Victory in the Pacific Day " , is celebrated by people all around the world to commemorate the surrender of Japan in 1945 .
What we need to emphasize here is that the atomic bomb explosion in Hiroshima and Nagasaki on 6th and 9th August respectively definitely hastened the surrender of Japan .
In the history of warfare , these are the only two nuclear weapons used in the offensive .
Now , more than sixty years later , nuclear weapons are still the most destructive weapons invented by human beings .
Surprisingly , when the nuclear technology was firstly discovered by scientists , it was seen as a method to satisfy human 's needs of energy .
First of all , we must acknowledge that the invention of nuclear weapon is a result of development of science and technology .
After Einstein 's General Relativity Theory and the famous equation E = mc2 , scientists thought more about how to get energy more efficiently and effectively .
In early 1939 , two German scientists first published their essay about nuclear fission and also stated that this new energy source could bring tremendous profits for human beings .
Unfortunately , against the background of World War Two , military demands had priority over anything else .
The discovery of nuclear technology gave both sides of the war an opportunity to win .
Both Axis and Allies wanted to catch the ball before the bound .
Obviously , Allies finally won the battle on the invention of nuclear weapons .
In around four years ' time , U.S. solved a lot of unpredictable technological problems and eventually successfully made three atomic bombs near the end of World War Two .
Japan tragically became the first and only target of nuclear weapons in history .
Even till now , whether the invention of nuclear weapons was for peace or war is still discussed all over the world .
We can not deny that the two bombs dropped in Japan finally brought peace back to people in the world .
However , the catastrophe it caused for the Japanese was really serious .
Hiroshima and Nagasaki were thoroughly destroyed and most residents were killed by the unimaginable power and heat from the explosion .
Even today , the nuclear crisis in North Korea and Iran still threatens the stabilization of world .
If there was no E = mc2 or World War Two , nuclear weapons may never have been invented .
But everything also seems very natural and has its inevitability .
This is history .
Maybe for the nuclear technology itself , utilizing it to make weapons is unfair , but we must agree that it is the social needs , or specifically the military demands , and government priorities at that time that determined the direction of this innovation .
Just like every year people celebrate the " Victory in the Pacific Day " , there should be some others remembering the nuclear weapons .
There are two different perspectives for the development of technologies : technological and sociological point of view .
When viewed from the technological point of view , it can be seen that the technology , consisting of hardware and software , is shaped according to how technology has improved .
However , that is not true as it can be seen that considerations like market and cost are not taken into account .
Therefore the sociological factors like affordability and user-friendliness are used to determine the development of technologies .
An example of such technology is the Global Positioning System ( GPS ) .
The technology consists of numerous satellites that orbit around the Earth that provide its users with various functions ranging from navigation to prediction of weather , thus , widely used in transportation industries .
The military also uses GPS in various methods from missile guidance to enemy tracking .
Besides that , the public has also benefited from this technology as it can be used for search and rescue purposes and also as a navigation aid .
Numerous factors have brought about the development of the GPS : mainly the government , military and public demands .
First , the government had a great part to play in the development of the GPS .
In 1983 , the U.S. President Ronald Reagan decided that the GPS will be made available for civilian use after the Soviet Union shot down a commercial airliner which had navigational difficulty , bringing about the death of more than 200 passengers .
Since then , the government realised that the GPS is the key to providing a dependable way of navigation and thus , pushed for its development .
Currently , the GPS is widely used in the aviation and maritime industry so that similar incidents can be prevented .
Second , the military brought about revolution in the usage of GPS by integrating missiles and other artilleries with GPS which improved the accuracy and efficiency of the weapons .
Besides that , it allowed the soldiers to do scouting and accomplish their tasks at night through GPS- receivers that coordinated their movements with command posts .
When the GPS is paired together with satellite cameras , enemy tracking and identifying targets are made convenient .
Next , the public demands have pushed the benefits of the GPS further when gadgets are integrated with GPS to provide constant relative motion and time coordination .
Using such products , users are capable of navigating in any part of the world .
As such , even the user 's estimated time of arrival can be calculated .
Such products have saved lives when rescuers tracked the GPS signals from their gadgets to locate the victim 's whereabouts , bringing the success rate of search and rescue mission to a higher level .
Today , the GPS is a widely used technology in not just the transport industry , but also in military and civilian purposes .
It has also since developed into a cost saving technology as it saves not just petrol and gasoline , but also time and effort .
Besides that , many victims owe their life to GPS when rescued from disasters and accidents .
It has been published that the GPS will fail in the year 2010 , however , with its wide range of purposes and benefits , efforts are being put in place by various governments around the world to not just keep it functional , but also to improve its capabilities .
Therefore , we can expect to see more GPS-related technology in future .
