An increasing death rate due to traffic accidents has become a major problem in many countries .
The World Health Organisation ( WHO ) states that traffic accidents are in the ninth position among the reasons which lead to death .
When considering the European Union , 1.3 million road traffic accidents occur each year , resulting in 1.7 million injuries and over 40000 death annually ( International Journal of Health Geographic ) .
Even Singapore which implements strong traffic laws and regulations has also been affected by this traffic accident problem .
The accident rate per 10,000 vehicles has increased from 2.34 in 2006 to 2.60 in 2007 in Singapore ( Singapore Police Force ) .
So , to reduce and solve the problem of traffic accidents , a new traffic system should be formed and it should be the current human need that should be given priority .
The engineering design process will be able to meet the need to form a new traffic system .
The three important features in the engineering design process will cater to the need to form a new traffic system .
Firstly , a feature in the design process is the identification of the problem and to gather pertinent information .
This step will allow us to identify the reasons for traffic accidents from different angles .
It will help us to identify problems in the current system by doing various studies of the current traffic system .
The studies include the gathering of relevant information to analyse the situation .
For example , doing traffic counts , area-wide surveys and parking surveys , as well as identifying the speed of moving vehicles , analysing the queue length and the junction delays could help to gain a better understanding of the problem .
For instance , the Times of India states that there was a survey taken in India to measure the percentage of vehicles on the road and the percentage of people taking public transports ( citation ) . This survey has really helped people to understand which cities have high rates of traffic jams and the reasons for them .
So , identifying the problem is a very important process in creating a new traffic system .
Another important feature is the idea generation process .
This is a very important process as it is the point where we will be able to come up with solutions to the problems .
In the process , we will be able to analyse the statistics/surveys that we have obtained and generate new ideas to solve the problem .
These solutions may include devices to identify speeding vehicles and to make sure that there is sufficient spacing between vehicles .
The Netherlands was the first country to implement such road safety devices and they prove to be helpful as road accident rates dropped by 25 % in 2000 as compared to accident rates in 1985 ( citation ) .
Gordon Walls states that the purpose of traffic planning is to provide a safe , convenient and economic movement of vehicles .
From this we can understand that it is essential to come up with a system which is useful in various ways .
So it is important to come up with ideas which will be useful and economical .
Thirdly , analysing and selecting the solutions will be the next step .
It is the point where we will select the solution which best suits the current situation and perfectly fits to the road of the country .
The solution is then implemented and continuously reviewed .
To conclude , it is very clear that engineering design process will be a useful method in solving the current traffic problem .
The three important features mentioned are problem identification , solution analysis and selection . They are the key features of the design process which will be really useful in solving the problem .
There are many pressing issues that need to be addressed in the current world .
They are problems like global warming and aging population .
We need to solve these problems as soon as possible .
The need for better health care should be the given priority since it affects us directly and its effects are much more immediate .
Hence , many health care products are created and modelled by engineers to meet this need .
They have been made more efficiently and better to human with a design process .
The thermometer and the wheelchair are examples of these products .
In recent years , there were two viral outbreaks that affected us badly and they are caused by the Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome ( SARS ) and the Influenza A ( H1N1 ) virus .
These viruses are very contagious and their victims show a common symptom --- fever .
The engineers have come up with new thermometers that can help to contain the spread .
In the process of developing them , engineers can follow the engineering design processes described by Khandani ( 2005 ) .
Firstly , by understanding what they need , , or " designing the problem " , engineers will know that the new thermometer has to minimise contact between users to prevent the spreading of virus .
Other than that , engineers will also need to go through the process of " analysing and selecting a solution " to make sure that the new product is fairly safe before releasing it into the market and it will not cause any health problem to the user .
As a result , the ear thermometer was introduced , which is safe and fast to use .
It also minimises with the ear by using a plastic cover on the detector that will be disposed after use .
Since then , this thermometer has replaced the conventional oral thermometer .
Besides the thermometer , another example is the wheelchair .
The wheelchair has been serving those who have mobility problems for quite some time now .
From the original design that requires manual operation to being moved with the touch of single button , the wheelchair has undergone many changes .
Every change is made possible not by chance , but by following a set of engineering design processes , like the set mentioned in Khandani ( 2005 ) .
Ever since the first wheelchair is being made , it has benefitted many people .
However , engineers were not satisfied because they felt that it can be improved further , after looking at how the users used it .
They started the process of creating an automated wheelchair by " defining the problem " that some users do not have enough strength to push the wheelchair .
After that , engineers have to " gather pertinent information " to make sure that this problem is real by doing a survey on the users , so that they will not waste time designing something that the market does not need .
And when they have the ideas on how to solve this problem , they need to ensure that they select the idea that is achievable with the current technology by " analysing the solutions " .
Finally , when the new product is out , they must " test and implement the solution " by conducting a trial on the new wheelchair .
Some wheelchair users will try it and find if it has met criteria like user-friendliness , before it is released into the market .
In conclusion , the two examples we mentioned have shown that engineering processes can play a big part in the designing phrase of a product .
Thus , we can see that engineering design processes can help to meet the health care need since they allow engineers to work faster and better with a proper set of steps to follow .
And most importantly , they help the engineers to take note of important points in the process of designing a product , which may be forgotten if a set of engineering processes is not used .
In the field of information technology , there is a clear boundary between conventionally generated and skunkwork developed technologies .
Specifically , in the operating system ( OS ) market , there are two well-known examples --- the Mac OS developed by Apple and the free open-source Linux OS .
These two OS reflect the obvious difference between the two ways of developing technology in their hardware platform : interface and price .
The first main difference is their hardware platform .
While the Linux OS is simply no more than a software and runs on PC platform machines , the Mac OS is exclusively designed for the Mac platform manufactured by Apple .
Since Apple designs the hardware for Mac , it makes the operating system perfectly compatible with the machine .
That is one of the reasons why Mac OS has always been praised by art designers for its smooth performance and high definition graphics .
Meanwhile , Linux , coded in the skunkwork environment , does not have that much funds and ability to compare with Mac at that level .
However , Linux has its own advantage .
The second difference between Mac and Linux lies in their structures .
As an open source operating system , Linux ' users are free to explore and modify the systems .
Mac users , on the other hand , are restricted from the entering the system files .
This makes the Linux OS more popular among computer programmers and others who work in the field of information technology .
According to Forbes , Linux is currently the most popular operating system for supercomputers .
It is agreed by programmers from largest IT corporations such as IBM and Sun Microsystems that Linux has so far the most suitable environment for high-performance computing .
Finally , there is the problem of security .
This is what Mac and Linux have in common .
Despite their different structures and platforms , the two operating systems are quite secured .
By not allowing modification of system files , a third party can not hack into a Mac .
As for Linux , open-source only means users can read its source file .
With its secured configuration , it is still extremely hard to penetrate a Linux server .
On the other hand , the sociology aspect has to be considered as well .
Being a skunkwork project , Linux has the advantage of price .
It is actually the only free operating system available .
However , this does not guarantee its popularity .
The requirement of a high level of computing knowledge makes Linux not popular among the average computer users .
Mac , in contrast , was designed for entertainment and it is easy to use .
Apple is also very efficient at advertising their product worldwide , and so even when Mac and its software are much more expensive than for a normal OS , they are still one of the most wanted .
Furthermore , with the coming price drop , Mac is expected to be the operating system of choice for education and business .
It is not possible to define whether the conventionally generated OS or the skunkwork developed one is better .
However , each technology has its own pros and cons .
Therefore , the choice should be made based on the user 's needs .
If it is a computer for an IT engineer , the choice would be Linux .
Oppositely , if the purpose is mainly for entertainment or paperwork , Mac would be the option .
Switching to Hybrid Cars
Berman ( 2006 ) defines a hybrid car as one that encompasses an electric motor together with a conventional gasoline engine , with a computer controlling the interaction between the two .
They use fuel cells that convert hydrogen to electricity , which is then stored in batteries and is used to assist in the power surge required when climbing a slope or overtaking .
But why do we need hybrid cars when we have cars that run just as well on gasoline ?
Gasoline cars are already an integral part of our economy and lifestyle , providing us with mobility and personal freedom .
However , research shows that the world is fast approaching two billion cars ( Sperling & Gordon , 2009 ) , and this poses a problem in the form of environmental pollution as well as causes adverse effects on our economy .
Environmental problems surrounding car production and usage are becoming an increasing threat to our world today .
According to Nieuwenhuis and Wells ( 1994 ) , " in the early 1900s , when gasoline cars starting gaining popularity , resources like gasoline and steel could still be found in abundance " ( p.53 ) .
An increase in the number of cars on the road will mean an increase in the amount of oil burned , which in turn contributes to more air pollution .
Globally , transportation produces a quarter of all emissions of carbon dioxide ( CO2 ) , the primary green house gas , with some 10000 billion cubic metres of exhaust fumes being released annually ( Nieuwenhuis & Wells , 1994 ) .
Every time a car is being driven on the road , it drains the world 's conventional petroleum resources , and contributes more to global warming .
Materials like iron , steel , plastic , and glass , are mined from the Earth and are used in the construction of cars ( Nieuwenhuis & Wells , 1994 ) .
At the end of the car 's lifespan , those materials that can not be reused are then thrown in a scrap pile , contributing to land pollution .
Hybrid cars solve part of these problems by using more reusable material like plastic , as well as making them lighter and relying more on electricity to reduce fuel consumption and carbon emissions ( Berman , 2006 ) .
Besides the environmental factors , cars can affect our economy negatively .
With the depletion of natural resources , funds have to be diverted into researching a cheaper alternative to gasoline .
Cars drain our Earth 's natural resources , thus inciting political skirmishes over oil , and overwhelming the roads of today 's cities ( Sperling & Gordon , 2009 ) .
Countries with few natural resources have to spend increasing amounts of money to import gasoline and other crude oils for these cars .
According to research on gasoline prices ( Energy Information Administration , 2009 ) , the price of a gallon of gasoline was about US $ 150 in 2000 .
By the end of 2009 , the price for a gallon is expected to increase to about US $ 250 .
Once again the solution presents itself in the form of hybrid cars that run more on electricity that can be harnessed from the sun or produced in man-made power stations and cost less than gasoline .
While the damage done by our continued reliance on cars and gasoline is severe , it is still not too late to do something about it .
In order to prevent more serious economic and environmental damage , dramatic reductions in oil use and carbon emissions have to be made within the next decade .
Policy makers and carmakers need to change the vehicles they design and the energy and transport systems they are embedded in .
Relying on hybrid cars might just be one of the most feasible solutions we can look at to save our planet .
