The production of credit card
Now credit cards are very popular in the world .
For example the circulation of credit cards in China jumped from 3 million in 2003 to 50 million in 2006 to 122 million in 2008
We can see the increasing speed is very fast .
However , before 1920s none knew what the credit card was .
How was the magical card created ?
Which factors led to its production ?
I think there are three factors which contributed to the production of credit card .
Firstly , from the technical perspective , the invention of magnetic stripe card technology makes it possible that credit card itself can record data of receipts and disbursements .
Moreover , computer technology and network technology broadened the range of credit card plural and made a strong link between the card and our daily lives .
Secondly , from an economical perspective , it can be summarized in two points : one is the consumption concept implied in the credit , that 'is ' consumption before payment .
The most important character of credit card is overdraft .
It means even though one does not have money at hand , he still possesses the ability of payment .
So the credit card can solve the instant shortage of money .
Also to some extent 'it ' increases the value of goods .
For example , one has to spend twenty days saving money before he affords to buy a nice coat .
But if one has a credit card , everything remains same except that he gets the nice coat twenty days earlier .
So one earns the extra twenty-day usage of the , thanks to the credit card .
This function of the credit card stimulates people 's consumption desire .
So many countries encourage releasing credit cards to stimulate domestic demand and promote economic development .
The other point is that the credit card saves a lot of manpower and material resources .
With globalization going on , more people travel around the world and money circulates more quickly .
The credit card adopts the electronic fund transfer , which reduces banks transferring a large amount of cash from one place to another .
It does save a lot of work .
Thirdly , from a social perspective , credit card brings a lot of convenience to our life .
There are several simple methods of payment by using credit card such as punching the card on POS and RFID machines . , network payment and telephone payment .
No matter when and where it is , one can get money by credit card instead of carrying a lot of cash .
This character of credit card makes it adaptable to the pace of modern life .
In summary , the concept that should be made before payment is the main reason for credit cards ' production .
The convenience that credit card brings leads to its wide usage in the world and makes it fashionable till now .
