Statistics Singapore ( updated on 26th September 2008 ) , statistics population in Singapore , retrieved 4th September 2009 , from http : //www.singstat.gov.sg/stats/charts/popn-area.html
Up till 2007 , 2.4 billion people or 36 % of the planet 's population actually carried at least one phone ( Tomi,2007 ) , which means there are around 4 out of 10 people carrying a phone !
The number of people using a phone is increasing every year .
How did this happen ?
We should thank the people who thought of the innovation of making this innovative product .
The mobile phone has been a technology which was socially determined .
There are many factors that affect the shaping of this technological innovation .
Such factors are due to economic factors , military demands or government priorities and the private sectors .
Firstly , one of the main factors that affect this technological innovation is the economic factors .
One of the few economic factors that affect is the price drop in mobile phones .
Around 10 to 20 years ago , the mobile phone with basic functions that is similar to a basic land line cost thousands
In contrast , mobile phones nowadays cost as low as 50 dollars or even given as free !
Another reason that caused this to happen is due to higher demand for the mobile phone .
The physical properties of the phone have been improved over the years.20 years ago , the size of phones were much larger than that of today 's phone .
In short , economical factors such as physical properties and price of phones are some of the examples that led the mobile phone to be socially determined .
Secondly , military demand is also another factor that shaped this innovative product .
Originally , the origin of the mobile phone was the radio phone which was used around the 1940s and during the World War 2 .
During the World War 2,Handie -Talkie and the backpack walkie-talkie were what soldiers used during the war ( Tom,2007 ) .Towards the end of the war , equipments used during the war , mainly the radio phones ( the mobile phone 's predecessor ) were then brought to everyday usage .
The development of the mobile phone was in process over 60 years and now we have such innovative products . The best example would currently be the IPhone .
In , we can see that military demands 60 years ago play an important role in today 's development of the mobile phone .
Lastly , the third factor that affected this innovative product is government priorities and the private sectors .
Most countries encourage people to use the computers , the internet service and the mobile phone .
Reports also show that the increased connectivity through mobile phones and the internet may lead to improved economic growth and job governance ( James,2009 ) .
The government encourages the wide usage of mobile broadband service such as 3G and 3.5G broadband services .
Furthermore , with the private sectors cooperating with the government to offer more different kinds of mobile services , this helps in the usage of mobile phones .
As a result , the number of people using mobile phones has increased .
As a conclusion , the economic factors , military demands and the government priorities are the main factors that lead to the innovation of the mobile phone .
