Innovation around the corner
In the 21st century , human beings are faced with a lot of serious problems , such as global warming , environmental pollution , weather change , and frequent natural disasters .
Among them , the shortage of energy resources is the most urgent one to be resolved .
Our prosperous society is built on automatic mass production which requires a large amount of energy .
As a result , starting a war , destroying natural balance and polluting the environment , they are just the side effects of disputing energy resources .
Since energy resource shortage is the root of so many problems , finding its solution is the priority for engineers .
In general , three areas of innovation are improving the effectiveness of energy use and production , designing methods to store and accumulate small portions of energy , and finding cleaner and renewable energy resources .
First of all , the most practical part of solution is to make full use of energy .
The phenomena of energy wasting can be found everywhere in daily life .
Even the industrial design can not avoid it .
For instance , most vehicles ' engines can only transfer about 30 % of fuel 's chemical energy into mechanical energy , while the other 70 % becoming heat and polluters .
Another example comes from the solar panel .
Although solar energy has been regarded as the most promising energy form , solar panel is also well known for its low energy exchange rate-less than 16 % .
However , if the effectiveness of both energy use and production can be improved , enormous amount of energy could be saved .
The following efforts should be put into storing and accumulating small portions of energy .

Although their power is small , the sum is considerable if they can be accumulated properly .
The best example is the wind power generator .
A single generator produces the power of several hundred watts , even less than a family 's need .
But once all energy generated by thousands of generators can be stored and transmitted with little loss , the huge industrial energy need is also able to be satisfied .
Last but not the least , it is still very important to find other cleaner and renewable energy resources .
The current energy pattern contains many dangerous disadvantages .
The traditional energy resources like oil and coal are going to end in less than 100 years according to scientists ' estimation .
On the other hand , the modern energy resources like nuclear power still can not be widely applied since no good solution has been found for its deadly radioactive nuclear wastes .
Many engineers are turning to ocean motion , geothermal power and other areas to find a good replacement .
In conclusion , the shortage of energy resources is threatening the development of the world .
To ensure a sufficient energy supply has become an urgent human need .
If engineers can improve effectiveness of energy use , make full use of small portions of energy and successfully find some other clean renewable energy resources , the society will be able to develop sustainably .
No one thinks and No one to share
From 1840 to 1949 , The Chinese people were suffering from World War II and The Chinese civil war .
After these battles and wars , The Chinese people finally stepped in to a new era , a peaceful but impoverished era .
The Chinese people did not have time to develop their economy and technology .
Therefore , the Chinese economy and technology was far behind that of developed countries .
However , the Chinese people did not give up ; Chinese leaders put forward a series of policies .
Moreover , The Chinese people wanted to contribute towards establishing a new China .
This is why the Chinese economic situation was much better than before .
With regard to technology , a group of Chinese scientists and engineers sacrificed their holiday and worked day and night in order to improve the technology of China .
Therefore , many excellent and well designed technological outcomes appeared during that period of time .
But now , there are two factors hampering the innovative design process .
One is that students lack innovative thinking .
Other one there is no co-operation between scientists and engineers .
Currently , the students in China are used to learning but not thinking .
Learning means to learn and use the knowledge which has been taught by the teachers .
They also do not care whether this knowledge is right or wrong .
However , thinking is a totally different thing .
Thinking means students consider how these theorems are derived and how to find the simplest way to solve the problem .
For example , when students ask their teachers a question , , they usually would say they can not solve a particular problem , and question why this formula does not work ? .
However , we need to hear students say that they have tried a new method to solve a problem .
their query is to ask if the teacher can help to check if their method could be used or not .
The main reason for the present lack is the Chinese situation .
China has the largest population , and they use the college examination to select the talented people .
Furthermore , the method of testing is to provide many questions and to have students solve them quickly rather than give students a single question and have them solve it in many different ways. .
There is also limited time for a teacher to grade the exam paper .
So if the solution is not the standard solution which is given by the ministry of education , the solution is incorrect .
Therefore , students are satisfied in using one way to solve a problem .
Chinese scientists and engineers do not know what is called co-operation .
For instance , when there is a finding which is interesting and can contribute to society ,
scientists and engineers will do their research individually and if someone were to invent a machine by this finding first .
He will publish his achievements as fast as possible .
He wants to make money by this invention .
However , one person takes a whole year to make one invention .
What if a group of engineers invents this machine ?
The time would be much shorter than one year and the quality of this invention would be much better .
Hence , if Chinese scientists and engineers work as a team , the efficiency of work will be improved and the period of work time will be less .
In conclusion , if Chinese scientists and engineers overcome these two problems .
There will be more innovative outcomes appearing in the Chinese market and the technology of China will be raised to a new level .
From a technological point of view , the way to the future from where we are today is either by creating something new or modifying current technology so that it performs better than the way it previously did .
This is where engineering design process comes into play .
In order to come up with groundbreaking innovations to improve the way we live , engineers need to have a design-oriented mind .
However , coming up with new ideas and innovations are more often than not , easier said than done .
As a matter of fact , statistically speaking , the number of failed attempts at innovation far exceed the ones which made it into the books .
Nevertheless , the process of learning through failures have significant importance in the engineering design process .
One of the main obstacles in the engineering design process has to be financial constraints .
Many great engineering design ideas were halted cold in their tracks just because the cost to realize them outweighs the benefits that they carry .
For instance , the proposed plan to use nuclear energy in Malaysia never came to pass due to the enormous funds that is required to carry out research in the technology and even if the necessary funds are secured , there is always the uncertainty if the research will yield any significant results .
On top of that , researchers and investors have all come to terms with the fact that running and maintaining a practical nuclear reactor in Malaysia will take too long for the technology to break even financially .
It is just not worth the effort .
Apart from that , new engineering design innovations need to be benchmarked against their environmental effects .
Engineers need to be sensitive towards this issue and thus , ensure that the impact of their ideas are minimal towards mother nature .
In the case of a nuclear power plant in Malaysia , the idea is not viable as the country has an abundance of forest reserves which needs to be kept untarnished and preserved .
Constant exposure to radioactive substances may alter the natural ecosystem of these reserves , causing irreversible damage .
Even in Singapore , all engineering projects have to abide by the Environmental Pollution Control Act before being carried out .
Besides that , the innovations that engineers come up with needs to be safe for the public to use .
In this case , safety measures need to be put in place before an innovation is unveiled to the public .
This can not be compromised .
As for the Malaysian power plant , The plant , due to the inadequacy of safe uranium containment as well as the skilled labour to handle them , the project is unable to be carried out .
The incident at Chernobyl , Ukraine serves as a good reminder as to why safety is of utmost importance .
In order to cut production cost , several safety precautions have been removed from the initial blueprint .
On the fateful day of April 26 , 1986 , one of the reactors exploded , consequently causing the area to be inhabitable till this day and instantly claiming 4 lives in the process .
In a nutshell , engineers may have great ideas and innovations .
Unfortunately , not all of them can be realized .
In fact , many of them will not .
However , all is not lost .
With small but useful engineering design ideas being introduced daily , serving as a basis for many bigger innovations , it 's only a matter of time before the many obstacles which are holding engineers back are removed .
