Similarity and difference between technologies discovered via research and serendipitously
The world 's technology is developing at a fast pace .
Among these new technologies , some of them are developed by research while others are discovered serendipitously , which means they are found by chance instead of studying on purpose .
Take the aspect of electric devices as an example , The refrigerator was studied for a long time in the laboratory after people had the desire of preserving things in a cold temperature longer .
On the other hand , the theory of the microwave oven was discovered by Percy Spencer by chance .
He noticed that candy in his pocket melted while he was doing another experiment and by using this technology the microwave oven was invented .
Comparing these two ways of finding new technology , they have similarities as well as differences .
As technologies of modern society , both The refrigerator and the microwave oven have practical meaning .
Refrigerators helps to keep food fresh and microwave ovens helps to heat food quickly .
They are used in a way to make our lives better and more convenient .
Actually , they both have become essentials of daily life .
In this way , the standard and quality of life has improved to a large degree .
Moreover , with these technologies , man-power is saved and efficiency of work is increased .
Thus , technologies discovered in these two ways have the same goal , which is to improve the quality of our life .
However , despite of the similarities , they also have differences , which mainly fall in two aspects .
Firstly , refrigeration was a concept before it was invented .
The idea of keeping things frozen to keep them fresh has existed for a long time , so people worked towards this purpose and after trying many times , the technology of refrigerator came out .
As a result , the product will sell well because the aim of the technology was a common desire to meet the demand of the public .
The microwave oven , on the contrary , was not known before the theory was discovered and the equipment invented .
Thus , sometimes there will be a risk in producing a large amount of equipment applying the serendipitously discovered technology because the market for this product might not be large .Since before it was invented , other ways may have already existed .
Secondly , developing the technology for the refrigerator in the laboratory needs a long time .
Since the idea was introduced , generations of people have used various methods to improve the machine and make the technology perfect .
However , the process of finding the technology of microwave oven was by chance and took a very short time , and it might even be ignored if people did not pay attention to the phenomena .
Therefore , developing a technology by research may require more work and developing a technology serendipitously will need more attention to details in daily life .
In conclusion , though differences exist during the processes they are developed , in the aspects of their use and in the marketing potential when the equipment comes out , both kinds of technologies contribute to the development of the society .
In fact , no matter in which way the technology is discovered , as long as it is beneficial to the society , we should appreciate it and enjoy the convenience it brings us .
Reference
Rogers , E.M. ( 2003 ) .
The generation of innovations .
Diffusion of innovations ( pp.136-158 ) .
New York Free Press .
Retrieved on September 7 2009 , from IVLE : http : //ivle.nus.edu.sg .
Do you know that the global worldwide energy consumption was 500 exajoules which is astounding 5 × 1020 J ?
Do you also know that 80 to 90 percent of that is obtained from the combustion of fossil fuels ?
( U.S. Department Of Energy ) As globalization takes place , coupled with an increasing world population , more electrical energy has to be supplied to homes and factories so as to meet the increasing demand .
However , fossil fuels such as coal and crude oil , which is used to produce electricity , will eventually be depleted as they are non-renewable resources .
According to Wikipedia , " Assuming that our rate of usage in 2005 remains constant , we will run out of conventional oil in 40 years ( 2045 ) and coal in 154 yrs ( 2159 ) .
" Hence , the current human need for energy is one need that we must prioritize .
Engineers have therefore started to work on new technologies , such as photovoltaic systems that can convert solar power to electrical energy so as to ease the need .
By definition , solar energy refers to the radiant light and heat from the Sun .
( " Solar energy " ) Every year , the Earth absorbs approximately 3,850,000 exajoules of solar energy .
( Smil 12 ) This amount of energy is almost twice the total amount of energy that can ever be obtained from non-renewable sources .
( Exergy Flowcharts ) As a result , many countries in the world are now tapping into this new source of energy .
The process of converting the solar energy to electrical energy is also known as the photovoltaic effect .
( " Solar cells " ) First , when sunlight is shone onto the surface of the photovoltaic panels , sunlight in the form of photons will be absorbed by the silicon .
Next , the electrons with higher energy levels in the panels will be separated from their atoms and allowed to flow in a single direction due to the special composition of the cells .
Complimentary positive charges that are produced will flow in the opposite direction of the electrons .
Finally , when both positive charges and electrons flow through the silicon photovoltaic cells , electricity is produced .
( " Solar cells " )
However , even though solar energy has proven to be a very good and efficient way to generate electricity , the electricity produced may not be available to everyone who needs them due to the cost of production .
Many modern countries have been setting up more photovoltaic plants to generate electricity .
( " Photovoltaics " ) However , in most third world countries , the governments or private industries may not have the funds to set up photovoltaic plants due to the high initial capital
As a result , despite many people in the country needing electrical energy , the country can not supply enough to meet the needs of everyone .
Therefore , this shows that the technology of solar energy has its own limitations too , which hopefully would be resolved soon so that it can become an accessible source of energy for everyone in the near future .
To sum up , the most current human need that has to be prioritized is the need for energy .
In the next few decades , the demand for energy will definitely increase exponentially as the world population continues to grow .
Therefore , solar energy being a clean and renewable source of energy will definitely build up its popularity as a popular source that can be used to produce electricity .
Hence in order to ease current as well as future needs for energy , solar power is one viable source to consider .
