In many companies , brilliant and capable engineers were often denied the opportunity to express their ideas through innovation .
Engineers in the past were innovative and a vast amount of creative ideas were generated to improve the technology .
However , many of these ideas were rejected by the corporate leaders of various companies .
The leaders were not risk-takers and reflected the ideas to be non-profitable to the company .
Passionate engineers ventured 'in the dark ' and started a skunk works project as they were unable to gain their superiors supports .
There are many defining features of a conventionally generated technology with those of a comparable innovation that was created in a skunk works environment .
Skunk works projects do not have access to the full resources of the company , have their own rules and have to maintain confidentiality about their projects .
Skunk works projects have their limitations in terms of resources .
The project is helmed by the project managers and all problems , including technical and administrative , will be handled by them .
The research funds and human resources are not made available to them .
Therefore the project managers will have to find their own financial support to fund their projects .
The construction of the team will not be easy as the choices are limited .
The more capable engineers were already involved with other projects and there can be no way to transfer out without the knowledge of the superiors .
On the other hand , conventional projects have a huge backing from the corporate level .
All administrative issues will be settled in a much shorter time to allow the project to begin earlier .
Also , capable engineers will be assigned to the new project , depending on its priority .
Skunk works projects aim is to develop the innovation .
Hence the rules of the company need not be enforced in their secret working environment .
Project managers will set the rules for those personnel involved .
There have been extreme examples of rules set by project managers where both emerged successful in their innovations .
In contrast , conventional project personnel have to follow the strict rules of the company .
An image has to be maintained .
Smart dress codes are to be adhered to at all times and working hours should be fully utilized in the company 's interest .
The engineers often follow a monotonous lifestyle .
Skunk works projects are secret projects not to be revealed to anyone .
Personnel will have to maintain a double life for this project .
No discussions on the project are to be made .
Personnel often have to stay back late after office hours to work on their secret projects and no claim of overtime is allowed .
Since they are involved in a secret project , no rewards will be guaranteed .
On the contrary , conventional projects engineers take pride in their work .
Special privileges were often granted to those involved in high-profiled projects .
There will also be media coverage and time to time updates on their projects .
Engineers working for conventional projects are more at ease with their jobs .
However they face equal stress on their projects .
They will have to follow their company rules while their leaders support them financially .
Skunk work projects do not have the backing of their leaders , resulting in secrecy and extra work .
Engineers must be highly motivated and passionate to achieve results .
Therefore conventional projects and skunk works projects are different in nature .
However an engineer can be successful as long as he is highly motivated , passionate and diligent .
Two problems that may hamper engineering design processes for innovations in my home country .
In the real world , there are countless problems waiting and engineers are often the ones to take up this challenge as they strive towards finding the best solution through innovating new products .
An engineer tackles problems by first detecting the problem before carrying out the necessary research .
After which , engineers would then start developing their products and subsequently proceed to commercialize it .
It is necessary to recognize that the entire process is fraught with numerous difficulties which could impede an engineer 's creativity .
These problems should be identified and rectified in order to prevent the emergence of additional problems .
As mentioned , the development of an intended product is part of the engineering design processes .
For these two processes , an engineer needs to be able to think out of the box .
One possible factor that might hamper such creativity is our educational system .
Singapore 's education system has been structured in such a way that it is rigid and text based and does not teach students to apply what is being taught .
There is so much to learn in the syllabus and yet so little time .
Hence , we see chunks of lessons squeezed into packed timetables .
The time needed to fully understand the concepts are usually not enough .
Therefore , many students eventually end up merely memorizing and going through the motion instead of thinking of different ways to apply the knowledge learnt to the real world .
Furthermore , the choice of subjects is very limited and the subjects are mostly of the same nature .
For creativity to be induced , it is important to be exposed to knowledge from various different aspects .
Another portion of the design process involves commercialization .
For a new product or technology to be successful , it is required to be accepted by the public .
Therefore , the society is a big deciding factor for the success or failure of the product launched .
Sadly , society as a whole is generally not that receptive tof new ideas and innovative products .
This is a potential problem which would hamper engineering design processes .
Humans in general , like to stay within their comfort zone and is often unwilling to accept new ideas or changes in their lifestyle .
The new product needs to be widely accepted so that it will be profitable .
Hence , an unreceptive society is not going to generate enough profits to enable the product to be sustainable .
Without profits , engineers will not be able or motivated to continue research and development necessary to improve the products as it is simply not worth it to do so anymore .
An example would be the case of the refrigerator .
Refrigerators currently common in the market are electric refrigerators , which generally produce a " humming " sound .
A soundless refrigerator was in fact produced in 1930 .
However , during that time , large investments went channeled into the research and development of electric refrigerators .
Furthermore , electric refrigerators were more aggressively advertised for .
All these factors led to the downfall of the soundless refrigerator .
In sum , a society which is less receptive to new ideas and innovative products could lead to the hampering of engineering processes for innovation .
In conclusion , there are several factors that play a part in the success of innovative engineering processes .
It is necessary for engineers to exhibit a high level of creativeness .
Moreover , for a new product to succeed in the market , it has to be accepted by the society as they are the ones purchasing the products and making them profitable .
Two problems have been identified which might hamper creativeness in engineers .
Although measures that tackle these problems might have already been introduced , we have yet to witness the effectiveness of these measures .
Source :
Rogers , E. M. ( 2003 ) .
The generation of innovations .
In Diffusion of innovations ( pp.136-158 ) .
New York : Free Press .
Thanks to the technology development , our life is much easier now .
Watching movie , sending SMS , and surfing Internet have almost been taken for granted in our daily school life .
However , several decades earlier , few people dared to declare that they were sure these innovations would surely be popular around the world someday
Similarly , few people risk to make a change , most of them focus on the development of existing productions .
The major job to make innovation has been given to skunkworks .
Despite the poor environment , tough stress , and high risk , skunkworks indeed value more than conventional technology .
To some extent , conventionally generated technology usually improves our life , but innovation in skunkworks often changes our lives .
Skunkworks - defined to pioneer the development of a technological innovation , normally has tougher working conditions .
Usually skunkworks can not get enough support to create a satisfying working environment .
Due to uncertainty , R&D groups in skunkworks often can not find enough people to conduct the innovation .
Without initial capital and sufficient crew , the developing process has no way to start .
In addition , it is a fairly stressful job because of the limitation of time and the finance .
By contrast , conventional technologies have well organized systems that can ensure the progress of work .
Seldom do they have a stressful workload .
The starting point of innovation in skunkworks and conventional technology are different .
Innovation in skunkworks is made for solving the potential problems or needs of life .
However , Conventional technologies is made for solving the existing problems or needs .
When NOKIA upgraded its N series hand phone annually , iPhone of the Apple company surprised the world , because it give a different definition to the touch phone .
The success of innovation is generally much more considerable than conventional technology .
Skunkworks takes a high risk in the innovation process , but it is rewarding .
For skunkworks , the entire work can be in vain if the products turn out to be a failure in the market , but still it is rewarding because of the generous profits in case of success .
Moreover , in many cases , the failure in the research can turn out to be a great success in other fields .
Just like " Post-its " of 3M , was initially considered as a failure , but was finally proved to be a great success in other fields .
on the contrary , it is more stable and reliable for conventional technology .
Therefore , the low risk means a low rewarding .
It can not make a substantial benefit for human life .
To sum up , skunkworks usually has a tough environment and a stressful workload .
Furthermore , it is often at a high risk to invest in skunkworks .
However , for the desire of changing the way of how people live , and also for the considerable benefits for companies and human life , innovation in skunkworks plays a more vital role than the conventionally generated technology .
Reference :
Rogers , E. M. ( 2003 ) .
The generation of innovations .
In Diffusion of innovations ( pp.136-157 ) .
New York : Free Press .
Social Construction of Compressed Natural Gas Vehicle
The Compressed Natural Gas ( CNG ) vehicle is an alternative fuel vehicle .
Instead of using fossil fuels such as gasoline or diesel , it uses compressed natural gas which consists of mainly methane ( CH4 ) as the fuel of a vehicle .
By 2008 , there are roughly 7 million CNG vehicles on the roads worldwide .
The development of CNG vehicle can be viewed as a socially determined technology , because of the influences of environmental , economic factors and government regulations on its development .
Firstly , the development of CNG vehicle is determined by the environmental factor .
Unlike the normal gasoline vehicle which emits greenhouse and harmful gases , the power of the CNG vehicle can emit 70 % lesser CO2 and little harmful gas .
Therefore CNG vehicles are more environmentally friendly than gasoline vehicles .
In the context of global warming becoming a more serious problem , the development of such environmentally friendly vehicles becomes a must .
Many automobile manufacturers ( Fiat , Volkswagen , Toyota and others ) conducted a lot of research , development and innovations for a number of years using CNG as a fuel source for vehicles .
CNG equipment manufacturers have invested in research and development to improve this technology and make it convenient and available for consumers globally ( wikipedia,2009 ) .
Apart from reducing the air pollution , The natural gas vehicle also produces lower noise levels than gasoline vehicles .
This is another positive feature of CNG vehicles .
The greater use of CNG vehicles for public transportation will result in a quieter urban environment , which will be a plus for our living environment .
( Lim , 2001 ) Thus , it is the environmental factor that spurred the development of CNG vehicle .
Moreover , the intention of reducing the fuel cost also shaped the development of the CNG vehicle .
The oil embargo resulted in an energy crisis in the U.S. during the 1980 's .
Such situations motivated the discovery of alternative fuels that could reduce our dependence on foreign imports .
The scientists found a new method that could compress natural gas in a small container which can be put inside a car .
With this development , the modern CNG vehicle became possible .
From 2000 , the oil price grew tremendously , but the price of natural gas was much less .
In order to reduce the fuel cost , many people preferred CNG cars in that period .
More owners of private cars wanted to convert their petrol-driven vehicles to also run on CNG .
This actually spurred the manufacturers to improve the technology of conversion from gasoline vehicle to dual-fuel vehicle so that the cost can be reduced and more car owners could benefit from the CNG technology .
Lastly , the development of CNG vehicle is also influenced by government policies .
Due to the increase of the oil price and the necessity of improvement of the urban environment , many countries ' governments support the development of CNG vehicles .
Many countries which have an abundance of natural gas introduce CNG cars and buses to their public transportations .
For example , in countries of South American , such as Argentina and Brazil , there are about 3 million CNG vehicles which are mainly used as taxicabs .
Some other governments provide tax rebate for the owners of CNG vehicles , so as to encourage the using of eco-friendly vehicles .
For instance , the Singapore government provided 40 % discount on the Open Market Value ( OMV ) cost of newly-registered green passenger vehicles from 2001 in order to build up the intensity of CNG vehicles ( wikipedia,2009 ) .
With the help of the favorable policies and sponsorship from the government , more talented people are attracted to researching the CNG vehicle .
As a result CNG vehicle technology is shaped by government policies .
In conclusion , CNG vehicle technology is a socially determined technology .
Without the requirements of cheaper and cleaner vehicle and governmental support , it might not be as well-developed as now .
Reference :
Lim,S .
S. ( 2001 ) .
Speech By Mr Lim Swee Say Minister for the Environment At the Launch of the CNG Bus and Taxis Pilot Project.September , 2009 , from national climate change committee : http : //www.nccc.gov.sg/Newsroom/speeches_4.shtm
wikipedia .
( 9 September , 2009 ) .
Compressed natural gas.Retrieved September , 2009 , from wikipedia : http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compressed_natural_gas
In recent years , with its growing prosperity and affluence , China is investing more on science and technology development .
However , the lack of research funding and an inflexible education system , in my opinion , has significantly hampered engineering design process in China .
First of all , lack of research funding has significantly hindered the development of many engineering design projects in China .
In China , innovation in science and technology is mostly driven by the state , rather than by the grass roots .
In contrast with some developed countries , the spending in R&D in China is obviously not as abundant .
Statistics shows that R&D spending takes up 3.2 percent of GDP in US and 2.9 percent in Singapore .
However , it is only 1.4 percent in China .
Also , a large proportion of the R&D funding goes to the state-owned military and defense technology cooperation , leaving even less for the rest of the R&D programmes .
The lack of funding gives rise to dissatisfactory research conditions and also implies that many of the engineering design projects may meet either construction or operating budget crunches long before any productive work can be done .
Thus insufficient funding is a prominent factor that hampers engineering design process in China .
On top of that , an inflexible education system in China has also hampered its engineering design process .
In order to come out with a new product , the engineers must be able to think out of the box and possess practical skills .
However , the education system in China does not train the student to think creatively and provide few chances for the students to put what they learn into practice .
The education in China is very much exam-oriented .
The students study hard in order to excel in exams .
The only aim of the students seems to be doing well in the university entrance examination and being enrolled into renowned universities .
In the so-called cramming method of teaching , teachers pay particular attention to memorization , even at the cost of comprehension .
During the examination , the students are evaluated by how much they memorize , and not on how they think .
Such a rigid education system has significantly hindered students ' creativity and poorly equipped them to apply knowledge in the real world .
In conclusion , the lack of research funding and an exam-oriented education system are the two most significant factors which have hampered engineering design process in China .
However , in its eleventh Five-Year Plan , the Chinese government has promised to increase the R&D spending to 2.5 percent of GDP by the end of 2010 .
Also , the education system in well developed cities such as Beijing and Shanghai is under restructure to better prepare the younger generation to compete in the globalized world .
Thus , the condition of engineering design in China may have a more positive outlook in the future .
Hard tomato program and the discovery of Warfarin
Nowadays , we have entered an age of technology .
It seems that technology is everywhere around us , and it has a great impact on our lives .
Therefore , it is beneficial for us to learn more about innovation and technology .
In general , technology can be divided into two types .
One kind of technology is conducted via research .
For example , in the 1970 's , a new tomato variety was launched by a research team in California .
This tomato variety could be harvested by machines , which was a big success .
The other one is discovered by serenity , and an example of it is the discovery of Warfarin , the effective rat killer .
These two examples both have their own features , since they belong to either type of technology respectively .
In my opinion , the innovation of mechanized tomato and Warfarin technology differ in their start , process and key to success .
The hard tomato program and the discovery of Warfarin started differently .
The program of hard tomato varieties began with an idea .
A California agriculture professor foresaw a future labor shortage in California and came up with a rough idea of tomatoes that could be picked by machine .
Then , he proposed this idea to his institution and got the research started .
However , the discovery of Warfarin happened during another research .
Prof Link , the discoverer of Warfarin , was involved in a research of sweet clove disease at that time .
After about ten years ' of research , he discovered Warfarin one day in an unrelated experiment , which turned out to be the most impressive progress in the whole research .
The big profit made by the patent was used to support other research projects of Madison professors , provide financial aid to doctoral students and cover other research expenses .
Moreover , the progresses of the two technologies are not alike .
The hard tomato program followed a whole procedure of research works .
A group of scientists were gathered together in an institution .
They were supposed to use the scientific approach to solve various unexpected problems occurring in the research .
In the process , development was extremely important .
They also cared about the commercialization part .
All of these included building a prototype of the machine used to pick the tomatoes , contacting producers who were willing to sell their products , making their research results known to the local farmers and collecting their feedbacks to improve .
Finally , they came up with their research results after many years of research , in due time according to their plan .
In contrast , in the case of Warfarin , the process was a reversed one .
The product came out first accidentally , followed up with some research to get a better understanding of the discovery .
Warfarin was put into practice directly after it , because its use was totally known when discovering it .
The whole process was highly effective and by chance .
No one expected it before head .
Besides , although both these two technologies were successful , the keys to their success were different .
As the hard tomato program was a research project conducted by a group of people , I think the success was mainly due to teamwork and cooperation of the whole group .
On the contrary , the key to success in Warfarin lies on Prof Link , who discovered the chemical .
In conclusion , the mechanized tomato program and the discovery of Warfarin had a different start , process and reasons for success
Reference :
Rogers , E. M. ( 2003 ) .
The generation of innovations .
In Diffusion of innovations ( pp.136- 158 ) .
New York : Free Press .
Profit Go First or Innovation
Technology is progressing every day , and different products are created using new technologies .
Life has become more convenient with these technological products and companies can benefit from producing these products .
However , not all technological products can bring profit to their companies .
Before manufacturing a product , companies have to evaluate its profitability and reject products with an uncertain future .
Conventionally generated technologies and technologies in " Skunk works " are of great difference while they still have features in common .
Technology in " Skunk works " is like a double-side sword , which not only can become a great success but also can be a super failure in the future .
Working in a " Skunk works " environment is much tougher than in a conventional environment , as engineers working in " Skunk works " are not rewarded unless their work turns out to be a success .
Nevertheless , both " Skunk works " technology and conventional technology make a contribution to technology development .
Compared to conventionally generated technology , " Skunk works " has great potential to become a big failure , while it also has the potential to be successful .
It is comfortable for engineers to make technology work and to optimize a design under given conditions .
Whereas , a well optimized design is worthless if it can not meet the desires , or at least the needs of the customers .
Therefore , on one hand , without sufficient market research , " Skunk works " is faced with a high potential to be a failure .
Whereas on the other hand , a talent " Skunk works " can also be a success in market .
As E.M. Rogers mentioned in his article - " the Birth of the Laptop Computer at Toshiba " , the laptop is a good example of successful " Skunk works " .
On the contrary , conventional generated technology is much safer than " Skunk works " , it can bring steady profit to its company , but , to most companies , playing safe is not enough to compete with their competitors .
The environment of " Skunk works " and the conventional one are very different .
The working conditions of " Skunk works " are tougher than those organized by companies .
Though engineers in " Skunk works " are enthusiastic about their project , it is very hard for them to find financial support , and other experts may criticize their work .
Therefore engineers in " Skunk works " are more pressured than those who work in a traditional way .
Engineers working in a project organized by a company do not have to worry about money , but their level of innovation is also limited by the company .
" Skunk works " and conventional projects are different , but both of them are making a contribution to the development of technology .
Conventionally generated technologies are closely connected to our life .
By doing sufficient market research , technologies provide things that can fulfill our desires and make our life become more and more convenient .
" Skunk works " care more about technology itself , and its aim is to produce the most advanced and optimized designs .
Therefore , " Skunk works " can promote technological innovation and also provide a platform for creative engineers .
In summary , A " Skunk works " environment is much tougher than a conventional environment , and " Skunk works " is more like a gamble for a company for it may either be a big success or be an absolute failure .
Conventionally generated technology plays an important role in fulfilling people 's need and generating profit for companies , so it is a surety of technology 's steady and continuous development .
However , " Skunk works " provide a platform for engineers with great creativity , and it is a necessity in technology 's evolution .
Therefore , both of them are indispensable for technological development .
Reference : Rogers , E.M. ( 2003 ) .
The birth of the laptop computer at Toshiba .
In Diffusion of innovations ( pp.144 - 146 ) .
New York : Free Press .
Jonathon Cagan ( nov 30,2005 ) .
Engineering the Products People Need .
From http : //www.businessweek.com/innovate/content/nov2005/id20051128_963473.htm
Two problems of innovation in China
With the largest population and adequate natural resources , China has developed quite well .
However , nowadays new technology is playing a more and more important role in society and replacing the importance of resources .
However , there are two significant problems in China restricting the development of the technology .
One of them is that intellectual property rights in China are not protected well and there are many illegal copiesa in China .
The other problem is that normal employees in many companies are not valued much by their employers .
The phenomena of illegal copies block the innovation of technology in China .
Here is an example .
As we all know , pirated software is very popular in China .
One of the reasons is that the popularity rate of computers has increased much faster than the rate of consumption levels in China , which means that the price of software is relatively higher than normal people can accept .
Therefore , pirated software comes in .
However , pirated software severely limits the development of software in China .
Because of the low price of pirated software , normal people usually prefer the cheaper one , pirated software .
Subsequently , the inventor of the software can only get a little profit , which will not impel him or her to continue paying much attention to innovation .
Some other people who want to make profit by inventing new software will also be affected by the phenomena .
As a result , fewer and fewer people will try to invent software in China .
When we compare the software area and the space flight area , we can easily find that space flight in China develops extremely fast because of innovation while software develops slowly with little innovation .
Therefore , the illegal copy phenomena restricts the development of technology in China .
Normal employees are not inspirited also limits the innovation in technology .
There is no doubt that China has developed fast since the foundation of the country .
However , when the focus on the enterprises in China is changed , it can be found that most of the huge enterprises are public and rely on resources and monopoly .
Huge enterprises which rely on high technology are very few .
One of the reasons is that normal employees are not inspirited to take part in the innovation .
In many companies , only certain research staff take part in the innovation of technology while normal employees just do their routine work .
Compared to professional research staff , normal employees have more experience about certain productions .
As the employers do not show much respect to normal employees , few employees will try their best to provide their experience to research staff .
Without practical experience , research and innovation are difficult to achieve .
It is well known that IBM employers value every employee in the company .
Many employees have a chance to make a suggestion to the company .
With the large amounts of outcomes of experience and observation , research staff can achieve new production relatively more easily .
Therefore , that normal employees are not inspirited restricts the innovation of technology in China .
Incentives and profits are essential to inspire people to invent new things .
Therefore , China should pay more attention to intellectual property rights to encourage people to innovate .
Unity is very important because different people have different opinions .
Uniting everyone can maximize the ability of the whole unity .
One way to unite everyone is to show respect to everyone .
China needs to solve these two problems to clear the way for innovation .
As the pace of society quickens , people around the world are faced with an increasing number of problems .
These problems could be man-made or naturally occurring .
Regardless of the cause , people have realized there is a need to find a way to solve these problems and improve their way of life .
This process involves the identifying of the problem , gathering relevant information , generating multiple solutions , analyzing and selecting the most appropriate and feasible solution and finally , testing and implementing the solution in the real world .
( Khandani , S. 2005 ) However , not everything is smooth sailing , and there are problems that may hamper the engineering design process .
In Singapore , one of the problems that engineers might face during the engineering design process is that Singapore 's education system is rigid .
Due to the inflexibility of the education system , Singaporeans have grown up getting used to rote learning .
This means they memorise formulae and information from the texts without really understanding , questioning and analyzing what they are studying .
This leads them to not being able to think out of the box and thinking of creative or alternative solutions other than those provided by the teaching system in Singapore .
Firstly , they would have trouble identifying problems in the real world .
The education system in Singapore works in such a way that the boundaries of problems are defined clearly .
There is usually a fixed method as to how a question is answered .
However , in reality , problems are not clearly seen and observation skills are needed to identify causes and sources of problems .
Engineers might also find it difficult to think of various approaches to tackle the problem , and also to use analytical skills to decide on the best method to solve the problem .
Secondly , as the information needed to solve questions and problems in school is already provided in textbooks and notes , engineers have not honed their skills of doing research for relevant information .
Thus , they might encounter trouble in gathering relevant information needed to solve the problem they may face .
Another major problem that engineers might face in Singapore is that people are less receptive to innovations and ideas as compared to Western countries .
The older generation is especially resistant to change , and would rather use products that they are used to .
Thus , despite the presence of new innovations that would greatly improve their way of life , they might not be so accepting of these new products .
This would affect the testing and implementation of the solution during the process .
When surveying the feasibility of the solution , results would not be accurate as the target group of an older age would generally be less supportive towards the new idea .
If the customer base for the new innovation is too small , investors will be less willing to provide funds to fund research and development of new innovations and products , therefore affecting the whole design process .
In conclusion , it is inevitable that there will be problems that might affect the various stages of the design process .
However , measures have definitely been taken to tackle these problems .
For example , the education system has now definitely improved in terms of its rigidity .
Since 2005 , the Ministry of Education ( MOE ) has introduced Project Work ( PW ) to junior colleges in order to improve communicative skills of students , as well as to encourage building of teamwork among students .
Hopefully in the near future , more effort will be put in to encourage society to be more accepting of new innovations that would greatly change their way of life for the better , and also to implement in not just aspiring engineers but in students in general , skills that they are able to use and apply in handling problems in the real world .
Sources :
* Khandani , S. 2005 .
Engineering design process - Education transfer plan , Thesis ( Ph.D. )
Rapid industrialization is one of the main economic boosters that characterize today 's society .
Singapore is a good example of such a society .
Since the 1960s , there has been a paradigm shift from low end industrialization to high end industrialization thus resulting in a rapid depletion of the already scarce resources .
Land scarcity is one of the pressing human needs that may require immediate attention .
Engineering design processes are therefore created to meet the above mentioned human needs .
One such engineering design processes is gathering pertinent information .
It is essential in minimizing the problems that arise due to land scarcity in Singapore .
According to Khandani , " Efforts spent searching for information about your problem...reveal facts about the problem...discover mistakes and false starts . " Researching land scarcity problems can help one to prioritize by deciding on the more important infrastructure to build to strike a balance between social and economic needs .
For example , high rise flats are built to help prevent overcrowding and to sustain the population while mega infrastructures like the Integrated Resort are for economic purposes .
By prioritizing , one can efficiently make use of scarce land material for maximal benefits .
The other process is the generation of multiple solutions .
According to Khandani , " Creative abilities can be developed if one is willing to take risks and is not afraid to tackle problems . " The lack of land is a challenging problem to the leaders of Singapore thus engineers have to come up with innovative solutions to tackle land scarcity .
In Singapore , a few solutions have been carried out to help solve land scarcity issues .
Some of these solutions are land reclamation , condensed structural landscapes and the construction of sky scrapers .
One of the final processes is to analyse and select a solution .
According to Khandani , Ergonomics is crucial in the designing process because production of final products must not result in disaster .
For example , the construction of Nicole Highway initially resulted in injuries but after detailed analysis made by relevant experts , the final product is on its way to completion without casualty .
Construction of sky scrapers is relatively safe despite their height due to deep analytical insights in the construction of these buildings .
As a result , the final products serve its purpose without imposing damage to the surroundings .
In conclusion , engineering design processes are generic as they can cater to all possible problems and help to benefit mankind greatly .
Land scarcity is a good example of the applications of all these processes .
Design or Accident
The naissance of all the greatest technologies and discoveries always have two different scenarios .
One is via research and the other is the result of some serendipitous discovery .
But history shows that that sometimes the fate of the two kinds of technologies are also not the same .
The " designs " are thought highly of by people at the beginning , though the importance of the " accidents " is realized much later .
Actually the majority of engineering inventions coincide with the " design " way .
Many great technologies can be successfully designed should owning to people persistent effect , countless experiment plenty of precise analysis and a mass of sources .
Though it may just be a matter of few seconds for the final success of a new technology development , the process from its infancy to maturity can be very long and tough .
With the coming out of a technology people will , of course , show their high concern on it , because it already cost a lot .
Take the atomic weapon test as an example , decades years ago the military of the USA tried to make use of atomic power . They employed a lot of human and non-human sources to complete numerous experiments and tests , and plenty of money was spent on inviting talented scientists and engineers to come to help them make the most powerful weapon in human history
According to Wikipedia " The Manhattan Project cost 2 billion dollars , this included the cost of the two bombs used as well as the test bomb .
This would be about 23 billion US dollars today .
The development and production of the delivery device ( the B-29 ) cost more than the Manhattan Project .
Therefore , the US treated this new technology as their most precious weapon .
In many cases , technology which was created via research will be thought highly of at the beginning .
Because of the formal research process , like the atomic bomb , many other technologies which were developed via research will draw people 's attention .
As we can see during the process , people know its property , figure out its purpose , understand its advantages and disadvantages , and at last master the way to make full use of it . we 'd feel more confident to take some more steps .
Another reason is that some human and non-human sources have already been expended , and governments do n't want to see these sources turn into nothing .
So technology which is designed purposefully will draw more attention .
In contrast , the second way to make things successful is totally different .
Sometimes people will get unexpected outcomes from their experiment or research .
Even some of the greatest discoveries come from accidents without any indication , for example , the discovery of penicillin and the invention of gunpowder .
Gunpowder was invented by an ancient Chinese alchemist accidently .
One day the alchemist wanted to find some medicine called the elixir of immortality aimed at giving people immortality. .
What he encountered was not the magic drug , but an explosion and the birth of gunpowder .
However , the alchemist did n't set enough value on this great power , nor did other Chinese people .
Gunpowder did n't have a chance to step onto the stage of history until the famous adventurer and merchant Marco Polo introduced it to Europe from China .
Only after that did the world gradually began to pay enough attention to this powerful chemical medicine .
Compared to the development of the atomic bomb , the discovery of gunpowder was just an accident or something unexpected that no one planned to make .
This is very crucial in explaining why nobody attaches importance to new technology at first .
That 's to say , though technologies like that may somehow change the world , it is not in people 's contemplation , time is needed for people to realize the existence of them and to learn more about them .
The world always improves along with the progress of technology step by step .
No matter whether their existence is a design or an accident , as long as it benefits people , that 's what society wants to see .

Embedding High Energy Efficiency into Engineering Design Products
In 2005 , news revealed that the Al Burquan Oil Field in Kuwait , which is the second largest oil field in the world will be depleted before the middle of this century ( AME Info , Inc. 2005 ) .
Meanwhile , the increasing oil price also indicates that society is facing a tough challenge , the energy crisis .
According to the Oxford English Dictionary ( 2006 ) , engineering is defined as the " science , discipline , art and profession of acquiring and applying technical , scientific and mathematical knowledge to design and implement materials , structures , machines , devices , systems , and { processes } that safely realize a desired objective or inventions .
" Overwhelmed by the demand for energy , increasing energy efficiency should be viewed as the priority or desired objective of inventions or engineering design .
Primarily , energy is the fundamental base for all human activities which exploit nature to meet our needs .
Without energy , the advantages of technology that we are enjoying now would vanish .
For example , if there was not sufficient fuel for automobiles , then we would go back to the era of antiquity when walking and riding were the only means for transportation .
Having a glimpse of our life now , we could not live without energy .
On the other hand , it is very irresponsible to squander energy otherwise our posterity would face the consequences of our behaviours .
Hence , maximising energy efficiency should be taken given priority in technology development so that human beings and the whole of society will develop and move forward sustainably .
Moreover , to give energy efficiency priority will prosper the engineering design process resulting from the multiple and more prudent choices of solutions .
It is defined that there are five stages to solving an engineering design problem , " to define the problem , to gather pertinent information , to generate multiple solutions , to analyze and select a solution and to test and implement the solution " ( Khandani , 2005 ) .
If all the engineers are trying to design the technology with higher energy efficiency then they probably will gather more information , generate more efficient solutions and select the solution which is more efficient .
At the time when engineers take energy usage into consideration , the design process is upgraded to a higher standard which meets our needs and fulfills the vital objective of engineering design for technology .
Specifically , when the engineers analyze the solutions after testing , they will compare the feasibility of all the solutions as well as the efficiency .
If all the solutions are capable of solving the problem , then the one which is the most efficient should be chosen .
The real example is that people now are pro hybrid gas-and-electric-powered automobiles instead of the conventional ones .
In one word , energy efficiency should be a priority concern for all engineers due to its positive impact on the design process .
Equipped with high efficiency , all the innovations of engineering technology will be more dynamic and practical to meet the country 's ever-increasing needs .
References :
AME Info , Inc. ( 2005 , November 15 ) .
Kuwait 's biggest field starts to run out of oil .
