A Graying World .
With the development of societies , governments and policy makers pay more attention to the phenomenon of aging populations , especially in developed countries .
According to incomplete figures , in the European countries , spending on pensions , health , and related issues is currently 15 % of GDP ( gross domestic product ) .
However , although spending on the aged is high , it should not be limited .
Some argue that public spending on the aged should be limited so that money can be diverted to other areas of the country 's development .
For instance , government should cut down the spending on the aged , and use more money to attract talented immigrants .
This can not only stimulate economic growth , but also buffer the rate of aging population .
To a large extent , it seems quite reasonable .
However , the result may be that many immigrants who have different cultural backgrounds will enter the country .
One country with a great influx of immigrants may become unstable , since cultures are different and cultural fusion needs a long period of time .
Hence , it is not necessary to limit public spending on the aged to attract talented immigrants .
On the one hand , limiting public spending on the aged does not mean that we can spend less money on the aged .
Some of the reasons mentioned are " reducing the share of public support does not eliminate societal costs " ( Friedland and
If public spending on the aged is limited , there will be social costs and repercussions on families and local communities .
Such costs may even be higher than the original cost of public spending on the aged .
At the same time , cutting down public spending on will shift the financial pressure on families with old people .
Therefore , we should not limit public spending on the aged .
On the other hand , such spending should promote a sense of humanity and result in more ways to help the vulnerable groups ; after all , it is the duty of government to pay more attention to these groups in society .
The aged belong to these , as their productivity is relatively low , with their medical expenses and social costs higher than other age groups .
Thus , public support to finance the aged is extremely important .
In contrast , some may say that it is of children to show filial obedience to the older generation , so young family members must take care of the older generation so government can take less responsibility for older people .
Thus , public spending on the aged should be limited .
However , the aim of government is to enable people in its country to live better and happier .
If we just cut down public spending on the aged and divert the money to other areas of the country 's development , this is contrary to the purpose of the government .
In other words , why do we divert the money to other areas of the country 's development in the first place ?
Because we want to make our country stronger and the lives of citizens better .
Consequently , diverting money to other areas of the country 's development is an extra and needless job .
In conclusion , public spending on the aged should not be limited just so money can be diverted to other areas of the country 's development .
However , it does not mean that the aged should totally depend on government 's support .
The aged are advised to solve their problems as possibly as they can and put public support as their second choice .
I agree with the statement that " public spending on the aged should be limited so that money can be diverted to other areas of the country 's development .
" Although we are moving towards a fast aging population , public spending should be limited and diverted to areas like monetary reward to encourage parents to have more babies .
The country 's development should not be hindered just because there is a need for public spending on the aged .
Besides , if we were to slow down the country 's development , this might hinder our economic growth which , in turn , will affect public spending on the aged indirectly .
As we are now facing the problem of a fast aging population , healthcare expenses incurred by the elderly need funding .
To fund these expenses , a large sum of money is needed .
Therefore , if public spending on the aged were to be limited , less budget would be set aside for the elderly , which would affect them as healthcare is very important to them as they face many health issues .
With the limitation of public spending on the aged , the elderly might not receive essential healthcare due to insufficient funding , which may lead to undesired .
If public spending on the aged were to be limited and diverted to funds to encourage couples to have more babies , many people would plan to have more babies since their worries of not having enough money to bring up or to support many babies might have been partially subsidized by the fund .
As the increase in the fund for baby bonus leads to more people planning to have more babies , this would eventually reduce the problem of having too many elderly which result in an aging society .
Besides , when these babies grow up , they will be able to work and earn money to support their parents .
In this way , it indirectly reduces the problem of having to set aside a big amount of money to aid healthcare services for the elderly .
Another reason for limiting public spending on the aged is that the children of the elderly should pay for their parents ' healthcare expenses .
If funding for the aged is limited , this will result in children bearing the responsibilities to look after their own parents .
As people can no longer depend on society to look after their parents , they will have to take up the responsibilities of looking after their own parents .
In this way , people will be setting a good example to their children on how to look after parents when they grow old .
Although funding for healthcare services for the elderly is essential , it should be limited and diverted to other areas , especially baby bonus .
With more babies born , it could mean more people looking after their parents in the future , which would in turn cut down funds needed for the elderly .
In addition , having more babies will reduce our median age and also solve our problem with an aging population .
References :
Robert B. Friedland and Laura Summer , Demography Is Not Destiny , Revisited .
Center on Aging Society , Georgetown University , March 2005 .
A Graying World , Peter G. Peterson .
Harvard International Review .
23.3 ( Fall 2001 ) : 66
I do not agree with the statement that public spending on the aged should be limited so that money can be diverted to other areas of the country 's development .
The elderly have contributed their years of youth to the society .
Critics might think that as someone is aging , that person can no longer provide for the society anymore .
Money should not be spent on them as they will leave sooner or later .
However , the elderly can still provide for the society even if they are old as they are the wisest group of people .
Firstly , the elderly can provide for society by imparting values to the younger generation .
The elderly have spent many years of their youth on this earth .
Thus they have the most life experiences .
They have gone through many good and difficult times .
Therefore they are in the best position to impart values to their children as they are the wisest person in each family .
In this way , the younger generation will be able to gain more wisdom from them .
Hence , crime rates will be greatly reduced as the younger generation will be wise enough to do only the right things .
This will help to make Singapore the safest country in the world .
Therefore the public should continue to provide for them .
Furthermore , even if someone is old , he/she can still provide for the society in terms of decision making .
With the amount of life experiences , they will know the consequences of implementing different kinds of solutions .
A very good example is our former Prime Minister , Mr Lee Kuan Yew .
Despite his old age , he still contributes to society by making major decisions for the country .
This shows that an elderly person is never a useless person in the society .
On the contrary , they are the ones who can make the wisest decisions .
These decision making skills can also be imparted to the younger generation .
Hence , the public should continue to provide for the aged .
In addition to the above mentioned factors , the elderly have already contributed many years of their youth to society .
Now that they are old , they have problems working for their own allowance .
It is the social responsibility of the public to provide for them in order to express their gratitude for the years that they have contributed to the society .
If not for them , Singapore would never have become a developed country .
Hence , there is no way that the other areas can be developed .
Therefore , the public should continue to provide for the aged .
However , the amount spent should not exceed a certain limit .
As children , it is their responsibility to take care of their parents and elders in the family .
By allowing the public to provide for the aged , the children tend to push their responsibility to the public .
They will have a mindset that the elderly can go to the different societies in the community to ask for financial aid .
Thus there should be a limit to the public spending for the aged .
In conclusion , I do not agree that public spending on the aged should be limited so that money can be diverted to other areas of the country 's development .
The elderly can contribute to the society by using their life experiences to make important decisions for the country .
They will also be able to impart life values and skills to the younger generation .
This may seem impossible but it can be made possible if each elderly person begins imparting these values to his own children .
In due time , Singapore will become the safest county that can make the best decisions .
Until recently , there was much concern about the consequences of over spending on the welfare of the aging population .
It is said that , if a huge portion of the public 's money goes to the aging population , it will cause undesirable effects to the country in many ways .
The median age in Singapore is anticipated to be doubled by 2050 .
Which means that the amount spent on the welfare of the senior citizens is also expected to be doubled .
Elder people tend to be the primary beneficiaries from the public spending .
Although , the welfare of the senior citizen may be important it should not to an extent where the other areas of the country 's development are being hindered .
What is therefore needed is to take a close look at the current situation and evenly distribute the public spending into different areas to ensure that the country is able to prosper .
Public spending must be limited so that it can be diverted into other major areas where it forms the pillars of the economy , like Education , Defense , Technology , and Research & Development .
If the government does not invest enough in these areas , the country will lose its competitiveness , productive capacity in the economy and decrease in public services which will greatly harm the economy .
The importance of a quality educational system is not less than the importance of the aging population .
There is a need to educate the future workforce of the economy , and also to create a workforce which is truly competitive and productive .
Japan is a country with little natural resources and yet has a very highly educated population , which resulted in them being one of the foremost and advanced countries in the world .
A population with poor educational background will find it hard to compete with other foreign talents with quality education background , thus losing out when it comes to employment and resulting in a huge percentage of the population being unemployed .
Furthermore , foreign investors will not set up factories in countries that are equipped with a poorly educated workforce .
Thus education is equally important .
The amount spent on the defense should not be neglected as well .
Singapore is a country which is constantly the target of terrorists .
There were several terror attempts on Singapore , but it was foiled mainly due to an effective and strong defense system .
A weak defense system can cripple a country 's economy .
For example , New York City was once a major financial center in the world , but after the September 11th incident , the majority of the investors left New York seeking safer alternatives .
This particular incident cost New York billions of dollars and also millions of job lost overnight .
In addition , defense is also used to safeguard the economic interest of Singapore .
Singapore , being a small country and yet having one of the strongest economies in Asia , has always been the target its neighboring countries .
Without a strong and effective defense , Singapore would have been an easy target .
Therefore , defense is one of the most important areas which safeguards the interests of a country and the allocation of budget to this area should never be overlooked .
Critics often said that the senior citizens were the country 's pioneers and they had been through the process of nation building and it is our responsibility to ensure that their welfare should never be overlooked .
However , the allocation of the public spending on the aged should be based on wants and the needs of the elderly .
The financially strapped elderly will receive the necessary subsidies for medical , and transportation costs from the government .
Therefore , those who are financially capable will have to rely solely on their retirement savings .
Otherwise , it would be a huge drain on the tax payer 's money , which will not be utilized to its maximum potential .
Clearly , public spending on the aged is required , but other areas which will affect the development of the country are also equally important , if not more important .
In this ever changing and competitive society , Singapore needs to make the necessary investments in other areas to ensure that it retains its foothold in the global economy .
Therefore there is a need to analyze the importance of each area and cleverly distribute the spending .
If we do not limit the spending on the aged , Singapore may risk losing its current global recognition status
Aging is an inevitable process which is often a slow and painful process for the society in general .
With the current research and development and policies , I agree this has helped to ease the aging process to a large extent .
Due to the globally aging population , many countries have since started their research and development on the aging process .
The government has also stepped in by introducing various policies to suit the needs of the aging population .
Thus in the next few paragraphs , I will explain in depth the various research and government policies being developed to help ease the aging process .
Firstly , the advancement in science in the 2lst century has brought numerous astounding discoveries to prolong good health in times of old age .
An example is that there has been quite a lot of research on the kind of food one consumes which will help to retard the aging process .
An example of the above is research done by Pusan National University in Korea stating that eating kimchi could reduce the risk of heart disease and retard the aging process by reducing the amount of oxygen the body burns ( ( Ilbo , 2000 ) , 2000 ) .
Another discovery was found in the last few years that drinking red wine in moderation helps to preserve good health and retard the aging process .
This is because red wine contains a substance known as " resveratrol " .
" Resveratrol " is considered to be so effective when it comes to slowing the aging process because the amount of [ pic ] antioxidants that are present within it .
The [ pic ] antioxidants that are present within this substance prevents and repairs cell damage that is caused by free radicals in the body .
It is these free radicals that wreak havoc within our bodies because they damage cells , which not only cause disease but also aging .
Thus , one can see how extensive this research being carried out to ease the aging process of mankind is. .
Secondly , the government has come up with various policies to ease the aging process .
In this case , we will take Singapore as an example because of the policies being implemented for the aging .
Singaporeans all know of the term " CPF " .
" CPF " stands for Central Provident Fund which is a scheme that helps the citizens to save up an amount of money for their retirements needs .
With Singapore 's aging population , the government has stepped in by increasing the interest rate of CPF .
The government also implemented the " Minimum Sum Policy " to ensure that one has a specific amount in his or her CPF before allowing them to withdraw it at the age of 55 .
The Minimum Sum was set at $ 80,000 in 2003 and will be raised gradually until it reaches $ 120,000 in 2013 .
This helps one to save up more for retirement in the later years .
Another policy implemented by the Singapore Government is the " ADVANTAGE !
" scheme .
It was introduced in October 2005 to support companies to recruit and retain mature workers as well as to re- employ them beyond the retirement age of 62 ( Berita Harian , 2007 ) .
The scheme has helped the elderly by introducing age-friendly initiatives such as job re-design , automation , wage restructuring , training and introduction of re-employment policies in the workplace ( Berita Harian , 2007 ) .
At the end of April 2007 , 411 companies had already adopted the scheme .
This shows how effectively the government pushes the policy .
Therefore , one can hardly see how the policies do not help to ease the aging process .
Controversially , citizens have argued that these policies do not help them in the aging process because it has taken a toll on their nett salary after having money deducted to their " CPF " contributions which make monthly living allowances even less for them .
An example is the rise in the " Minimum Sum " scheme .
This has been proven to be untrue as the majority of Singaporeans supports the " CPF " schemes which encourages safer retirement and there are many citizen who even went to sign up for more policies from the government on their own accord .
To conclude , due to a globally aging population , research and development have been carried out to slow down the aging process and the policies implemented by the government for late retirement .
It is hard to see how such research and policies do not help to ease the aging process
