Based on a recent survey conducted on the impact of technology on the elderly , the majority of the elderly surveyed believe that advancement in technology " will produce better quality of life for themselves " ( 1 ) .
Indeed , advancement in technology has helped to ease the aging process in terms of health , lifestyle and safety .
Firstly , technological inventions in the field of science have made health care more efficient .
Majority of the elderly suffer from memory loss .
In fact , up to " 5 percent " of the elderly in a population suffer from it ( 2 ) .
This can cause health deterioration , as these elderly may not be able to remember to take their medications .
However , recent technology such as the " Med-eMonitor from InforMedix " can help to ease this burden ( 3 ) .
The Med- eMonitor is a pill organizer that has different compartments to separate medications , a built-in reminder system , an on-screen instruction panel and a communication line ( 3 ) .
When it is time to take the medication , a musical chime will be played to alert the elderly .
If the elderly does not respond to this chime , " the machine can place a phone call to a family member or care provider " ( 3 ) .
Another example would be online health services .
Today , health care has gone digital .
There are many websites available , which provide online health checkups .
One example would be Hear-it.org .
It provides an online hearing test that determines whether an elderly would " benefit from wearing hearing devices " ( 4 ) .
This makes it much easier for the elderly , especially for those who have trouble walking , as they do not have to visit a test centre in order to get their hearing tested .
Such technologies make health care much simpler , which in turn , makes it much more efficient .
Secondly , technological inventions can help improve the lifestyle of the elderly by making them more independent and bringing them closer to their relatives .
Take Japan for example .
Nearly " 22 percent " of its population consists of the elderly ( 5 ) .
Thus , Japan resorted to technological inventions " to care for [ its ] rapidly graying population " ( 5 ) .
An example would be " Secom Co. 's My Spoon feeding robot " that helps the elderly eat with a " spoon and fork-fitted swiveling arm " ( 5 ) .
Another example would be the " rubber and nylon muscle suit developed by the Tokyo University of Science " ( 5 ) .
This suit " helps to keep the elderly active by providing upper body support " and allows them to " lift heavy objects " with ease ( 5 ) .
With inventions like these , the elderly will no longer need to rely on relatives and care providers for support .
Today , there has been an increase in the number of breakdown in family ties .
One of the reasons for this may be that many elderly suffer from hearing loss .
Conversation between family members and relatives becomes frustrating , as they have to constantly repeat themselves .
This causes tension between relatives and family members .
Thus , many elderly tend to seclude themselves from the society ( 6 ) .
With hearing aids , this problem will no longer be present .
" More than 30 percent [ of the elderly ] experience improvements in six months " ( 7 ) .
With these improvements , elderly will no longer have to worry about troubled family relationship , thus bringing them closer to their family .
Lastly , technological inventions can help keep the elderly safe in their homes .
Today , many companies provide home monitoring systems .
An example would be QuietCare .
QuietCare uses an " average of five to seven " sensors to monitor movement within the elderly home ( 8 ) .
It can detect , using infrared sensors , if there is " a lack of movement " within the home and notify the relative or a care person ( 8 ) .
Another example would be the intercom doorbell , which can help the elderly " respond to visitors without having to rush " ( 9 ) .
This , in turn , can help prevent injury caused by falls .
The most common invention would be the webcam .
An example would be Willing Webcam that has a built-in " motion capture detection sensor " ( 10 ) .
This sensor can activate actions such as " sending emails " , " SMS text message " or " sounding an alarm " ( 10 ) .
It can detect " the slightest movement in the home " and notify the user if there is an intruder ( 10 ) .
With such technologies at hand , the elderly will be confident to live alone knowing that their safety is well taken care of .
With such advancement in technology , aging would be a worry of the past .
As we head towards the future , more technological inventions would rise , easing the aging process even further .
Who knows , in the future we might even have a fully automated house with a built-in conveyer belt to guide the elderly from one point to another .
