Singapore expresses vibrant and youthful lives through the numerous creative architecture designs of our buildings .
For the past 44 years , Singapore has made drastic changes to the layout of our buildings and many of these commanding buildings symbolize our country 's success .
For instance , the unique " durian " appearance of the Esplanade gives our small city a distinct sky-line and becomes one of the main tourist attractions in Singapore .
However , Singapore is facing a rapidly ageing population with a rise in median age from 20 in 1970 to 37 in 2009 ; there is a need to improvise our buildings ' architecture using current technology to ease the aging process .
Government spending on investment in architectures for the aged has increased tremendously over the , so as to build a friendly environment for elderly to live .
A good example is the LUP ( Lift Upgrading Program ) , which ensurensures that all apartment blocks , including the older buildings built before 1990 , will have lift access to all storeys by year 2014.In the past , this project is not feasible due to the high costs involved and technology is not realistic .
Nonetheless , with our present advanced architecture technology and economic status , lifestyle for the elderly can be improved to a large extent .
To ease the aging process , it is of utmost importance to build a safe environment for the elderly .
In the past , Singapore is young nation with weak economic status , many interior and exterior safety precautions of architectures are being neglected , which resulted in the elderly suffering from injuries at home and in the outdoors .
Falls are potential threats to all elderly in the age group of 55to74 years and 58 % of deaths are caused by accidental falls .

Another potential danger is open drains in the walkway that elderly might fall into and injure themselves .
The aged are weak physically and they usually have difficulties in maintaining their balance on both legs , and needless to say , these poor architectural designs further escalate the danger .
In recent years , modifications in architectures have been made to ensure the safety of the elderly .
For instance , the government has come up with the EUP ( Estate Upgrading Program ) , in conjunction with the policy of " ageing in place " in revamping the estates , such as introducing the use of drain covers , non-slip flooring finishing , and corridor railings .
These enhancements in estate architectures to improve the safety of the elderly are fully subsidized by the government .
It is also significant to create a barrier-free environment for the increasing ageing population in Singapore .
With steps and stairs at pathway , The elderly with crutches have difficulties climbing up and the stairs ; therefore , it is impossible for the wheelchair bound elderly to move out from their houses .
To ease aging convenience , Obstruction-free walkways are built to connect various districts within the neighborhood .
Accessibility to all the facilities in the neighborhoods is enhanced with the distribution of ramps throughout the vicinity . The elderly and the disabled could move around comfortably because the gradient of the ramps is design in such a way that even without the help of a second party , elderly will also be able to move up and down freely .
At community level , drop off porches are built to seamlessly connect driveways to other surrounding buildings effortlessly , which benefits elderly in wheelchairs to move about remotely .
At block level , lifts are improvised to stop at every storey and additional features such as the widening of the lift door for wheelchairs and the lowering of handrail bars for the elderly to grip on for support are included .
These architecture advancements are frameworks of the 5-years Barrier-Free Accessibility ( BFA ) Upgrading Program . The BCA ( full name of BCA ) invested $ 40 million of Accessibility Fund into this program in 2007 .
It aimed to transform Singapore into an elderly friendly and barrier-free environment for the elderly in the near future .
With our current developments , obstructions to elderly accessibility are thus reduced tremendously .
Improvements in the architecture of the external environment are essential in boosting the physical and mental development of the elderly .
Elderly who are prone to illnesses need sensory stimulation and exercises to maximize their mobility .
A study has shown that outdoor parks and regular exercises have therapeutic effects on the elderly in improving their health and wellness , as well as increasing their muscle strength and stimulating their spiritual developments .
Within housing estates , elderly wellness stations and community gardens are built under the MUP ( Main Upgrading Program ) to promote healthy living among elderly residents .
There is a wide variety of exercise equipment at the elderly wellness station and pebble walks are also available .
Since elderly have brittle bones , more resting areas with lower benches have also been built to cater to their needs .
These recreational outdoor facilities are being built extensively to create a better living environment for the ageing population .
" Old age is n't so bad when you consider the alternative " , said Maurice Chevalier ( citation ) .
Indeed , we are actively implementing various architectural developments and policies to meet the special needs of the aged .
To raise awareness of the importance of " shaping a safe , sustainable and friendly environment " ( citation ) for people of all ages , a BCA Universal Design Award was introduced in 2007 to promote barrier-free accessibility in our environments .
With these improvements , we are one step closer in building a totally barrier-free healthy environment where the elderly can travel around freely and safely in absolute comfort .
