Doomsday Prediction about Population Aging Are Exaggerated .
Nations in Asia are suffering from the problem of an aging population . With the increasing problem , the government has no choice but to spend a large sum of money to help and allow the process of aging in the society to be easy and convenient .
With policies , resources and money set aside for elders , elders are prepared to retire and enjoy retirement in a more fulfilling manner .
Reasons for the government to increase their spending on the elders include , the importance of an elderly in a family setting is important and we should all respect them in all aspects
Elders in countries have given most of their lives in their homeland and as a result become a significant part of development of their nations .
In return , the government should take care of our elders as a means of gratification .
Lastly , the potential contributions of the elders would be valuable for the current generation .
Firstly , we should all respect our elders at home and everywhere else .
Given the fact that they have been with us , are living with us and their presence has brought joy into the different households , the support they give us and the advice they always share with us , lies far more than just a duty to them . Rather it is love and appreciation for taking care of them .
To be an example for the households to respect the elders in their family , the government first must show examples of it .
If the government pays more attention to them , the chances of the individual families to pay attention to their elders would increase .
Secondly , our elders have given most of their lives to their homeland and contributed to the society as much as they could while they were younger .
Taking Singapore as an example , just after the World War II , people started to work hard for their future and we the following generations simply enjoy the fruits of their labor .
Remembering that our forefathers have done so much , we can not just simply abandon them when they are old and seemingly useless .
If we just neglect them , there are many other complications that might lead to facts that seems that the aged are really of no use .
Japan has increasing crime rates and from what they see is that , a lot of them are the . Why is that so ?
Shibata , whose task force has questioned 220 elderly people arrested mostly on charges of theft .
" Stated that " When people feel lonely , there is an impulse to commit a crime so they will somehow connect with someone "
It was also noticed that the crimes that they commit are non-violent , t small and minor thefts
With that to show that the elderly really need that attention and help from the government , we can not forget them and leave them aside but help them in the process of growing old .
Lastly , the potential contribution of an elder would definitely be valuable for the current generation because of the knowledge and experience that they have , that would bring many great lessons to the younger generation . Making use of this important factor would allow the younger generation to appreciate them so much more .
The aged are a valuable asset if we know how to make use of their strengths and not focus on their weakness .
Hence , when they are contributing to the society by giving valuable lessons to the younger generation , the best that we can repay them is in monetary value to allow them to get by in this expensive and fast-paced world that we live in .
As they grow older , we must not leave them . Instead we must them get through with just a little guidance to bring them alongside the . There is much that an elder would be able to give their advice on .
In conclusion , elders have so much that we can learn from and they are indeed a precious human resource in a country . instead of looking at them in a negative light and saying that they are of no use , let 's make use of their strength in terms of experience and knowledge to help the younger generation and advice them more .
Therefore the government should try its best to support them , in all aspect of their lives , emotionally , physically and mentally .
Aging is the accumulation of changes in an organism or object over time .
Aging process happens naturally and does not result from disease or accident .
The effects of this process differ from each person but most likely they will suffer from declining organ function .
Vision and hearing loss , smell problems , and memory loss are some examples of illnesses that often attack the elderly .
These illnesses will affect their daily lives in some ways such as cause inconvenience in social life and inhibit their activities .
Nevertheless , current development in technology has produced a variety of devices that help simplify the aging process .
Research shows that of people aged 70 years , 8.6 % report problems with both hearing and seeing " .
This vision impairments and hearing loss can be a serious problem to the elderly as they may lead to misunderstanding in communication .
Elderly who suffer from vision and hearing loss will find difficulties in making a phone call , listening to voice mail , and using text messages with cell phones .
However , the development in technology has eventually overcome such problems .
In 2006 , an electronics brand , Samsung , launched its Jitterbug J , an excellent cell phone for the elderly .
This gadget provides the elderly a simple way in making phone calls and using text messages .
Jitterbug cell phone suits the elderly as it has loud and clear sound as well as large and brief on-screen text .
A satisfied customer , MakenzieB , purchased a Jitterbug for her 62-year-old mother .
Her mother absolutely loves it and could easily understand how to use it .
She can easily call her family and check voicemail by herself .
Technology development has also helped the elderly with smell problems .
A statistic from National Institutes of Health shows that " More than 2 million adults have disorders of smell " .
These problems are more common in elderly because the sense of smell changes as people age .
When sense of smell changes , elder people will lose the ability to detect smoke , leaking gas , or airborne pollutants and toxins .
Thus , they will need warning devices to detect smoke and carbon dioxide .
A device called The Shake-Up Alarm is a solution to this problem .
When smoke is detected , the smoke detector will transmit signals to two receivers which are a bed vibrator and a strobe light .
The bed vibrator can be placed under a pillow or mattress .
Thus , the vibrator will alert the owner even when he falls asleep .
The second receiver , which is a strobe light , will flash 60 times per minute .
The other illness that usually attacks elderly is memory loss .
According to a mid-March story from HealthDay , " 5.4 million Americans over 70 have memory loss that affects their daily lives " .
One problem that occurs as an effect of memory loss is a difficulty to manage a strict schedule of numerous prescription drugs .
Many pills look similar and there are different instructions for taking each of them .
Thus , it will be a big problem for the elderly with memory loss to remember the instructions of each pill .
However , there is a device called Med-eMonitor which can help ease such burden .
Med-eMonitor is a pill organizer which functions as medication separator and system reminder .
This device also shows on-screen instructions which will help elderly take the drug with proper dosage and schedule .
Another device that can help elderly with memory loss is Mnemonic .
Mnemonic is a wrist-wrapped device that reminds the owner about important events or meetings .
It has a special feature which is built-in accelerometer which will keep the display on top no matter which direction it is rotated .
In conclusion , every person will face the aging process and as a result , various diseases such as vision and hearing loss , smell problems , and memory loss are likely to attack as they age .
After all , nowadays research and development in technology has eventually provided a variety of gadgets that suit the elderly and help them handle the aging process .
Thus , elderly will feel convenient to do their daily activities and live independently .
Science , Technology and Social Policies Ease the Aging Population
" Man is different from most other species of animals in that an abundance of resources tends to reduce rather than increase fertility .
" ( ) As the productivity of the world has increased greatly compared to decades ago , an ageing society has come to being .
Problems led by decrease in manpower come along ; however , research was made and strategies were proposed meanwhile .
This essay is going to elaborate the effects that scientific discoveries , technological inventions and social policies have on easing the aging process .
Firstly , new scientific research and discoveries are regularly annouced and the elderly can follow the suggestions given by the researches .
For example , it was found that muscle training can help ease senescence , especially to women .
( Stein , 2008 ) " The lack of physical activity plays a big role in the aging process .
" Strength training stimulates the growth or muscles and people feel more energetic ; also , the elderly with strong muscles are less likely to fall and suffer bad consequences .
In fact , we keep hearing health tips from the news broadcast or feeds such as healthy recipes , aerobic exercise and Yoga .
These are the practical summaries of scientific research and discovery
Secondly , uesful technological inventions have also been convenient to the elderly .
It is not unsual that the elderly have problems with their body like loss of senses .
Technologies like The Hearing Aid may be old news to us ; however , a new invention enables the blind to see .
That is , the device converts what its footage captures to electronic signals , which are transmitted to the tongue .
( ' ) " They can not necessarily read a book but they can read a sign " , said the development company .
The blind are able to gain a rough perception of their surroundings with the " eye " and be independent from their families ' care .
It helps the blind as well as their family attendants , who now have more time with their work , which is conducive to the society 's productivity .
Thirdly , social policies like CPF ( Central Provident Fund ) have helped alleviate the financial support of the elderly .
CPF is a policy to help people save a portion of their salaries while they are economically active .
With CPF , the eldly have money for life after retirement without extra financial help from the government , thus the implementation of CPF alleviates the government 's financial problem , and it is also favored by the rest of the society since they do not have to pay for the expenditures of the eldly after retirement .
Critics of science , technolological and social policies ' for an aging population argue that the elderly could live a satisfatory life in terms of the material ; however , it is hard for them to be happy since the society does not favor old people who do not fit its fast pace .
This is not necessarily true .
It is because there are communities which welcome the retirees who are healthy , independent and rich . In time , they will become more popular and be 'recruited ' by the communities since traditionally , women have provided much of the voluntary work but now more of them have joined the work force .
( A. K .
Rose. , UC Berkeley and NBER ) Retirees in this way have many more chances to communicate and probably they would not feel lonely .
In conclusion , scientific discoveries ease the aging process by educating the elderly on what is healthy ; technological inventions do this in ways to heal the sick , injured and even the disabled ; finally , social policies help the elderly in finance to secure a peaceful life .
