People today have to face an extremely serious problem of an aging population .
According to a definition on the Wikipedia website , reasons for an aging population , are usually migration , longer life expectancy , and decreased birth rate , which increase the number and proportion of the older people in the society .
Since , the aging population has been dramatically influencing various fields in people lives such as economics , healthcare system , and social policy .
Therefore , many research , development and policies have been proposed to help to ease this process .
Firstly , for a graying population around the world , lots of policies have been applied to control the birth and death rate or to balance the age structure .
One of the most possibly effective ways is the " two child " population policy in Shanghai , a big city in China .
The Shanghai Daily says about 22 % of the population is over 60 years old .
additionally , for a long time , the Chinese population was controlled by a " one child " policy .
As a result , an increased aging population has developed .
Therefore , " a " two child " policy can relax this problem and boost a higher birth rate , with a government campaign that encourages couples to have a second child .
However , due to a lack of financial incentives , there is still no official announcement with regard to this .
Secondly , to cope with the aging process , an increase in healthcare demand can be organized by improving system performance , redesigning service delivery , support informal caregivers , and shift demographic parameters .
Obviously , the older people use more healthcare than young people .
Nevertheless , health costs are independent of the age structure , which defines the distribution of predetermined expenditures .
Particularly , in Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development ( OECD ) , aging population does not have any connections to health expenditure as a part of GDP .
For example , the over-65-year-old Swedish made up 17.3 % in 2000 , but Sweden just spent 8.6 % GDP on health .
The former in Australia was 12.7 % , and the latter was 9.3 % , figured in 2001 and 2002 .
Thirdly , as mentioned in " A graying world " by Peter Peterson , late retirement not only solves the employment problem , but also lightens the financial burden on the young .
In countries with a limited labour force , taking advantage of experienced , stable employers is very important , as it also contributes to the family income and saves training cost .
Moreover , providing work to the older people helps them from being bored , alone , and maybe depressed .
Therefore , the younger people who are the breadwinners of the family are more relaxed and under less pressure , so their work will be more efficient but less stressful .
In conclusion , due to a development in various areas , world has to face a problem of aging population .
Awaring of this , lots of countries have applied a plenty of effective policies to adapt to a new changing world .
Although there are many developments and improvements for it , it seems that some governments still have not seriously concerned on it .
Reference :
http : //www.businessweek.com/globalbiz/blog/eyeonasia/archives/2009/07/shanghai_pushes.html http : //www.mja.com.au/public/issues/180_11_070604/coo10869_fm.html # elementId-1084475 http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ageing
Technological inventions in three fields ease the aging process
There is a robot project called Twendy-one under research at WASEDA University .
This project aims to develop a daily life support robot for the aged .
( Sugano Laboratory , 2007 ) Currently , this 147cm tall human-symbiotic- robot can perform conversation with people ; provide motion support and perform sophisticated tasks such as fetching seasonings from the refrigerator and picking up a piece of bread from the toaster and putting it on a plate using a food tong without spoiling it .
With these functions , this robot may bring great convenience to the life of the elderly and ease the aging problem if it can be industrialized .
In fact , there are a number of researches like Twendy-one , which focuses on technological innovations helpful to the aged people , which is being currently done
First , technological inventions provide solution to the vision problem that comes with aging , presbyopia .
The aged may choose to wear optical lenses for presbyopia , and current research has raised the technology of this lens to a new height .
( Pizzo & Segre , 2008 ) Each piece of this kind of lens is divided into two parts with different focus .
This enable the presbyopia patients , usually the aged , to see both far objects and near objects clearly without changing lenses .
Moreover , this kind of contact lens rides on the eyeball but does not roll together with the eyeball .
This means , when the patient looks down , he or she can use the lower part of the lens to read and use the upper part of the lens with a different focus to look at distant objects .
Besides , the aged may also choose to carry a portable digital magnifier which takes a picture behind the device , magnifies it to a desired clearness and shows it on the screen such as PocketViewer .
( HumanWare Group , 2009 ) With these technological inventions , the aged may be able to read and write like young people .
Hence , the pressure of the aging process is reduced .
Second , technological inventions provide health condition monitoring for the elderly in order that they may be able to arrange their activities accordingly and get treatment in time .
This is enabled by the invention of portable , user-friendly and accurate devices which works as sphygmomanometer , glucometer or electrocardiograph .
For example , one hospital in Qindao , China is providing a 24 hour heart electrocardiogram monitoring service to the aged .
( Surprising !
Heart can be monitored 24 hours a day , 2008 ) People receiving this service will carry a newly invented device which captures a persons heart electrocardiogram and sends it to the hospital through a mobile phone network in real time .
This information is further recorded and processed by the server in the hospital .
The server can recognize abnormal patterns of the electrocardiogram and send warnings accordingly to the doctor .
Moreover , this service system allows patients to get consultation from doctors using the device whenever they feel unwell .
With technological inventions like this , it is likely that the aged will enjoy a healthier and longer life which will ease , , the aging process .
Third , technological inventions provides help for the aged who are incapable of walking by himself or herself .
With the decline of muscle and motor nerve , the aged tends to have difficulty in walking and doing physical activities .
To cope with this problem , technological inventions use two main methods : either to assist and enhance the ability of weak limbs or provide alternative transport .
For example , Cyberdyne Inc. in Japan introduced a robotic suit called HAL to enhance the ability of limbs .
( Sankai , 2009 ) This robotic suit is driven by a battery and can be worn by a person .
It detects bio-signal from a person 's skin , analyzes the signal to figure out the person 's movement and provides the necessary support
In this way , a person 's weak limbs can be enhanced .
Another example is the wheelchair , which gives the aged an alternative way to 'walk' .
New technological inventions such as Topchair even allow wheelchairs to climb stairs .
This wheelchair from France is able to climb up and go down stairs as well as moving at a speed greater then 35km/h while it only needs one or two fingers to operate .
( Stair climbing wheelchair , 2008 ) With the help of this kind of technological inventions , the mobility problem of the aged is eased .
In this way , the process of aging is eased by technological inventions .
In conclusion , current research in technological inventions mainly have accomplishments in three areas : vision assistance , health condition monitoring and mobility support .
In each area , inventions are solving practical problems faced by the aged .
By solving these problems , the lives of the aged are enhanced while the stress of the aging process is reduced .
Therefore , current research in technological inventions have helped to ease the aging process to a large extent .
