Caring for the old
Recently , a controversial topic has been put forward .
It is about whether public spending on the aged should be limited so that money can be diverted to other areas of the country 's development .
It can be argued that public spending on the aged should not be limited .
The reasons are as follows : Firstly , put first things first .
Secondly , cutting down public spending may arouse complaints from the public .
Thirdly , limiting public spending on the aged will surely increase the load on the youth .
First of all , put first things first , this means satisfying the basic needs ofthe aged is the most important thing for a country , as only when the basic needs of people are satisfied , can development be possible. .
Imagine if the aged are starving , how can the government still limit public spending and use the money on other areas , regardless of thousands of lives .
It looks like exchanging development with people 's lives .
For instance , after the war , the government of Iraq tried to collect money for public spending and basic reconstruction .
In the case of Iraq , satisfying the basic needs of the people is the most important thing which should be put first .
Different countries have different cases that can not be talked together .
Another reason is that limiting public spending may arouse complaints from the public , which in return , has an effect on the development of the country .
For some elderly people , public spending is the only source of income .
Limiting public spending will make it harder for them to live , especially for old people who have no children and are in poor physical condition .
So if their incomes are limited , it must arouse complaints and evoke the indignation .
People may be anti-government and try to hinder the implementation of new policy , which eases the development of the country .
The most interesting thing is that voters tend to vote for those who approve the usage of money on public spending .
So the government should not limit public spending in case of complaints from the public .
Finally , limiting public spending will surely increase the burden on the youth , since they will share much more responsibility for supporting the aged .
The youth have already borne the load of bringing up their children ; they must feel more stressful if the society throws the aged problem onto them .
Some people may say that offering sufficient public spending will make the aged rely more on the government .
However , it is not true .
Elderly people are still looking for light jobs to make money .
For example , waiters and cleaners in shops like Macdonalds are mostly made up of old people .
The aged still try their best to create value for society
Offering public spending just supply the guarantee of their life .
Limiting public spending on the aged is a serious matter , especially for those who are physically disabled or who live alone without children .
The aged should be cared for by society . Their basic needs should be satisfied first , then the countries ' development can be talked .
Furthermore , limiting public spending may cause complaints from the public and increase the load on the younger generation .
Therefore , public spending should not be limited as limiting public spending is the wrong way to develop a country .
Aging populations are a global phenomenon which affects economic growth , sustainability within families and public spending .
It is caused by declining fertility and rising life expectancy .
It reduces economic growth as the size of the workforce shrinks as more elderly people leave the workforce and less people are recruited into the workforce .
Another impact is the sustainability of families , because there are far less children supporting far more elderly .
This results in severe financial stress for the working population .
Public spending is also stressed to provide pensions , building infrastructure and healthcare catered for the elderly .
Therefore , Public spending for the aged should be limited because it is impractical for public spending on the aged not to be limited , and that the limit should be set on healthcare without neglecting the healthcare and social needs of the elderly .
It is impractical for public spending on the aged not to be limited .
If it is not limited , then it will increase indefinitely .
Either other areas of public spending have to receive less funding , or taxes have to be raised to allow for more funds to be spent on the aged .
These two solutions are both impractical .
Firstly , public funding on other sectors is also limited and can not be reduced as they are equally important .
Housing and healthcare are basic needs of people .
The military is needed for the defense of the nation .
Public spending on technology can not be reduced as it is a substitute for the decline in productivity of a shrinking workforce .
This is because , technology provides the automation and machines to increase productivity solving the problem of a shrinking workforce .
Secondly , the main income for public spending is from taxes , especially income taxes from the working population with services tax forming the largest proportion .
If taxes are raised substantially , it would worsen the severe financial stress for the working population and adversely impact the consumer market .
Therefore , public spending on the aged definitely has to be limited , ensuring enough funding goes to other sectors such as education , military , technology , transport , housing , healthcare , sports , etc which are equally important so as not to increase taxes for the working population .
The government should limit public spending on healthcare for the aged , and the limit should satisfy the healthcare needs of all the elderly .
Healthcare has become more of a want rather than a basic need .
The government has to distinguish between needs and wants .
Needs are consultation and medication upon falling ill .
Wants are usually specialist services that perform detailed checkups to determine the underlying cause of the illness , analysis of patients ' symptoms to predict illnesses they might contract and certain pharmaceutical medicines which act as supplements .
The wanted healthcare costs are significantly higher as specialist services and pharmaceuticals use high technology equipment and expertise .
Therefore , individuals should pay for what is wanted and only needs should be subsidized by the government to reduce public spending on healthcare for the aged .
The government should also support healthcare costs for those elderly in families with financial problems as poverty would come into place if basic healthcare is not provided to everyone .
The elderly are extremely susceptible to certain illnesses due to age .
These illnesses or diseases could be non-communicable or chronic which include cardiovascular disease , dementia and Alzheimer 's disease , cancer , arthritis and diabetes .
Hence , self reliance such as retirement savings has to be in place first to allow the elderly to be able to pay for illnesses which they might contract later .
Otherwise , it would be a huge drain on government resources to pay for all their medical expenses .
Although , public spending on the aged has to be limited , it can not neglect the social needs of the elderly .
Social needs of the elderly include being able to communicate with the community .
As the elderly are physically weaker and have poorer vision , elderly friendly infrastructures ,which include enhancements to transport facilities and housing , are necessary to free the elderly from problems of mobility within the community. .
Imagine if there were plenty of staircases and no lifts , signs with small fonts and no resting areas . no resting areas .
It would be an anti-elderly society where the elderly would most likely stay at home .
These elderly friendly infrastructures are meant to give accessibility for the elderly to physically communicate with friends , families and other people making them part of the community .
After all , it is only morally right to do so as the elderly were once part of the working population that contributed to the nation and they now form a significant portion of the population .
In conclusion , the world should shift towards fostering an elderly friendly society that values their contribution and allows them to be part of the community .
It should also inculcate a strong sense of self reliance among the workforce to prepare them for their old age .
This would reduce their dependence on children or government to support them and not hinder the growth of other areas of the country 's development , as these other areas currently receive fewer funds due to the increasing amount of funds being diverted into helping the growing aged population .
Psychological help to ease the aging process
According to the definition from the Internet , " psychology is an { academic } [ HYPERLINK : http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academic ] and { applied } [ HYPERLINK : http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Applied_science ] discipline involving the systematic , and often { scientific } [ HYPERLINK : http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science ] , study of human/animal { mental functions } [ HYPERLINK : http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mental_function ] and { behavior } [ HYPERLINK : http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Behavior ] .
" ( Wikipedia , 2009 ) .
As psychology develops , it has benefitted humans a lot in helping people to know more about themselves .
Furthermore , current psychological research and development have indeed helped to ease the aging process by dealing with elderly depression , promoting life-long learning and eliminating ageism .
Elderly depression , which could lead to serious consequences and even become life-threatening , can be prevented and eased with psychological consultation and treatment .
As a common elderly mental illness , elderly depression could as well result in miocardial infarction , high blood pressure and coronary heart disease .
According to statistics from the World Health Organization , seven to ten percent of the elderly population have depression problems ( Baidu , 2009 ) .
However , as psychology advances , elderly depression can be dealt with through psychological means .
Firstly , elderly depression could be prevented with psychological consultation .
For example , a qualified psychological consultant is able to offer an old person constructive suggestions on how to prevent depression such as , keeping a positive attitude towards aging , developing hobbies and participating in social activities which can activate the mind .
The consultant might also advise the children of the old person to keep the elderly company regularly and care more about them .
Elderly depression may be prevented from happening to old people with active minds and lots of emotional support .
Secondly , elderly depression could be treated with psychological treatment .
The means is more or less the same with the prevention means , but is more enhanced .
For instance , psychologists can address the importance of sports as appropriate amounts of sport can keep old people 's bodies and minds active .
At the same time , volunteers can play a part in helping as listeners .
Speaking out personal experiences and difficulties in life is a good way of letting go of negative thoughts for old people .
Current psychological development has functioned well in the two points and hence helps to ease the aging process .
Besides , promoting life-long learning has played a significant role in helping to ease the aging process .
Life-long learning is known as " lifelong , lifewide , voluntary , and self-motivated pursuit of knowledge for either personal or professional reasons .
" ( Wikipedia , 2009 ) .
It not only enhances personal development for the elderly , but also equips them with knowledge to compete in employment .
As an old saying puts it , it is
By continuous self learning , the elderly are able to refresh their minds and keep up with the pace of time .
They could identify themselves in the new era better since they are capable of adapting themselves to an environment that is different from theirs with life-long learning .
After we stepped into an information age , a good command of computer use has become increasingly necessary for everyone .
If a grandfather knows how to surf the Internet , his life will be more colourful and meaningful because he has more opportunities for recreation and more access to information .
On the other hand , with life-long learning , the old are more competitive in the work force because they possess new knowledge needed in a new age and have profound working experience , which is an advantage over the young .
In " A Graying World " , Peter G. Peterson ( 2001 ) introduces six strategies for policy reforms to ease the aging process , one of which is to reduce elderly dependency by encouraging later retirement .
Once the elderly become more competitive in employment , it is easier for them to choose late retirement .
As a result , the aging problem can be eased .
However , one might propose that psychology development has brought about ageism , which involves prejudicial attitudes to the
Nevertheless , although the term was coined with the development of psychology , it is not psychological development that breeds ageism .
On the contrary , psychological development has helped to eliminate ageism ,
With the aid of psychology , people could gain a better understanding of aging , which is a natural phenomenon , and appreciate the elderly more .
It is the old who have contributed to our society a lot .
Psychological development has provided the right view of aging , helping to eliminate ageism and ease the aging process .
In conclusion , elderly depression problems are becoming less severe with the help of psychological consultation and treatment , life-long learning has been promoted by psychological development to equip the elderly better for employment , and ageism is somewhat eliminated by correct psychological perspective .
Current psychological research and development have helped to ease the aging process to a large extent .
