Revival of nuclear reactor , molten salt reactor
On 26th April 1986 , a severe reactor 's meltdown occurred in Chernobyl nuclear plant , Ukraine which released more radioactivity compared to the time when atom bombs were dropped on Hiroshima and Nagasaki .
In the accident , 56 people were killed and about 600000 people were exposed to significant levels of radiation ( Greenpeace , Jan2009 , ) .
This accident is considered as the worst nuclear disaster in the world .
As the result , many people are afraid of nuclear power even until today .
Hence , most people oppose the revival of nuclear reactor while support the renewable power such as solar power and wind power .
Although there are a lot of opposition to the reborn of nuclear power ; there is some evidence which show that the potential benefits of molten salt reactor ( MSR ) far outweigh its dangers .
Opponents of nuclear power claim that nuclear reactors are totally insecure as the incidents of Three Miles Island and Chernobyl led to catastrophes .
Another example was the technical failure in the Forsmark nuclear power plant in Sweden , 2006 .
According to the former director of that plant , it was pure luck that the plant had no meltdown ; otherwise , it could be another disaster ( Greenpeace , Jan2009 ,
However , the possibility for a MSR to melt is relatively small compared to the old nuclear power plant .
This is because molten salt reactor has different safety approaches which can prevent the meltdown .
Firstly , the molten salts have low chemical activity at sea-level pressure .
They are also mechanically stable as their boiling point is very high .
Besides that , there is a passive cooling system which includes passively cooled dump tanks that will perform emergency cooling and shutdown in any emergency conditions ( Forsberg , C.F , June2006 , ) .
Moreover , in a MSR , the mobile fission products are removed continuously and reused .
This means that the accident rate can be reduced to the minimum .
Opponents also mention that there is no solution to radioactive waste .
Since the beginning of nuclear power , radioactive waste has remained a major problem .
Reprocessing the radioactive waste once became a useful method .
However , according to a study published in 2001 , there was a significant increment of leukaemia among under-25 year olds who were living within 10 km of La Hague nuclear reprocessing plants , in northwest France ( Greenpeace , Jan2009 , ) .
Yet , reprocessing the radioactive waste and recycling the salts seem to be possible in MSR .
In fact , MSR would still produce hazardous waste and radionuclide .
Nevertheless , the organic components in that waste would be oxidized in the molten salt oxidizer ( MSO ) and radionuclide would be retained in the salt .
The salt would then be recycled and reused in the MSR ( Gat , U. , Jun1993 , p.3 ) .
Some of the radionuclide is still left out in this recycling process .
In order to get a shorter-lived radioactivity , the radionuclide is combined with some mixtures such as glass , ceramic and concrete .
Hence , the radioactive waste is brought to an optimum for disposal and lesser harmful radioactive waste is produced by MSR .
The final argument advanced by opponents of nuclear power is that nuclear energy is too expensive .
Still , a molten salt reactor is worth its price .
Through research , a molten salt reference plant can produce power up to 1000MWe which is very efficient .
This amount of power produced is enough to outweigh other energy sources as it can cover the increased energy needs in the future .
Moreover , the system of circulating molten salt fuel mixture can reduce the operation cost considerably which provide MSR another advantage
( . Besides that , MSR has a lower construction cost as it is smaller compared to other types of nuclear reactors .
This is because MSR system offers an integrated fuel cycle and embodies a breeder reactor concept .

In conclusion , though many people are still opposing the concept of reactor generation IV , I believe that MSR could bring the nuclear power to another new age .
MSR has many advantages such being cost-effective , minimize the danger of disposal and it has a nearly perfect safety precaution which reduce accident rates greatly .
Hence , it has the potential to become the main source of energy in the next decade .
