In view of today 's environmental problems of global warming , there is an increasing necessity to introduce a clean , safe and efficient alternative energy source .
Although the nuclear power plant is considered safer and cleaner than fossil power plants , the devastating consequences of its occasional meltdowns deter the general public and policy makers from accepting it .
However , the development of technology has resulted in a continuous evolution of nuclear energy systems .
One of the latest prototypes of generation IV nuclear reactor is the Lead Cooled fast reactor ( LFR ) .
Unlike the previous generations of nuclear reactors which are constantly critiqued by opponents , the LFR is considered to be not only safer in different aspects , but also more sustainable and economical .
The most criticisms towards nuclear power generators arise from their safety issues .
The memories of the 1979 reactor meltdown at Three Mile Island made the US government hesitate to order new nuclear power plants ( Nature , 2004 ) .
Most opponents claim that although rare , nuclear plant accidents are too catastrophic and should not be encouraged for power generation .
An example will be the 1986 core explosion at Chernobyl in Ukraine , in which 31 people were killed immediately and many more after years because of radioactive contamination .
However , good heat transmission of lead used for the LFR ensures low likelihood of core damage .
This in turn minimizes potential risks such as core meltdowns .
Also Lead 's low vapor pressure lowers the chances of core explosion and its high shielding capability of gamma radiations minimizes potential off-site radioactive contamination (
All these factors reflect the LFR as a more reliable future nuclear power generator .
Since the 911 incident , there have been concerns about the unimaginable consequences of terrorist attacks on nuclear plants .
However , the LFR has made improvements on its physical structure to minimize physical damage from external attacks .
For example , the reactor uses independent , redundant and diversified Decay Heat Removal ( DHR ) loops to control damages and prevent potential radioactive releases ( World Nuclear Association , 2008 ) .
There is no flammable or reactive coolant materials used to ensure that no big scale explosion occurs when being attacked .
In fact , various studies have shown that nuclear power plants can withstand such attacks better than almost any other civil constructions ( World Nuclear Association , 2009 ) .
The physical protection promises top security of building nuclear power plants like the LFR .
Despite the safety issues , opponents also assert that the government should discourage nuclear power plants because of the high cost incurred to construct them .
However , most of these criticisms arise from a lack of foresight .
While it is true that its first time investment of fuel and capital can be more expensive than that of a coal power plant , the plant sustainability and efficiency should also be taken into consideration .
Studies have shown that the average cost of a nuclear plant is about $ 30 per Megawatt-hour which is only slightly higher than $ 29.1 per Megawatt-hour of a coal plant
The LFR maintains this economic competitiveness as lead is an inexpensive coolant and with long refueling cycle .
Moreover , supercritical water is used in the reactor to increase the overall efficiency of the nuclear plant .
Considering the efficiency , sustainability , and environmental friendliness of a nuclear power plant , these benefits far outweighs the small economic disadvantages
Thus , the LFR can be the best alternative to replace coal power generators .
While the benefits of the LFR are largely acknowledged , its limitations and potential risks should also be recognized .
For example , as corrosion of lead may take place under high temperature , the LFR only works under 550 , which in turn limits its overall efficiency .
Also , operation of nuclear plant should be closely regulated to prevent any abuse use of nuclear materials .
This requires a concerted effort from countries around the world .
In fact , such regulatory agreements already exist .
An example will be the International Atomic Energy Agency 's ( IAEA ) safeguards system under the Nuclear Non-proliferation Treaty ( NPT ) .
Nuclear power plants are gaining importance in the world as they help many countries , such as France , to maintain power independence .
Yet the non-nuclear weapon states should be monitored to prevent any undeclared nuclear activities .
In conclusion , the LFR helps enhance safety of nuclear power stations while not compromising economic factors .
Though it may not be the optimal design because of its potential risks and limitations , the LFR is still one of the possible future energy plants .
After all , we should expect the nuclear industry to dominate in generating world 's electricity in the future as technology matures .
Nowadays , with the increasing population of the society , the limited resources can not meet the large amount of demand of energy .
In order to overcome the energy shortage situation today , human beings have tried many ways to explore new kinds of energy , for instance , natural energy which includes wind energy and water energy .
However , the consequence is not that satisfactory , due to its low efficiency and high cost .
It seems a perfect solution to the bad situation nowadays , however , the use of nuclear energy becomes a controversial issue which causes fierce discussion among not only scientists , but also publics .
In my point of view , using nuclear energy is the right way to meet today 's increasing energy demand , due to its high efficiency and environmental emission .
There are several disadvantages of using nuclear energy : The funds paid on developing this technology is high , the time taking to explore the technology is long and there exists dangers which can actually be solved .
First of all , some opponents may think that it will cost large amount of funds to develop this technology .
However , if we take all conditions into consideration , we may find that the argument is totally wrong .
Firstly , the fuel cost for a nuclear plant is only a third for a coal-fired plant in producing the same amount of electricity .
Due to this issue , we can save a lot of resources for our future .
Secondly , if we do not use nuclear energy , it will cause a serious shortage of fuel , which will lead to the increase the price of electricity .
For example , in European countries , " the price of electricity from coal will double and that from gas will increase 30 % " ( World Nuclear Association , 2009 ) .
The above data shows that if we use nuclear energy , it will at least save 50 % cost , and this 50 % implies saving a lot of funds as it is commonly known that the funds used for producing electricity is quite large .
Thirdly , if we keep using normal fuel energy instead of nuclear energy , it will weaken the quality of the gas , since it will emit green house gases . In order to deal with global warming , governments will pay a lot of money .
However , if we use nuclear energy , we will not have this kind of worry due to its non-green-house-gas emission .
In conclusion , using nuclear energy can actually save a lot of funds .
In addition , some opponents may argue that it will take a long time to explore this technology .
Here it is suitable to make an assumption . If the time used to explore this technology is fixed , according to the conclusion reached in the previous paragraph , it is easy to know that if we explore the nuclear energy earlier , we can save more money and save more resources .
Moreover , human beings now can not find a kind of ideal energy to replace nuclear energy . which means the use of nuclear energy is just a matter of time .
So in conclusion , it is better to explore nuclear energy as soon as possible .
Besides the above two factors , some opponents may believe that it is dangerous to use nuclear energy .
We use Very-High-Temperature-Reactors ( VHTR ) , which is one of Generation IV reactor concepts , as an example .
Due to the special design of its Helium Coolant , Graphite Reactor Core and temperature controlled system , the danger can be greatly reduced .
It is true that dangers still exist , however , with the development of the technology , it is desirable that those dangers could be overcome .
To sum up , the Generation IV reactors is a trend of the 21st century . It will make a great improvement and progress for our life .
with the increasing demand of energy , only nuclear energy is the correct choice as it has so many advantages as compared with other kinds of energies .
Its high efficiency is the most attractive . The environmental emission makes it better for human beings .
Even though there are shortages that still exist , it is believed that with the development of the technology , all the problems will be solved and all the difficulties can be overcome .
