Design process is a linear sequence of events which was started by creative human act and ended with an invention of a new product .
It is also a kind of planning on how to apply the knowledge to the making of an object or a system .
Psychology is the characteristics of mental states and the science of human behavior .
It plays an important role in every human attempt in design processes .
( { http : //dictionary.reference.com/browse/psychology ? o = 100074 } [ HYPERLINK : http : //dictionary.reference.com/browse/psychology ? o = 100074 ] ) .
There is a relationship between psychology and design process which can prevent accidents from happening .
Design errors affect the safety of a product .
Unless the prevention method has been well-planned , one will not know about the shortcoming of a product until an accident happens .
Here is an example of a real major industrial accident . The world 's deadliest high-speed train accident , which occurred on 3rd June 1998 , in Eschede , Germany .
It was caused by a single fatigue crack in one wheel which derailed the train when the wheel failed .
The steel tire on the wheel broke and peeled away from the wheel , penetrating into the floor of the train .
This resulted in the vibration of the train .
The embedded metal was noticed by a passenger in the coach .
He quickly informed the conductor of the train but the conductor was procrastinating by investigating the case himself before stopping the train .
The train was totally damaged after hitting a bridge support .
The proximate causes were the disintegration of the wheel rim and the failure to stop the train after the wheel had delaminated .
Flawed emergency operating procedures were the contributing cause of this disaster .
( { http : //pbma.nasa.gov/docs/public/pbma/images/msm/derailed.pdf } [ HYPERLINK : http : //pbma.nasa.gov/docs/public/pbma/images/msm/derailed.pdf ] , { http : //www.youtube.com/watch ? v = p_KLA2LMIeA } [ HYPERLINK : http : //www.youtube.com/watch ? v = p_KLA2LMIeA ] , { http : //www.5min.com/Video/The-Eschede-Train-Disaster-in-Eschede-Germany-119997168 } [ HYPERLINK : http : //www.5min.com/Video/The-Eschede-Train-Disaster-in-Eschede-Germany-119997168 ] )
Failure avoidance and effective process and production control of complex systems determine the safety as well as the reliability of the system .
From the major accident discussed , it proves that the actual causes of an accident are the failures on the component of the system , individual action which is incorrect , team work activities that are incomplete and dysfunctional relations within the organizations as well as the extra organizational environment .
In the train accident above , the metal fatigue of the wheel was the component failure of the train .
If the wheel did not crack , no metal would have been embedded into the train and the derailment of the train would not have happened .
However , this accident was not just because of this single component failure .
Frequent maintenance of the wheel can help to prevent the wheel failure from occurring .
Beyond this point , human error plays an important role in initiating accidents .
Other than that , if the train had been stopped immediately when the wheel had disintegrated , the disaster might not have occurred and countless lives would have been saved .
Unfortunately , no one pulled the emergency brake during the emergency condition .
All these show that decision-making and human action played an important part in the cause of the accident besides component failure .
If the conductor decided to stop the train by pulling the emergency brake immediately, .
Design errors in socio-technical system have really made a significant difference in their reliability and safe operation .
Researches from the nuclear and chemical industry show that 20 % to 50 % of accidents and failures involve errors in design .
Moreover , since design errors are always corrected before they are involved in these incidents , the real percentage is actually much higher .
If corrective action is taken after an incident , it entails either the redesigning of the operational processes or the installation of another barrier .
These are feedback controls of safety .
They are just add-ons to the system .
However , it is better to use the path of feed-forward control of , , to do a correct original system design right from the beginning .
To improve design safety , a scientist is needed .
This person can help to analyze the future requirements of the system and to improve accident prevention .
Apart from this , a scientist may also be called upon to help evaluate the prototype by using simulation techniques .
It is necessary to introduce add-ons as all possible design errors will not be discovered until the system is used .

In conclusion , an accident is never caused by a single component failure or a single human error .
Psychology plays an essential role in design processes .
The role of humans in safeguarding complicated socio-technical systems can not be neglected .
If the psychology factor is not considered in design processes , accidents may happen easily .
Hence , psychological inputs should be incorporated in design processes .
Can Engineering Accidents be Solved by Engineering Psychology ?
" The reasonable person adapts himself to the world : the unreasonable one persists in trying to adapt the world to himself .
Therefore , all progress depends upon the unreasonable person .
" ( ) .
This sentence indicates why engineering psychology will become closer and closer to our life .
What is engineering psychology ?
Generally speaking , engineering psychology is concerned with adapting equipment and environment to people ( Blum , 1952 ) .
This adjustment is based on people 's psychological capacities and limitations , and the aim of it is to improve the overall system performance .
The conception of engineering psychology was first brought out during the First World War , when people found that the efficiency of machines was reduced sharply when they were operated by women instead of men ( these machines were designed for men and not women ) .
Since then people began to realize that sometimes the engineering problem was related to equipment design rather than the people who operate or other mechanical reasons .
However it is hard to say whether we can solve the engineering problems by simply improving the psychological problems , since for many engineering incidences the technical problems had occupied an overwhelming part .
Hence in this essay I will argue about the proportion of psychological problems and technological problems during engineering incidences and give a conclusion from my own view .
Based on the report provided by Reason ( 1990 ) , 92 % of all nuclear utility accidents between 1983-1984 were caused by people and only 8 % of them were cause by control room operators .
For instance , there were two serious incidences which are cited frequently in technical literature .
They happened in Three Mile Island and Chernobyl .
The failure for the first one included operators who were unprepared to handle serious accident due to the lack of training . Complex and confusing operating procedures led to the operators ' incorrect action . There were problem within the Nuclear Regulatory Commission .
None of these deficiencies explain the basic causes in terms of the 'operating error' .
Moreover Reason ( 1987 ) suggests two main reasons for this kind of incidence in his own report for Chernobyl .
The first factor relates to people 's misunderstanding of effects of their actions on the whole system . The second factor is a kind of persistent action which is made by a small and cohesive group in the process of pursuing an unsuitable aim .
What is the most important evidence for his theories is that after realizing these engineering psychology problems , quite a lot of America 's nuclear institutes began to train their staff in a psychology-related way , which indeed prevented the nuclear accidents from happening again till now .
However the operator errors during these two nuclear accidents can not be ignored .
Although there is nuclear incidences have not happened in recent years , it is too biased to say that the engineering psychology can solve the problems by itself .
One saying about the cause of Chernobyl disaster is the problem in peculiarities of physics and the construction of the reactor ( ) .
Firstly , the Chernobyl RBMK-1000 reactor got a dangerous positive void coefficient .
This makes RBMK reactor to be very unstable at lower power level .
Secondly the control rod of RBMK reactor is 1.3 meters shorter than necessary , which led to an abnormal decrease of reactor output power .
These problems definitely can not be solved from psychological view since even we had solved all human-related problems , these defects of system are still vital .
However , the human-factor has again been considered as the main cause to the reactor design by IAEA 's 1986 analysis ( ) .
It seems that the boundary between the technological problem and psychological problem is very vague .
To sum up we can conclude from these two aspects that the human factors and the technical factor are connected and have both played a role in the accident .
To simply solve one of them will contribute nothing to the problem .
Engineering accidents are not always caused by technical problems and the issue of engineering psychology will become hotter and hotter with the development of technology in the area of advanced transportation , co-operative work , teleworking , health , pollution and leisure .
