The importance of psychology for design engineer
As more engineers feel stressful from their high workload , a psychologist plays an important role in their work .
Most engineers only care about how to apply technology into practice , but they seldom care about how to make products that can be used easily .
Designing products should include psychological factors for consumers and operators .
An inadequate industrial design may lead to catastrophic consequences
( Bernhard , 2006 . Many people argue that psychology is non-related with engineering design ; companies do not need to spend extra money on the unnecessary outcome .
But I consider psychology as the requisite factor for engineering work .
Human error has been recognized as the main reason for industry accidents ; psychology can prevent human error
Some managers are against employing psychologists because they must spend extra money on psychologists ' salaries .
If 3 psycholists serve the whole company , every psychologist can get 4000 Singapore dollars per month , and then three psychologists will get 144000 Singapore dollars from their company for one year .
The amount is a large amount .
The three Mile Island accident was the result of human error and design problems ( ) .
The whole factory was in ruins , all the residents living in the villages close to the Three Mile Island had to move away .
It is more expensive than S $ 144000 , and thousands of lives were threatened .
People who do not agree that psychology is useful in engineer work demonstrate the purpose of engineering design .
The engineering design is to apply technologies to help people solve problems .
The issue of how to attract consumers is not the business of engineers .
Furthermore , they think the job of design engineer is to build factory structure and to operate something that belongs to operators .
It sounds correct to some extent .
, engineers must consider safe factors when they design the structure
If the arrangements of products and instructions are incomprehensible and complicated , purchasers will be confused when using these gadgets
( Bernhard , 2006 . If people do not like using the product , the product is a failure .
Design engineers always overestimate the ability of users ; the design may not give sufficient help to operators
( Bernhard , 2006 . Three Mile Island 's tragic consequence was caused by inadequate structure design .
When the radioactive gas and coolant leaked , the valve should have been closed immediately in order to prevent radioactive materials draining away .
The operator thought that the valve has been closed , but there was no instrument showing the position of the valve
( . Then this accident happened .
If designers had designed an instrument to show the process of cooling circuit , then operators would have known that the valve had not been closed , and this disaster would have been prevented .
People who opposite views insist that psychologists can help engineers release their high working pressures .
They forget that counseling fee is very expensive ; engineers usually do not look for psychologists by themselves .
The work efficiency is different when people work with different feelings .
People can not have an active attitude when they are under high pressure .
Psychology can help them have an active and optimistic attitude towards work .
Psychology is important to engineering work ; company employers should employ some psychologists for their workers .
Psychology has prevented accidents to some extent . It has guaranteed the workers ' mental health .
Incorporate the Psychological factors when they designing products is convenient for purchasers to use .
Furthermore , psychologists can persuade engineers to have good attitude towards their work and help engineers to release their pressure .
