Title : Should countries support further research and development funding for Very-High-Temperature Reactors ?
The world 's demand for energy has increased drastically over the last few decades .
As fossil fuels and natural gas are depleting quickly , nuclear energy has emerged as a vital and strategic energy source in the world 's future energy supply market .
The demand for nuclear energy has led to the initiative of developing Generation IV nuclear reactors guided by the Generation IV International Forum ( GIF ) .
Among the six prototypes of nuclear reactors designed , the very-high-temperature reactor ( VHTR ) is one of the most promising candidates proposed in the GIF
( Umeda , 2008 . However , many people strongly oppose this new prototype due to their inherent fear about nuclear plants .
Nonetheless , the VHTR is claimed to not only offer high-efficient electricity production but is also designed to be safer higher security against nuclear weapons .
Thesis
Opponents of the VHTR have argued that developing heat-resistant materials for the VHTR is a challenge unlikely to be overcome .
However , the basic technology of producing heat-resistant materials has long been well established in former High Temperature Gas Reactors plants , such as the US Fort Saint Vrain and Peach Bottom prototypes .
. Moreover , this technology has been furthermore improved to meet higher temperature requirement .
For example , Japan 's Atomic Energy Research Institute based in Kashiwa has already operated a similar reactor as the VHTR which is able to reach a record high temperature of 950 Degree Celsius in 2004
( Butler , 2004 . Therefore , developing materials that resist high temperatures is no longer a problem for building the VHTR .
In fact , the VHTR has the highest technical feasibility amongst the six prototypes so far .
TS
Opponents are also worried about the difficulty in controlling the temperature of the VHTR in the event of an accident .
Vivid in people 's minds is the partial reactor meltdown in 1979 at Three Mile Island , Pennsylvania .
Opponents argue that the VHTR 's very high operating temperature may lead to similar accidents due to reactor meltdown if it were to be built .
However , the opponents are probably unaware of the safety measures specially designed for the VHTR .
The core of the VHTR with multiple protection layers inside is able to withstand heat at temperatures up to 1600 ° C without cracking .
Even in the case of core cracking down , there is also a backup system in place .
Heat can be conducted from the core through air-cooled panels so that the core can be cooled down in a few seconds .
( Rachael Elder & Ray Allen , 2008 ) Thus the VHTR will be a very safe prototype given its multiple protection layers and effective backup system .
TS
Another reason why people oppose the VHTR is that its waste is not reprocessed , hence a growing amount of resources are required to store the waste .
However , not reprocessing the waste ensures no production of plutonium , which is a by-product in the processing , and it can be used to make nuclear weapons .
Moreover , waste reprocessing is expensive and fuel consuming as it requires continuous burning of the wastes
( Declan , 2004 . Therefore , the benefits of not reprocessing the waste overweigh the costs of storing the waste .
TS
In addition , the VHTR is a highly efficient reactor .
TS Very high gas temperatures can be achieved ( 900-1000 ° C ) within the VHTR to separate hydrogen gas efficiently , thus it offers highly efficient electricity generation
( . It can produce 50 % more electricity from the same amount of fuel compared to conventional nuclear plants .
( Butler , 2004 )
In conclusion , the VHTR is highly feasible , safe and efficient .
Though the danger of nuclear reactors can never be completely avoided , the VHTR may offer the best solution to the increasingly sever energy shortage .
Therefore , countries should support further research and development funding for the very-high-temperature reactor .
On July 17 , 1981 in Kansas City , Missouri , United States , The Hyatt Regency walkway collapse killed 114 people and injured more than 200 others during a tea dance .
It was one of the deadliest structural collapses in U.S. history
( Martin , 1981 . The accident was caused by the lack of communication between the designers and the constructors .
Although it may not be possible to avoid all accidents from happening , we can take some measures to decrease the possibility of risks .
The involvement of psychology during engineering processing is a helpful and practicable measure .
It can lower the possibility of accidents that are caused by human factors .
In the case of walkway collapse , it can be estimated that if psychology was applied during the structural processing , the collapse would have been avoided .
The design and construction of building are regarded as the work of engineers and irrelevant with psychology .
However , people are likely to make mistakes in every aspect in life , including engineering processing .
Lots of accidents are caused by human factors rather than technical problems or financial liability .
Previous research finds that about 90 percent of engineering accidents are due to human errors
( Gordon & Flin , 2001 . Hence , psychology , a human science which studies human 's mental processes and behaviors can help to decrease the mistakes caused by human factors
( . To further explain it , psychology can be used to analyse the man-made reasons which causes errors , such as engineers ' attitudes , habits and social ability .
After that we can obtain some strategies from the analysis and utilize them in the engineering processing to prevent accidents from happening .
In the Hyatt Regency walkway collapse , the design was modified halfway , which was thought as a small trivial by both the designers and the constructors .
They believed that the party had rechecked the details , while in fact nobody did before construction .
Therefore it can be expected that if psychology was involved during the construction , this tragedy caused by lack of responsibility would not have occurred at all !
Some opponents argue that it is a " wise after event " or just an imagination to use psychology during engineering processing , for it is hard to combine abstract psychology with concrete engineering processing .
However , as a branch of today 's applied psychology , psychology in industrial safety is quite practical and convenient to conduct .
What needs to be done is to organize some training sessions which can make the engineers more skillful , or some meetings that cover the common mistakes in engineering processing which embed the awareness of safety in people 's mind.
Furthermore , there could also be some encouraging activities which help to build the engineers ' loyalty towards their companies and help them to realize their importance in the companies .
Study has proved that when employees feel they are valued during a mission , they tend to be more responsible and as a result , the safety and quantity of production are greatly improved
( Kelley , 1996 . As for the collapse accident , if somebody had been responsible and rechecked the design , it could have been avoided .
To summarize , If psychology was involved in the building of Hyatt Regency walkway collapse , which was a practicable measure , this unfortunate accident would have been eliminated at the very beginning .
