Nuclear power is a great discovery in human history .
Nowadays , nuclear technology is widely used as an extra resource for electric generators .
It is clean and stable .
Many people believe that nuclear power plant will take the place of our traditional electric generators in the future .
However , people do n't realize that there will be many problems caused by using nuclear technology , in terms of environment , cost , and nature resources .
As a big breakthrough , nuclear power was discovered by two Germany scientists , Otto Hahn and Fritz Stresemannin 1938 .
They found that , when they used a neutron to collide with another heavy nuclear , the nuclear broke into two parts and there was some mass lost .
The lost mass generates what we call " atomic energy " , as square of light speed times as the lost mass .
After that , the atomic bomb came up , which led to end of the World War II .
Actually , the reason why atomic bomb killed so many people is not the explosion itself . it is the radiation generated by the Uranium and chain reaction .
The radiation will not dissipate within 100 years .
When people began to use controlled chain reaction , they were really concerned about the radiation and the impact on environment .
From early 1960s to 1980s there were several anti-nuclear movements in United Sates , which showed people 's concern about the nuclear power .

Although the Atomic Energy Commission had advocated for peaceful uses of nuclear power since the development of a atomic bomb , people were still worried about that .
Although we can not say it is safe enough to use nuclear power , Uranium is really a clean and cheap resource compared to coal and oil .
First , it wo n't give off carbon dioxide and sulphur dioxide , which has a positive impact on our environment .
We are really worried about the Green house gases now , there is data to show that every year the temperature globally increases from 0.2 to 0.3 degree Celsius .
So , it is very effective to use Uranium to stop the Green house gases .
Second , the cost of purifying Uranium and getting coal which generate the same amount of energy is almost the same .
It is means that the cost is acceptable .
Pure Uranium is easy to transport , because only 1 ton of Uranium will use the same energy as burning 5000tons of coal .
So , many countries , including U.S , China , Russia , France , U.K and Japan , have begun to use Uranium .
In the twentieth century , the safety of using Uranium is still under discussion .
A few accidents have happened during the Uranium 's purification and reaction process .
Our human ability is limited .
We can not say that we have fully controlled the nuclear reaction process , but it now can be controlled and react at a peaceful rate .
What our government is happy to hear is that , Uranium is still enough to support us for hundreds of years , although it is hard to be purified .
There are many Uranium mines existing underground .
Nuclear power plants first started in 1954 and proliferated rapidly due to its many advantages over conventional fossil-fuel plants .
Today , there are altogether 439 nuclear power reactors in operation throughout the world ( International Atomic Energy Agency [ IAEA ] , 2009 ) .
However in the 1970s , nuclear accidents at Three Mile Island and Chernobyl stirred up a big controversy over nuclear power and practically halted the development of nuclear power in many countries ( Butler , 2004 ) .
The argument is that the nuclear plants are a safety hazard to the country and is a probable target for terrorists .
In addition , environmental risks from nuclear waste and discovery of other renewable energy sources also contributed to the push for phasing out nuclear power which had lasted for several decades .
Lately , a number of new designs for nuclear power generation , known as Generation IV reactors , are the subject of active research and may lead to the revival of nuclear power in the future .
One such design is the SCWR which attempts to eliminate or reduce previously debated risks surrounding nuclear power .
While some may be skeptical on tapping nuclear power due to various issues , the new SCWR will alleviate their concerns if there is continual research and development funding for the design to materialize .
Critics believe that nuclear power is not safe as it poses a health risk to workers and the public due to low-level radiation from the plants .
They are also concerned that the new reactors will reenact the events leading to past disastrous nuclear accidents that had resulted in high fatality .
On the contrary , studies conducted by non-profit , neutral agencies have found no compelling evidence of a correlation between nuclear power and risk of cancer caused by exposure to high radiation level ( National Cancer Institute [ NCI ] , 1996 ) .
The studies done are based on comparing the number of cancer patients in the vicinity of nuclear power and non nuclear power settlements .
According to another report , nuclear power accidents have also caused fewer deaths than accidents related to other forms of energy ( World Nuclear Association , 2009 ) .
Besides that , the SCWR is also integrated with passive simplified safety system that can eliminate boiling crisis instances common in nuclear accidents ( Buongiorno , 2002 ) .
Hence , there is less reliance on sophisticated backup systems or experienced operators .
Less dependence on human will equate to lower risks as human error was a significant factor in most nuclear accidents ( Butler , 2004 ) .
In the event of an unlikely emergency , extensive evacuation plan and protective actions will be carried out and coordinated between governments and power plant officials ( N.S.NRC , 2008 ) .
One concern expressed by the public and governments is the vulnerability of plants to attack by terrorists as well as the usage of nuclear waste by product as a weapon .
Under the new SCWR power plant security blueprint , these concerns are well taken into consideration .
More patrols , stronger and more capable security forces , additional physical barriers , greater stand-off distances for vehicle checks , more restrictive site access controls were introduced to minimize security risks ( U.S.URC , 2008 ) .
The United Nations had also called upon the world leaders to improve security in order to prevent radioactive material from falling into the hands of terrorists .
There are also plans for a centralized , permanent , and secure waste repositories to be built and for security stationed along transportation routes to be increased ( BBC , 2003 ) .
Apart from the increase in nuclear plants ' security , enhanced scram system fitted in SCWR could shut down a reactor in less than 5 second severely deterring a terrorist force with any intention to release radioactivity ( Gonyeau , 2006 ) .
Lastly , the SCWR is also able to operate without having to depend on the much debated reprocessing of plutonium waste ( Butler , 2004 ) .
Opponents perceive costs and performance of nuclear reactors as inferior to conventional reactors .
It was pointed out that the costs of constructing a nuclear plant , decommissioning nuclear facilities and the costs of storing nuclear waste are expensive .
Materials needed for the plants are also either costly , rare or do not exist yet .
Moreover , much public subsidy funding and tax expenditures are consumed in nuclear research and development projects when they could be used to invest in alternative renewable energy technologies .
However , the SCWR will actually be economically viable .
Far simpler designs , with elimination of circulation pumps , pressurizers , steam generators , steam separators and dryers reduce its capital and building costs ( Butler , 2004 ) .
Additionally , the supercritical coolant has a high specific enthalpy and promises to deliver high thermal efficiencies of approximately 45 % versus the current 33 % of light water reactors ( Buongiorno , 2002 ) .
Combination of higher operating temperature which increases power output and low fuel utilization translates to cheaper energy .
The SCWR estimates are at $ 900/kWe and ¢ 2.9/kWh ( Buongiorno , 2002 ) which can be considered to meet the economic and sustainability requirements .
So despite its high initial capital cost and operation , nuclear power is still competitive with fossil fuel for electricity generation .
If the social , health and environmental costs are also taken into account , nuclear power plants will be exceedingly outstanding compared to fossil-fueled plants ( World Nuclear Association [ WNA ] , 2009 ) .
Finally , experts speculated that increasing scarcity of oil will drive oil prices up to $ 100 and $ 150 per barrel in the future ( Huffman , 2009 ) which will lead to an increase in energy prices for fossil-fueled power plants .
It is evident that in the long run , when energy cost for fossil-fueled plants increases continually , using nuclear power for electricity generation is much more economical .
To sum it all , SCWR can effectively meet the requirements of the modern globalised world while addressing all the various concerns .
It is specifically designed to be very safe and free from accidents .
Newer technology helps to increase energy security as well as produces cleaner energy .
Many security enhancements will also be put in place to protect the plants from potential terrorist threats .
In fact , SCWR is considered to be proliferation resistant .
In addition , it is categorised as a more efficient and cheaper energy source than conventional power technologies .
SCWR could indeed replace prevalent fossil-fuel reactors by economical standards .
With continual R&D funding for development , SCWR will become a reliable and bountiful source of power in the future .
