Support Further Research and Development Funding for Very-High-Temperature Reactor ( VHTR )
The development of nuclear power plant becomes more and more important as nuclear power is a more efficient and environment friendly source of energy .
From 1951 , when the first nuclear power plant generated electricity , the technology of nuclear power has become more efficient and safe .
The Very-High-Temperature Reactor ( VHTR ) is one of the most recent prototypes of the generation IV reactors .
VHTR is a graphite-moderated , helium-cooled reactor with a once-through uranium fuel cycle .
It supplies heat with high core outlet temperatures ( about 1000 ) which enables applications such as hydrogen production or process heat for the petrochemical industry or others .
( VR , 2007 ) Further research and development funding for VHTR should be supported by the governments or companies , because it is an efficient , secure and practicable technology , despite the worries raised by the opponents .
Many people consider nuclear power industry as highly dangerous since the radioactive fuels can be very harmful to our bodies and environment .
According to a survey conducted in Australia in 2009 on the public opinion on building nuclear power plants in Australia , there were 43 percent of the public opposing the plan because of the safety and security issues with nuclear power plants .
( Munro & Strong , 2009 ) However , nuclear power reactors are much safer and securer than most people can imagine even when the reactive temperature is very high .
Firstly , in VHTR , the fuel used is uranium dioxide in a TRISO configuration , where TRISO is the type of fuel that small amount of uranium dioxide is in the center and coated with four layers of three isotropic materials ( Olander , 2009 ) .
The TRISO particles are either dispersed in a pebble for the pebble bed design or molded into the hexagonal graphite blocks .
Such designs are able to slow down neutrons to control the nuclear chain reaction ; thus the reactivity can be controlled in a reasonable range and explosions can be prevented .
Secondly , because helium is used as coolant of VHTR , unexpected reactions can be prevented .
One reason is that helium is an inert gas , which hardly reacts with any material .
Additionally , exposing helium to radiation does not make it radioactive , unlike most other possible coolants , for example light water ; therefore it is a safer choice of coolant .
Moreover , since the reactor can only operate under a high temperature , in case of destructions by terrorism or other outside forces , the system will cool down and automatically stop the reaction .
This function ensures VHTR is very safe under attacks .
Therefore , VHTR is a very safe and secure prototype of the generation IV reactor .
Other than the safety issue , the efficiency of VHTR is also a concern for those who want to invest in the project .
A Molten salt reactor can burn 99 % of initial fuel , while VHTR can burn 65 % of its initial fuel , which is less than that of a molten salt reactor .
However , VHTR is very efficient compared with the conventional light-water reactor , which can only burn up 5 % of the initial amount ( n.f .
2008 ) .
VHTR is not only able to produce electrical power but also produce hydrogen via electrolysis of water at high temperature .
Besides generating energy , the energy generated from nuclear reaction can also be used in crude oil refining or metal production ( Ogawa , & VonLensa , 2002. ) .
In this sense , VHTR is efficient in use of energy .
Compared to a molten salt reactor , VHTR has a simpler design and this leads to another advantage which is its high feasibility .
One more factor that affects the funding of a project is the feasibility of the project in terms of techniques and cost .
VHTR seems to be the most feasible design in the IV generation reactor .
Firstly , similar prototypes such as HTR-10 have already been operated in China and Japan .
VHTR is just an update of High-Temperature Reactor ; therefore it is easier to build a system with the foundation of similar technology .
Secondly , there is no reprocessing in VHTR .
Although some people argue that this causes energy waste and produces radioactive waste , the lack of reprocessing reduces the cost of the power plant and makes it more affordable since the reprocessing is very expensive .
The elimination of reprocessing will not cause any problems .
That is because the burning of fuel in VHTR is very efficient ; thus the amount of waste is very little .
In addition , the radioactive waste can be stored underground .
Lastly , even though the initiation of a nuclear power plant requires about 1 billion US dollars , for the long term profit , this project is practicable .
This is because of the need of electricity of humans and the relatively low maintaining fees for VHTR .
Thus , in terms of feasibility , the VHTR is a better choice for further development .
In conclusion , VHTR should be chosen to proceed on for further research and development .
This is because of its relative high efficiency , high safety and practicability .
There is much research going on in U.S. , China and Japan to improve the Very-High-Temperature Reactors .
Optimistically , by about 2020 , the first commercial VHTR would be in operation .
