Supercritical water reactor could be further developed
People nowadays have fierce controversy over the use of nuclear power due to the appalling nuclear accidents which occurred at Three Mile island and Chernobyl , or even the recent nuclear accident at Sellafield , England .
These accidents destroy cities , take people 's lives and leave many deadly post-effects for future decades .
Then , why do people continue using nuclear power ?
In fact , nuclear power is the cheapest power people can produce ( The Virtual Nuclear Tourist , 2006 ) .
Therefore , safety becomes the main concern when people choose to continue using nuclear power .
A series of generation IV nuclear reactors are newly designed for better efficiency , in the meantime , they are also improved on safety issues .
Among all the reactors , supercritical water reactor ( SCWR ) is outstanding for its high thermal efficiency and also better reliability .
However , opponents argue that SCWR is not reliable since it has no prototype .
Moreover , SCWR is operating under very high temperature and pressure , which makes SCWR less likely to be further developed .
Even though SCWR has not been tested yet , it is proved to have less possibility of causing nuclear accidents as has happened before ; it is easier to implement compared to other generation VI reactors , and it has a relatively high thermal efficiency which makes its long-term cost relatively low .
Firstly , opponents may doubt the safety and reliability of SCWR .
This doubt arises from the lack of knowledge of the design of this reactor .
The nuclear accident at Chernobyl was mainly because the nuclear plant utilized positive void coefficient of reactivity , causing it impossible to stop the working process when things went wrong .
( Bodansky , 2004 ) On the contrary , SCWR uses negative void coefficient instead , which could effectively reduce the possibility of this kind of fatal accident ( U.S DOE 2002 ) .
Moreover , opponents may also argue that the notion of SCWR is rather a pure theory with no prototype , so that this reactor may not be as effective as stated .
This counter-argument is sensible but not totally true for SCWR .
Actually , the notion of SCWR is an add on of two current techonologies .
One is light water reactor ( LWR ) , which is currently under use all over the globe .
The other is supercritical fossil fuel fired boilers , which is also in use now ( Idaho National Laboratory , 2007 ) .
Therefore , it would be easier , safer and even more convincing to put SCWR into use under the guarantee of these practical experiences .
Thus , although SCWR has no prototype yet , it actually has some reliability for implementation .
Finally , SCWR has a higher thermal efficiency of 44 % compared to LWR of 33-35 % ( Baindur , 2008 ) .
However , opponents may point out that this high thermal efficiency is achieved at the expense of operating under very high temperature and pressure , which could increase its potential danger .
This concern is necessary but SCWR has overcome this issue .
The coolant in the SCWR system is supercritical water , which has very high specific heat , so that it is very effective acting as a coolant .
Besides , this system is simple to construct and control since only one phase of coolant is present throughout the process ( Generation IV International Forum , n.d. ) .
Therefore , the safety issue concerning high temperature and pressure is overcome to some extent .
To sum up , although there exists disagreement of the use of SCWR due to its issue of reliability and safety , SCWR is worthy for further research because it is based on two current technologies , which increases its reliability , and its design principle improves its thermal efficiency compared to LWR and reduce the possibility of causing nuclear accidents .
Hopefully , SCWR could be better improved on current problems in future development .
