Essentiality to develop VHTR
Nuclear technology has been around in the world for many decades .
Due to its huge energy production and no emission of carbon dioxide , many nuclear power plants have been built .
However , the controversy on the construction has been an issue since then .
People have been arguingg about the safety problems and the cost brought by these plants for a long time .
Despite the controversy , the nuclear power plants still find their way back onto the table .
During Generation IV International Forum , the concept of Very-high-temperature reactor ( VHTR ) was raised . It is more efficient than the previous ones .
( Bulter , 2004 ) .
From my perspective , it is very meaningful to research on this , through which we can build more efficient and safer reactors so that the energy problem can be solved to a great extent .
First of all , the biggest advantage of VHTR over othert reactors is that it not only generates electricity but also Hydrogen .
The generation of Hydrogen brings about two improvements of the reactors .
The first one is that the efficiency of the conversion of the heat generated by nuclear fission increses a lot .
In other words , the heat is more fully used .
The other one is that the Hydrogen provides a good fuel to substitute petrol .
The Hydrogen powered cars remain the combustible engine .
Unlike elctrical cars ' battery engine which needs more time to be fully charged , the Hydrogen powered cars need much less time to be filled with hydrogen fuel .
Apart from this , the hydrogen fuel has higher combustion energy and lighter weight .
Acoording to scientific measurement , the energy generated by per unit hydrogen is about 2.6 times greater than fossil fuel .
( Hydrogen , 1995 ) Moreover , there are four realities suggesting that the current energy system is not sustainable .
The growing energy demand , the tense political situation caused , too much emission of carbon dioxide and the susceptible third world economies all point out this unstainbilty .
( A sustainable energy economy , 2007 ) .
Things must be done to change this energy system .
Some opponents will say that a large sum of money may be spent on the research and be pessimistic about the result .
However , the cost is what we should not consider .
According to an American report , USA spent about 25 billion dollars only on the oil report last year .
( Reducing America 's oil dependence,2008 ) .
That is to say about 385 dollars tax will be imposed on every person in America .
Comparing to the huge cost , the money spent in the research is negligible .
What is more , we should look at the problem over the long term .
We must know clearly about the benefit VHTR will bring to us once the research is successfully done .
Henceforth , our energy supply can be guaranteed .
Safety may be the most controversial point .
Indeed , we can never deny that nuclear power is dangerous .
However , we can not discontinue the research on the VHTR just because it is dangerous .
Actually , in our modern world , many beautiful things are dangerous .
We enjoy the excitement brought by the roller coaster and the convenience and the enjoyment brought by cars .
They all have dangerous .
Accoding to car crash states in America in 2005 , there were nearly 6,420,000 auto accidents and about 40,000 people were killed .
( Car accident statistics , 2005 ) .
However , we never forbid people from driving cars .
Instead , we make traffic rules to make drivers drive more carefully to avoid accidents .
Similarly , although we know the nuclear energy is too huge to be safe , the unstainable energy system forces us to make full use of it .
And because we know very clearly that it is dangerous , we devote very much effort to monitor the whole process in case accidents happen .
Hence , we can feel safe to use the electricity and drive cars powered by Hydrogen which is supplied by VHTR .
In conclusion , energy is the key to keeping our society and economic development sustainable .
So far , the nuclear reactor especially VHTR maybe the best choice to supply the energy .
Undeniably , nuclear power is always dangerous .
However , we must realize that the probability is very low and many measures have been taken to guarantee the security .
Thus , it is essential to do research on VHTR and it will deserve the effort and the funds we spend in the future .
