VHTR of Nuclear Power
Nowadays , people 's hearts are dragged by the price of petroleum .
As the consequence of the decreasing source of oil , people have turned to find other sources to replace petroleum .
Nuclear power became one of their choices , since it is clean and efficient .
Nuclear energy is defined as the energy coming from the nucleus of atoms due to the " nuclear fission , nuclear fusion , or radioactive decay " CITATION The05 \ l 2052 ( The American Heritage Science Dictionary , 2005 ) .
People change the energy release from bonds between atoms to electricity .
However , some accidents , like the reactor core exploding and 31 people dying in 1986 , scared many people ( Butler , 2004 ) .
Nevertheless , the new generation of reactor would make the process more efficient by using higher temperature , and there will be no waste to the outside world .
I think that Very-high-temperature-reactors ( VHTR ) will become the most popular in the future , since there are lots of advantages .
In this essay I will talk about VHTR concept through three aspects : safety , economic problems , and technology requirement to support my stance .
First of all , people who do not support the development of nuclear power are worried about the safety during its processing .
The Chernobyl accident gave people a big shock .
However , I think that people should not judge things by their own view .
For example , even though the accident rate of trains is much higher than that of airplanes , many people are still afraid of travelling by air .
There are two major safety problems of building nuclear plants .
First , the radioactivity released from the reactor core will harm public health .
Comparing to the other five generation concept , the waste in VHTR will go directly to repository so that we would not worry about the radiation .
Second , the big accident during the reactor processing will destroy " capital assets " , and people will lose confidence in nuclear power research CITATION The03 \ l 2052 ( The Future of Nuclear Power , 2003 ) .
It seems that VHTR might be very dangerous since it needs high temperature and high pressure .
However , the " inherent safety features of the fuel and reactor " make VHTR more reliable CITATION SMM03 \ l 2052 ( Modro , 2003 ) .
In short , VHTR has good safety conttrol .
Secondly , some people may think that nuclear reactors will require a lot of money to build and need high technology equipment .
The VHTR will require large amounts of money to be spent on special materials that can provide high temperature and high pressure .
However , in the long run , nuclear factories will produce more profit than other reactor concepts .
At first , since the VHTR has been arrange in to a direct cycle , it will save much money to build a waste recycler .
Second , the high efficiency up to 50 % , which is the highest among six generation IV reactor concepts , will bring a lot of profit to the factory .
Last but not least , VHTR will not only produce electricity but also hydrogen .
Therefore , we can get a lot of benefits through VHTR .
Besides the safety and economic issues , some people are worried about the performance of nucleus reactors .
The VHTR includes graphite-moderated process , helium-cooled reactor and uranium fuel cycle CITATION VHT09 \ l 2052 ( VHTR , 2009 ) .
It increases the temperature to 1000 degree by using " high core outlet temperature " .
This high-efficiency system is wildly used in the " high-temperature , energy-intensive and non-electric processes " .
Even though VHTR still needs further research in heat-resistant fuels and materials , it has developed fast though early cold fast neutron reactor and Pebble Bed Modular Reactor .
Considering the large economic benefit VHTR can bring , governments tend to put it as top priority .
It is predicted that this system can be performed by 2020 .
In conclusion , VHTR has a high-efficiency system that can produce electricity and hydrogen , and it has a high rank of safety .
With the effort that the scientists and the engineers put into development of nuclear power , I believe that nuclear power will supplant the fossil-fuel and become a major power in our daily life .
