Very-High-Temperature Reactor
Nuclear power generation emits relatively low amounts of carbon dioxide and its contribution to global warming is therefore relatively smaller .
Moreover , the technology is readily available ( especially for the generation III reactors , to which category many of the current reactors belong ) and new theories and technologies are being researched and developed .
Thus , nuclear power generation is definitely one of the solutions to the energy challenge that mankind is facing now .
According to European Nuclear Society ( 2009 ) , at the end of September , 2009 there were 436 nuclear reactors in operation in 31 countries all over the world to provide a net output of 370,221 MW , supplying an important part of the world 's total energy consumption .
The U.S. alone obtains 20 percent of its energy from nuclear power.To date , we have come up with 6 concepts for the Generation-IV reactors , which mean to produce more reliable energy at lower cost and risk .
Among the 6 concepts , the Very-high-temperature reactor ( VHTR ) is more secure , reliable and efficient and should receive more funding .
Many people doubt the safety of nuclear plants and thus oppose the construction of new nuclear plants .
However , the VHTR has resolved many of the safety concerns and proved to be much safer.The VHTR can be a pebble-bed reactor like HTR-10 in China .
The fuel is in the form of small pebbles with uranium dioxide ( UO2 ) inside and a graphite coating .
Each pebble can perform as a " mini " reactor independently .
" The pebble-bed reactor has high safety and reliability grades due to the inherent safety features of the fuel and reactor .
It also gets good ratings for proliferation resistance and physical protection ( Hylko , 2008 ) " .
Furthermore , it has been proved that with all the supporting machinery failing , the reactor will not crack , melt or explode .
" It simply goes up to a designed " idle " temperature and stays there .
In that state , the reactor vessel radiates heat , but the vessel and fuel spheres remain intact and undamaged " .
( FHSST Authors , 2005 ) .
" Even after decommissioning , the VHTR can still discharge surplus heat and does not need additional safety systems like other types of reactors " .
" The HTR-10 was subject to a test of its intrinsic safety in September 2004 when it was shut down with no cooling .
Fuel temperature reached less than 1600 ° C but there was still no failure " ( World 's First Commercial High Temperature Nuclear Reactor starts construction in China in 2009 , 2008 ) .
Efficiency is another problem that challenges many nuclear reactors .
But this is no problem because of the nature of the VHTR.Running at very high temperatures of about 700-900 ° C , the VHTR can supply energy to split water into oxygen and hydrogen , providing hydrogen for the nation 's industry .
According to Hylko ( 2008 ) , the VHTR has relatively higher efficiency for heat transfer and hydrogen production .
" It can squeeze 50 % more energy from the same amount of fuel " ( Butler , 2004 ) .
Moreover , bearing the property of running at such high temperatures , the VHTR can also realise " deep-burn " , during which up to 65 % of the initial fuel is burnt .
This shows great advantage over the conventional reactors which possess burn-up levels of around 5 % .
" Moreover , instead of 95 % of the uranium going into nuclear waste , this kind of reactor would only turn 35 % of it into waste " ( TendersInfo , 2008 ) , which will help with the growing storage problem of hazardous radioactive wastes .
It is understandable that many people doubt if there is anyone willing to inject money into this new reactor since is costs great amounts of money and time .
However , as is mentioned , the VHTR adopts the design of pebble-bed , making it possible to realize the concept of " modular reactors " .
Modular reactors are reactors that can be deployed part by part and each part can work independently .
Therefore , the initial investmentt to build the reactor can be controlled at an acceptable level ,
All these will make the VHTR more competitive in the fierce competition of today 's energy market ( Renkai , 2000 ) .
To sum up , the VHTR is highly safe and reliable .
It can perform high efficiency with an acceptable initial investment and construction period .
As a result , the VHTR is more favourable among the 6 Generation-IV concepts and further research and development funding should go for it .
Very-High-Temperature Reactor Will Be Built In The Future
Although the public is very concerned about the safe operation of nuclear reactors , the technological breakthrough and theory innovation shows that Very-High-Temperature Reactor ( VHTR ) will be built in the future .
In 1979 , there was the partial reactor meltdown at Three Mile Island , Pennsylvania ; in 1986 , the tragedy occurred at Chernobyl , Ukraine . In this case , , the core of the reactor exploded , 31 people were killed on the spot and radioactive debris spouted and spread over Europe ( NATURE , VOL429 , 2004 ) . Opponents of nuclear reactors being built claim that it is very dangerous for nuclear reactors ' operation .
According to Philippe B & Dominique B ( 2004 ) , some specific studies have been launched in CEA in order to make sure that the operation of VHTR is safe .
These studies include dynamic behavior when working normally as well as accidents which happened the moment when machines and certain components are functioning .
Through these , engineers can predict the impact of a possible defect in current and faraway situations ; study about the Leak Before Break ( LBB ) technology ; make model for Vessel Cooling System ( VCS ) ; analyse of the moment when the accident happened ; explore safety aspects of the ways to combine the reactor to the hydrogen production plant .
Hopefully , through the realization of these studies , the danger of nuclear reactors ' operation will be reduced .
Opponents may insist that it is very expensive to build and operate nuclear reactors .
However , the new generation of nuclear reactor , VHTR , has improved the efficiency , which means reduced cost of operation .
The study ( R.B.Vilim , 2007 ) shows that using the Gas Plant Analyzer and System Simulator/Hydrogen ( Gas-Pass/H ) code , the requests of the heat at the interface between a High Temperature Steam Electrolysis ( HTSE ) plant combined with the Very High Temperature Reactor ( VHTR ) have been investigated .
Thus , through the input deck , interconnections among components are supplied to the code .
Through this cycling process , the advanced design VHTR could produce 50 % more electricity than conventional plants ( NATURE , VOL429 , 2004 ) .
Moreover , compared to the increasingly expensive fossil fuels , it is reasonable to use nuclear energy .
So we can say that it is economically feasible for VHTR 's operation .
Opponents may also say that such nuclear reactor 's performance is doubtful .
Nevertheless , according to Idaho National Laboratory 's study ( 2009 ) , the VHTR system should be highly-efficient .
During different processes , the heat can be re-circulated .
To make the system perform better , electricity generating equipment may be added in .
The system can also adopt cycles for uranium/plutonium and minimize the waste .
Therefore , the VHTR provides a number of processes to use the heat and produce electricity efficiently .
Simultaneously it retains the safety properties provided by high-temperature gas-cooled reactors .
In short , the performance of VHTR is excellent through using so many advanced technologies .
Besides , considering the energy crisis we are facing nowadays , using nuclear energy is really a useful as well as practical method to handle the energy crisis .
Furthermore , compared to other energy resources like gasoline and natural gas , which produces greenhouse gases , nuclear energy is much more environmental friendly .
Last but not least , the theories and technologies of Very-High-Temperature Reactor are quite mature already . It is feasible to make it come true .
So we should have faith that VHTR will be built in the future .
From the above , on the one hand , the worries of opponents of nuclear reactors being built all can be solved by scientists and engineers ; on the other hand , energy needs of the society and the development of the related technologies have made it possible for VHTR to come true .
Therefore , Very-High-Temperature Reactor will be built in the future .
