The Advantages of Gas-cooled Fast Reactors
Some people think that nuclear reactors are not safe .
Nuclear radiation can cause mutation in human cells , cancer , and other diseases .
Nuclear reactors are also expensive to build and maintain .
Hence , only a few countries have built nuclear reactors to produce electricity .
But now , scientists have developed six new types of nuclear reactors called Nuclear Reactor Generation IV which are said to be safer than previous generations .
One of these reactors is the gas-cooled fast reactor ( GFR ) which has more benefits in terms of cost , safety , and performance than the other five reactor concepts , particularly the very-high temperature reactor ( VHTR ) .
Some people say that GFR is not safe because it produces plutonium waste which can be used to make nuclear weapons .
Plutonium in repository remains radioactive for several thousand of years ( " Energy Resources : Nuclear Power " ) .
Because of this , the development of GFR is obstructed .
Although GFR produces fuel waste that contains plutonium , it reprocesses its fuel waste such that the amount of waste produced can be cut by about 96 percent ( " Fuel Cycles " , page 33 , table 4.3 ) .
The plutonium produced from reprocessing of waste stays at a high temperature , making it too hot to be stolen .
In addition , as the fuel waste is recycled , there is no need to replace the fuel for a few years .
For comparison , VHTR can not reprocess its fuel waste , and because of that , the amount of fuel waste that it produces is getting bigger and bigger as the electricity demand increases ( Rohrer , 2007 ) .
These prove that GFR is safer and more environmentally-friendly than the VHTR .
Another group of people say that the performance of this reactor is still under VHTR .
Different from VHTR , which can work on 1000 degrees Celsius , GFR can work only on 850 degrees Celsius .
They say GFR produces less energy than VHTR. .
In reality , there is no need for reactors to work on 1000 degree Celsius , because the chain reaction of the fuel ( in this case Uranium-233 's reaction ) can be done perfectly only within 850 degrees ( Butler , 2004 ) .
This means that the amount of energy GFR and VHTR produce is almost the same , although there is 150 degrees difference in their temperature .
This proves that GFR works more efficiently than others such as VHTR .
One more important information is thatt there is no need for GFR to be manually moderated because GFR has already used Thorium which can absorb fast neutrons and decay into Uranium-233 ( " Gas-cooled Fast Reactor " ) .
This makes GFR cheaper to maintain and safer than VHTR which needs to be checked every time in order to make it operate safely .
In conclusion , based on the above mentioned points , GFR is proven to be a better option for future development .
The reason is because GFR allows its waste to be reprocessed .
Thus , it produces less waste than the others , especially VHTR .
It is also more efficient than other reactors , because it can produce the same energy as VHTR at just 850 degrees
