Surveillance technology such as RFID ( radio-frequency identification ) should not be used to track people ( e.g .
human implants and RFID tags on people or products ) .
Nowadays , surveillance technology is growing at a rapid speed and surveillance equipments can be found in many common places such as supermarkets , schools and airport terminal .
Surveillance technology is actually used to monitor and keep track of an individual 's activities , behavior and data .
People are actually being observed from a distance by surveillance technology equipment such as CCTV cameras and GPS tracking devices or being tracked by means of microchip or an RFID device which using radio waves .
It has been proven that surveillance technology can be beneficial to mankind in terms of deterring crime and terrorism , monitoring employees and improving patient 's welfare .
Thus , surveillance technology such as RFID ( radio-frequency identification ) should not be banned .
First of all , surveillance technology should be used as it helps in eradicate crime and to identify the faces of a terrorist from miles away .
This surveillance technology equipment is installed in buses , common places or schools and with the constant video monitoring , detailed evidence of any suspicious movement or criminal activity can be assessed .
Moreover , an individual is less likely to commit a crime if he knows that he is being watched .
If potential criminals are aware of this fact,there is a high possibility that crime can be greatly deterred .
In addition , this surveillance technology protects a country 's safety and security from terrorist attacks .
For instance , " as a direct result of the September 11 terrorist attacks , United States government and law enforcement officials have implemented surveillance technologies to deter future terrorist attacks ( Jim , 2009 ) .
Therefore , surveillance technology should be used since it puts criminals and terrorists away and protects the society .
Furthermore , employees in work places can be monitored by means of surveillance technology and it has many advantages .
Implementing this technology properly can help improve security in work places .
Examples of devices that are used are entrance and exit cameras , internal and outdoor cameras and cash register and counter cameras ( Bill , 2006 ) .
The presence of surveillance cameras can prevent theft in the company because employees are less likely to steal company products as they fully aware that they are being watched by unblinking cameras which can provide evidence .
However , opponents of surveillance technology argue that it invades an individual 's privacy .
They do not realize that with a clear understanding of where and how security cameras can be installed , potential privacy intrusion can be avoided ( Lynn , 2006 ) .
Hence , surveillance tools must be used in every work place to improve the security as well as the employee 's good behavior .
Last but not least , surveillance technology also helps in improving the welfare of both patients and the elderly people .
A small electronic device such as a microchip is incorporated into a patient 's body in order to track them by using radio waves .
This kind of procedure is essential for Alzheimer 's patients because they have very poor memory and may forget the way back if they go somewhere . Hence , RFID really plays an important role here to track the Alzheimer 's patients .
In addition , the microchips are also applied to patients so that doctor can monitor their health condition such as heart rate , blood pressure and glucose level in blood .
I must admit that , opponents of this position argue that microchip incorporated in a human 's body can affect the system later on .
It is because our cells can only identify our own cells and they identify the microchip as the foreign cell and eventually immune systems will act against the microchip .
However , there is no concrete prove about the above argument scientifically till now .
Therefore , this RFID should not banned as it reduces risk of getting sick and saves life .
In conclusion , surveillance technology such as RFID should be used to track people since it helps in deterring crime and terrorism , monitoring employees and improving welfare of patients .
If surveillance technology is banned , safety of the society and the country 's security will be under a big threat .
Criminals and terrorists tend to commit more crimes since they are not being watched and there is no concrete evidence to put them behind the bars .
Thus , to ensure our continued freedom , surveillance technology must be commonly used .
